      1   !<
      2       ==================================
      3       ImpactECON MyGTAP Model
      4       Version MyGTAP v2
      5       Based on GTAP 6.1
      6       May 2016
      7    
      8       This version incorporates additional foreign transactions and
      9        separates the government from the regional household.
     10       As well as Multiple households in one or more regions
     11       by Terrie Walmsley and Peter Minor
     12    
     13       ImpactECON LLC, Boulder, Colorado
     14       https://impactecon.com/
     15    
     16       ==================================
     17    
     18       Based on:
     19       =========
     20    
     21       MyGTAP v 1 produced in February 12, 2012
     22    
     23       and
     24    
     25       Global Trade Analysis Project
     26       The GTAP Modeling Framework
     27       GTAP Version 6.2
     28       September 2003
     29    
     30       ==================================
     31    
     32       For documentation see:
     33    
     34       (a) Walmsley T. L., and P. Minor, (2013). “MyGTAP Model”, ImpactECON
     35       Working Paper No. 02, ImpactECON: Boulder, CO, USA
     36    
     37       (b) Minor, P. and T. L. Walmsley, (2013). “MyGTAP Data Program”,
     38       ImpactECON Working Paper No. 01, ImpactECON: Boulder, CO, USA
     39    
     40       (c) Hertel, T.W. and M.E. Tsigas, "Structure of the Standard GTAP Model",
     41       Chapter 2 in T.W. Hertel (editor) "Global Trade Analysis: Modeling and
     42       Applications", Cambridge University Press, 1997.
     43    
     44       (d) R.A. McDougall, "A New Regional Household Demand System for GTAP",
     45       GTAP Technical Paper #20, Center for Global Trade Analysis, Purdue
     46       University
     47    
     48       (e) Hertel T.W., K. Itakura and R.A. McDougall, "GTAP.TAB: The Standard
     49       GTAP Model" (yet to be drafted), GTAP Technical Paper, Center for Global
     50       Trade Analysis, Purdue University,
     51       http://www.agecon.purdue.edu/gtap/techpapr/.  This technical paper
     52       documents all of the changes since the GTAP book TAB file.
     53    
     54    
     55       --------------------
     56       HISTORY of this file
     57       --------------------
     58    
     59       MyGTAP v2 produced in April, 2016
     60           Added welfare decomposition and other supplementary files.
     61    
     62       MyGTAP v1 produced in February 12, 2012
     63           Added multiple households and foreign transactions, including foreign
     64           aid, capital and labor payments.
     65    
     66       Version 6.2 fixes bugs and provides minor enhancements:
     67           - EV_ALT, CNTdpar fix
     68           - SX_IR fix
     69           - new treatment of export and import tariffs
     70           - original levels defined for power-of-tax variables
     71           - CNTalleffir range extended from TRAD_COMM to DEMD_COMM
     72           - INCOME formula, quantity index equations more AnalyzeGE-friendly
     73    
     74       Version 6.1 fixes bugs in 6.0:
     75           - Computation of tax receipts ratio is now separately done for total
     76             tax and indirect tax (equation DTAXRATIO and DINDTAXRATIO).
     77           - Computation of DTBALR, the ratio of the trade balance to regional
     78             income, has been corrected (equation DTBALRATIO).
     79           - Computation of EV_ALT, the summary variable for EV, has been
     80             corrected (equation EV_DECOMPOSITION).
     81       Also the notation has been changed for the tax-income ratio variables:
     82           TGCR -> del_taxrgc,    TPCR -> del_taxrpc,    TIUR -> del_taxriu,
     83           TFUR -> del_taxrfu,    TOUTR -> del_taxrout,  TEXPR -> del_taxrexp,
     84           TIMPR -> del_taxrimp,  TINCR -> del_taxrinc,  DTAXR -> del_ttaxr.
     85    
     86       Version 6.0 replaces version 5.0 used in the August 2000 short course, but
     87       never formally released.  The subsequent changes have been quite
     88       significant (primarily focused on final demand and welfare decomposition),
     89       so we decided to give it a new version number.  This also prevents
     90       confusion with the soon to be released version 5.0 GTAP data set.
     91    
     92       The differences with the previous publicly released version of GTAP.TAB,
     93       Version 4.1, dated November 1998, are numerous.  One goal of this version
     94       is to reorganize the TAB file which had not be redesigned since its
     95       inception.  In addition, there is a long list of substantive changes that
     96       have been made between Version 4.1 and 6.0.  These include:
     97    
     98           - provision for multiple margins sectors (to accommodate post version
     99             5 GTAP data)
    100           - introduction of the new theory of final demand following McDougall's
    101             GTAP Technical Paper #20
    102           - modification of the welfare decomposition following McDougall's
    103             Technical Paper #20
    104           - correction to the treatment of technical change, ao, in the presence
    105             of ESUBT > 0 (affects equations VADEMAND and INTDEMAND)
    106           - addition of import-augmenting "technical change" in the Armington
    107             nest: ams which can be used to lower the effective price of imported
    108             products
    109           - specification of Baldwin-type capital accmulation effects following
    110             Francois' Technical Paper #7
    111           - introduction of uniform consumption tax instrument, tp(r)
    112    
    113    
    114       ----------------------------------
    115       Overview of the GTAP.TAB Structure
    116       ----------------------------------
    117       Preliminaries:
    118           FILES
    119           SETS
    120           READ statements of Base Data
    121           Common VARIABLES
    122           Common COEFFICIENTS
    123    
    124       Modules:
    125           1.  Government Consumption
    126           2.  Private Consumption
    127           3.  Firms
    128           4.  Investment, Global Bank, and Savings
    129           5.  International Trade
    130           6.  International Transport Services
    131           7.  Regional Household
    132           8.  Equilibrium Conditions
    133    
    134       Appendices:
    135           A.  Summary Indices
    136           B.  Equivalent Variation
    137           C.  Welfare Decomposition
    138           D.  Terms of Trade Decomposition
    139   >!
    140    
    141    
    142   !<
    143       -----
    144       FILES
    145       -----
    146   >!
    147    
    148   File
    149       GTAPSETS # file with set specification #;
    150   File
    151       GTAPDATA # file containing all base data #;
    152   File
    153       GTAPPARM # file containing behavioral parameters #;
    154    
    155    
    156   !<
    157       ----
    158       SETS
    159       ----
    160    
    161       Sets define relevant groupings of entities over which we will be
    162       performing operations in the model.  SUBSETS are defined in order to
    163       facilitate summation over only a portion of a given group, e.g., tradeable
    164       commodities.  Users with access to GEMPACK can increase the maximum set
    165       sizes to permit larger aggregations, provided you have sufficient RAM for
    166       implementing them The standard model (10x10 aggregation with decomposition
    167       code) is designed to run with 16 Mb of RAM.
    168    
    169    
    170       Aide-Memoire for Sets
    171       ---------------------
    172    
    173       |--------------------------------------|
    174       |         DEMD_COMM                    |
    175       |----------------------------------------------------|
    176       | ENDW_COMM |       TRAD_COMM          |  CGDS_COMM  |
    177       |----------------------------------------------------|
    178       |        NSAV_COMM                                   |
    179       |----------------------------------------------------|
    180                   |                     PROD_COMM          |
    181                   |----------------------------------------|
    182    
    183       For Endowments,
    184       |-------------------------|
    185       | ENDW_COMM               |
    186       |-------------------------|
    187       | ENDWM_COMM | ENDWS_COMM |
    188       |-------------------------|
    189   >!
    190    
    191   Coefficient
    192       VERNUM # version of GTAP data #;
    193   Read
    194       VERNUM from file GTAPDATA header "DVER";
    195   Update (change)
    196       VERNUM = 0.0; ! force it to be copied to update file !
    197    
    198   Set
    199       REG # regions in the model #
    200       maximum size 10 read elements from file GTAPSETS header "H1";
    201   Set
    202       HHLD # Households in the model #
    203       maximum size 10 read elements from file GTAPSETS header "HOU";
    204   Set
    205       TRAD_COMM # traded commodities #
    206       maximum size 10 read elements from file GTAPSETS header "H2";
    207   Set
    208       MARG_COMM # margin commodities #
    209       maximum size 10 read elements from file GTAPSETS header "MARG";
    210   Subset
    211       MARG_COMM is subset of TRAD_COMM;
    212   Set
    213       NMRG_COMM # non-margin commodities # = TRAD_COMM - MARG_COMM;
    214   Set
    215       CGDS_COMM # capital goods commodities #
    216       maximum size 1 read elements from file GTAPSETS header "H9";
    217   Set
    218       ENDW_COMM # endowment commodities #
    219       maximum size 5 read elements from file GTAPSETS header "H6";
    220   Set
    221       ENDW_GTAP # Original GTAP endowments commodities #
    222       maximum size 5 read elements from file GTAPSETS header "ENDW";
    223    
    224   Set
    225       ENDWC_COMM # capital endowment commodities #
    226       read elements from file GTAPSETS header "ENDC";
    227   Set
    228       ENDWL_COMM # capital endowment commodities #
    229       read elements from file GTAPSETS header "ENDL";
    230    
    231   Subset
    232       ENDWC_COMM is subset of ENDW_COMM;
    233       ENDWL_COMM is subset of ENDW_COMM;
    234    
    235   Mapping MAPENDW from ENDW_COMM to ENDW_GTAP;
    236       read (by_elements) MAPENDW from file GTAPSETS header "MFAC";
    237    
    238   Set
    239       PROD_COMM # produced commodities # = TRAD_COMM union CGDS_COMM;
    240   Set
    241       DEMD_COMM # demanded commodities # = ENDW_COMM union TRAD_COMM;
    242   Set
    243       NSAV_COMM # non-savings commodities # = DEMD_COMM union CGDS_COMM;
    244   Subset
    245       PROD_COMM is subset of NSAV_COMM;
    246    
    247   !<
    248       Check for non-overlapping sets (users can't use the same name for elements
    249       of ENDW_COMM, TRAD_COMM or CGDS_COMM).
    250   >!
    251    
    252   Coefficient
    253       SIZE_TRAD # size of TRAD_COMM set #;
    254   Formula
    255       SIZE_TRAD = sum(i,TRAD_COMM, 1);
    256   Coefficient
    257       SIZE_ENDW # size of ENDW_COMM set #;
    258   Formula
    259       SIZE_ENDW = sum(i,ENDW_COMM, 1);
    260   Coefficient
    261       SIZE_DEMD # size of DEMD_COMM set #;
    262   Formula
    263       SIZE_DEMD = sum(i,DEMD_COMM, 1);
    264   Assertion (initial)
    265       SIZE_DEMD = SIZE_TRAD + SIZE_ENDW;
    266    
    267   Coefficient
    268       SIZE_CGDS # size of CGDS_COMM set #;
    269   Formula
    270       SIZE_CGDS = sum(i,CGDS_COMM, 1);
    271   Coefficient
    272       SIZE_PROD # size of PROD_COMM set #;
    273   Formula
    274       SIZE_PROD = sum(i,PROD_COMM, 1);
    275   Assertion (initial)
    276       SIZE_PROD = SIZE_TRAD + SIZE_CGDS;
    277    
    278   !<
    279       The sluggish endowments are now defined dynamically, based on the variable
    280       SLUG.  SLUG is a binary variable that is zero for mobile endowments and
    281       one for sluggish endowments.  We must define and read in this variable
    282       before proceeding further.
    283   >!
    284   Coefficient (integer,parameter) (all,i,ENDW_COMM)
    285       SLUG(i) # sluggish primary factor endowments #;
    286   Read
    287       SLUG from file GTAPPARM header "SLUG";
    288    
    289   Set
    290       ENDWS_COMM
    291       # sluggish endowment commodities # = (all,i,ENDW_COMM: SLUG(i)>0);
    292   Set
    293       ENDWM_COMM
    294       # mobile endowment commodities # = ENDW_COMM - ENDWS_COMM;
    295    
    296   !<
    297       ----------------------------
    298       READ Statements of Base Data
    299       ----------------------------
    300    
    301       We read in here almost all the base data, and define variables and
    302       coefficients associated with them.  A few data arrays used each in a
    303       single module are read in those modules: VKB, VTMFSD, and DPARSUM.
    304    
    305       The READ statements are divided into six sections:
    306    
    307       Saving
    308       Government Consumption
    309       Private Consumption
    310       Firms
    311       Global Bank
    312       International Trade and Transport
    313    
    314       Since these are invariant for each solution of the model, they are termed
    315       coefficients.  Coefficients are assigned upper case to distinguish them
    316       from variables.  (This is purely cosmetic, as GEMPACK is not
    317       case-sensitive.) Variables in GEMPACK are assigned lower case labels to
    318       denote the fact that they are percentage changes.  In some cases, original
    319       levels values for selected variables are defined to permit the user to
    320       compare post-simulation levels values across several simulations.
    321    
    322       The updating command indicates how the new level of the coefficient will
    323       be computed based on the previous solution of the linearized equations.
    324       Note that the notation used in the update commands is a shorthand for
    325       total differentials of these coefficient values.  Thus, w * v indicates
    326       that we want to take the total differential of W * V, plug in the
    327       calculated values of w and v, and add this to the base level in order to
    328       obtain a revised value for this product.
    329   >!
    330    
    331    
    332   !<
    333       Saving
    334       ------
    335   >!
    336   !Savings from Income.tab adjusted for remit, aid, FY etc.!
    337    
    338   Variable (all,r,REG)
    339       psave(r) # price of savings in region r #;
    340   Variable (all,r,REG)
    341       qsave(r) # regional demand for NET savings #;
    342    
    343   Variable (orig_level = SAV_GOV)(all,r,REG)
    344       qgsave(r) # Real Government saving/deficit in region r#;
    345   Coefficient (all,r,REG)
    346       SAV_GOV(r) #Government Saving in region r# ;
    347   Read SAV_GOV from file GTAPDATA header "SGOV";
    348   Update (all,r,REG)
    349       SAV_GOV(r) = psave(r) * qgsave(r);
    350    
    351   Variable (orig_level = SAV_HHLD)(all,h,HHLD)(all,r,REG)
    352       qhsave(h,r) # Real Savings by Household h in region r #;
    353   Coefficient (all,h,HHLD)(all,r,REG)
    354       SAV_HHLD(h,r) #Savings by Household h in region r#;
    355   read SAV_HHLD from file GTAPDATA header "SHLD";
    356   Update (all,h,HHLD)(all,r,REG)
    357       SAV_HHLD(h,r) = psave(r) * qhsave(h,r);
    358    
    359   Coefficient (all,r,REG)
    360       SAVE(r) # Total Regional savings #;
    361   Formula (all,r,REG)
    362       SAVE(r) = SAV_GOV(r) + sum{h,HHLD,SAV_HHLD(h,r)};
    363    
    364   !<
    365       Government Consumption
    366       ----------------------
    367   >!
    368    
    369   Variable (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,s,REG)
    370       pgd(i,s) # price of domestic i in government consumption in s #;
    371   Variable (orig_level=VDGM)(all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,s,REG)
    372       qgd(i,s) # government hhld demand for domestic i in region s #;
    373   Coefficient (ge 0)(all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,r,REG)
    374       VDGA(i,r) # government consumption expenditure on domestic i in r #;
    375   Update (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,r,REG)
    376       VDGA(i,r) = pgd(i,r) * qgd(i,r);
    377   Read
    378       VDGA from file GTAPDATA header "VDGA";
    379    
    380   Variable (orig_level=1.0)(all,i,NSAV_COMM)(all,r,REG)
    381       pm(i,r) # market price of commodity i in region r #;
    382   Coefficient (ge 0)(all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,r,REG)
    383       VDGM(i,r) # government consumption expenditure on domestic i in r #;
    384   Update (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,r,REG)
    385       VDGM(i,r) = pm(i,r) * qgd(i,r);
    386   Read
    387       VDGM from file GTAPDATA header "VDGM";
    388    
    389   Variable (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,s,REG)
    390       pgm(i,s) # price of imports of i in government consumption in s #;
    391   Variable (orig_level=VIGM)(all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,s,REG)
    392       qgm(i,s) # government hhld demand for imports of i in region s #;
    393   Coefficient (ge 0)(all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,r,REG)
    394       VIGA(i,r) # government consumption expenditure on imported i #;
    395   Update (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,r,REG)
    396       VIGA(i,r) = pgm(i,r) * qgm(i,r);
    397   Read
    398       VIGA from file GTAPDATA header "VIGA";
    399    
    400   Variable (orig_level=1.0)(all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,r,REG)
    401       pim(i,r) # market price of composite import i in region r #;
    402   Coefficient (ge 0)(all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,r,REG)
    403       VIGM(i,r) # gov't consumption expenditure on i in r #;
    404   Update (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,r,REG)
    405       VIGM(i,r) = pim(i,r) * qgm(i,r);
    406   Read
    407       VIGM from file GTAPDATA header "VIGM";
    408    
    409    
    410   !<
    411       Private Consumption
    412       -------------------
    413   >!
    414    
    415   Variable (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,h,HHLD)(all,s,REG)
    416       ppdh(i,h,s) # price of domestic i to private household h in s #;
    417   Variable (orig_level=VDPMH)(all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,h,HHLD)(all,s,REG)
    418       qpdh(i,h,s) # demand by houshold h for domestic i in region s #;
    419   Variable (orig_level=VDPM)(all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,s,REG)
    420       qpd(i,s) # private hhld demand for domestic i in region s #;
    421   Coefficient (ge 0)(all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,h,HHLD)(all,r,REG)
    422       VDPAH(i,h,r) # private consumption expenditure on domestic i in r by h#;
    423   Update (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,h,HHLD)(all,r,REG)
    424       VDPAH(i,h,r) = ppdh(i,h,r) * qpdh(i,h,r);
    425   Read
    426       VDPAH from file GTAPDATA header "VDPA";
    427    
    428   Coefficient (ge 0)(all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,r,REG)
    429       VDPA(i,r) # private consumption expenditure on domestic i in r #;
    430   Formula (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,r,REG)
    431       VDPA(i,r) = sum(h, HHLD, VDPAH(i,h,r));
    432    
    433   Coefficient (ge 0)(all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,h,HHLD)(all,r,REG)
    434       VDPMH(i,h,r) # private consumption expenditure on domestic i in r by h#;
    435   Update (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,h,HHLD)(all,r,REG)
    436       VDPMH(i,h,r) = pm(i,r) * qpdh(i,h,r);
    437   Read
    438       VDPMH from file GTAPDATA header "VDPM";
    439    
    440   Coefficient (ge 0)(all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,r,REG)
    441       VDPM(i,r) # private consumption expenditure on domestic i in r #;
    442   Formula (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,r,REG)
    443       VDPM(i,r) = sum(h, HHLD, VDPMH(i,h,r));
    444    
    445   Variable (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,h,HHLD)(all,s,REG)
    446       ppmh(i,h,s) # price of imports of i by private household h in s #;
    447   Variable (orig_level=VIPMH)(all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,h,HHLD)(all,s,REG)
    448       qpmh(i,h,s) # demand for imports of i in region s by household h#;
    449   Variable (orig_level=VIPM)(all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,s,REG)
    450       qpm(i,s) # private hhld demand for imports of i in region s #;
    451   Coefficient (ge 0)(all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,h,HHLD)(all,r,REG)
    452       VIPAH(i,h,r) # private consumption expenditure on imported i in r by h#;
    453   Update (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,h,HHLD)(all,r,REG)
    454       VIPAH(i,h,r) = ppmh(i,h,r) * qpmh(i,h,r);
    455   Read
    456       VIPAH from file GTAPDATA header "VIPA";
    457    
    458   Coefficient (ge 0)(all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,r,REG)
    459       VIPA(i,r) # private consumption expenditure on domestic i in r #;
    460   Formula (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,r,REG)
    461       VIPA(i,r) = sum(h, HHLD, VIPAH(i,h,r));
    462    
    463   Coefficient (ge 0)(all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,h,HHLD)(all,r,REG)
    464       VIPMH(i,h,r) # private consumption expenditure on i in r by household h#;
    465   Update (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,h,HHLD)(all,r,REG)
    466       VIPMH(i,h,r)= pim(i,r) * qpmh(i,h,r);
    467   Read
    468       VIPMH from file GTAPDATA header "VIPM";
    469    
    470   Coefficient (ge 0)(all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,r,REG)
    471       VIPM(i,r) # private consumption expenditure on domestic i in r #;
    472   Formula (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,r,REG)
    473       VIPM(i,r) = sum(h, HHLD, VIPMH(i,h,r));
    474    
    475    
    476   !<
    477       Firms
    478       -----
    479   >!
    480    
    481   Variable (all,i,NSAV_COMM)(all,r,REG)
    482       ps(i,r) # supply price of commodity i in region r #;
    483   Variable (orig_level=VOM)(all,i,NSAV_COMM)(all,r,REG)
    484       qo(i,r) # industry output of commodity i in region r #;
    485    
    486   Variable (all,i,ENDW_COMM)(all,h,HHLD)(all,r,REG)
    487       psh(i,h,r) # supply price of endowment i in region r owned by household h#;
    488   Variable (orig_level=EVOAH)(all,i,ENDW_COMM)(all,h,HHLD)(all,r,REG)
    489       qoh(i,h,r) # supply of endowment i in region r owned by household h#;
    490   Variable (all,i,ENDW_COMM)(all,h,HHLD)(all,r,REG)
    491       qoh_s(i,h,r) # supply of endow i from hhld h in region r, incl unemployed#;
    492    
    493   Coefficient (ge 0)(all,i,ENDW_COMM)(all,h,HHLD)(all,r,REG)
    494       EVOAH(i,h,r) # value of income on endow i owned by hhld h in region r #;
    495   Update (all,i,ENDW_COMM)(all,h,HHLD)(all,r,REG)
    496       EVOAH(i,h,r) = psh(i,h,r) * qoh(i,h,r);
    497   Read
    498       EVOAH from file GTAPDATA header "EVOA";
    499    
    500   Variable (all,i,ENDW_COMM)(all,j,PROD_COMM)(all,r,REG)
    501       pfe(i,j,r) # firms' price for endowment commodity i in ind. j, region r #;
    502   Variable (orig_level=VFM)(all,i,ENDW_COMM)(all,j,PROD_COMM)(all,r,REG)
    503       qfe(i,j,r)  # demand for endowment i for use in ind. j in region r #;
    504   Coefficient (ge 0)(all,i,ENDW_COMM)(all,j,PROD_COMM)(all,r,REG)
    505       EVFA(i,j,r) # producer expenditure on i by j in r at agent's prices #;
    506   Update (all,i,ENDW_COMM)(all,j,PROD_COMM)(all,r,REG)
    507       EVFA(i,j,r) = pfe(i,j,r) * qfe(i,j,r);
    508   Read
    509       EVFA from file GTAPDATA header "EVFA";
    510    
    511   Variable (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,j,PROD_COMM)(all,s,REG)
    512       pfd(i,j,s) # price index for domestic purchases of i by j in region s #;
    513   Variable (orig_level=VDFM)(all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,j,PROD_COMM)(all,s,REG)
    514       qfd(i,j,s)  # domestic good i demanded by industry j in region s #;
    515   Coefficient (ge 0)(all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,j,PROD_COMM)(all,r,REG)
    516       VDFA(i,j,r) # purchases of domestic i for use by j in region r #;
    517   Update (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,j,PROD_COMM)(all,r,REG)
    518       VDFA(i,j,r) = pfd(i,j,r) * qfd(i,j,r);
    519   Read
    520       VDFA from file GTAPDATA header "VDFA";
    521    
    522   Variable (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,j,PROD_COMM)(all,s,REG)
    523       pfm(i,j,s) # price index for imports of i by j in region s #;
    524   Variable (orig_level=VIFM)(all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,j,PROD_COMM)(all,s,REG)
    525       qfm(i,j,s) # demand for i by industry j in region s #;
    526   Coefficient (ge 0)(all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,j,PROD_COMM)(all,r,REG)
    527       VIFA(i,j,r) # purchases of imported i for use by j in region r #;
    528   Update (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,j,PROD_COMM)(all,r,REG)
    529       VIFA(i,j,r) = pfm(i,j,r) * qfm(i,j,r);
    530   Read
    531       VIFA from file GTAPDATA header "VIFA";
    532    
    533   Variable (all,i,ENDWS_COMM)(all,j,PROD_COMM)(all,r,REG)
    534       pmes(i,j,r) # market price of sluggish endowment i used by j in r #;
    535   Coefficient (ge 0)(all,i,ENDW_COMM)(all,j,PROD_COMM)(all,r,REG)
    536       VFM(i,j,r) # producer expenditure on i by j in r valued at mkt prices #;
    537   Update (all,i,ENDWM_COMM)(all,j,PROD_COMM)(all,r,REG)
    538       VFM(i,j,r) = pm(i,r) * qfe(i,j,r);
    539   Update (all,i,ENDWS_COMM)(all,j,PROD_COMM)(all,r,REG)
    540       VFM(i,j,r) = pmes(i,j,r) * qfe(i,j,r);
    541   Read
    542       VFM from file GTAPDATA header "VFM";
    543    
    544   Coefficient (ge 0)(all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,j,PROD_COMM)(all,r,REG)
    545       VIFM(i,j,r) # purchases of imports i for use by j in region r #;
    546   Update (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,j,PROD_COMM)(all,r,REG)
    547       VIFM(i,j,r) = pim(i,r) * qfm(i,j,r);
    548   Read
    549       VIFM from file GTAPDATA header "VIFM";
    550    
    551   Coefficient (ge 0)(all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,j,PROD_COMM)(all,r,REG)
    552       VDFM(i,j,r) # purchases of domestic i for use by j in region r #;
    553   Update (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,j,PROD_COMM)(all,r,REG)
    554       VDFM(i,j,r) = pm(i,r) * qfd(i,j,r);
    555   Read
    556       VDFM from file GTAPDATA header "VDFM";
    557    
    558   Variable (all,h,HHLD)(all,r,REG)
    559       dpprivh(h,r) # private consumption distribution parameter #;
    560   Variable (all,r,REG)
    561       dppriv(r) # private consumption distribution parameter #;
    562   Variable (all,r,REG)
    563       dpgov(r) # government consumption distribution parameter #;
    564   Variable (all,r,REG)
    565       dpgsave(r) # government saving distribution parameter in region r#;
    566   Variable (all,h,HHLD)(all,r,REG)
    567       dphsave(h,r) # household saving distribution parameter #;
    568   Variable (all,r,REG)
    569       dphsave_all(r) # hhd saving dist'n parameter applied to all hhlds equally #;
    570   Variable (all,r,REG)
    571       dpsave(r) # total saving distribution parameter #;
    572    
    573   !<
    574       Global Bank
    575       -----------
    576   >!
    577    
    578   Variable (all,r,REG)(all,h,HHLD)
    579       kbh(h,r) # beginning-of-period capital stock in r owned by household h#;
    580   Variable (all,r,REG)
    581       kb(r) # beginning-of-period capital stock in r #;
    582   Variable (all,r,REG)
    583       pcgds(r) # price of investment goods = ps("cgds",r) #;
    584   Coefficient (ge 0)(all,h,HHLD)(all,r,REG)
    585       VDEPH(h,r) # value of capital depeciation on capital owned by h in r#;
    586   Read
    587       VDEPH from file GTAPDATA header "VDEP";
    588   Update (all,h,HHLD)(all,r,REG)
    589       VDEPH(h,r) = kbh(h,r) * pcgds(r);
    590    
    591   Coefficient (all,r,REG)
    592       VDEP(r) # private consumption expenditure on domestic i in r #;
    593   Formula (all,r,REG)
    594       VDEP(r) = sum(h, HHLD, VDEPH(h,r));
    595    
    596   !<
    597       Value of capital depreciation is used to compute the (exogenous)
    598       depreciation rate and therefore does not appear in update.
    599   >!
    600    
    601    
    602   !<
    603       International Trade and Transport
    604       ---------------------------------
    605   >!
    606    
    607   Variable (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,r,REG)(all,s,REG)
    608       pms(i,r,s) # domestic price for good i supplied from r to region s #;
    609   Variable (orig_level=VXMD)(all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,r,REG)(all,s,REG)
    610       qxs(i,r,s) # export sales of commodity i from r to region s #;
    611   Coefficient (ge 0)(all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,r,REG)(all,s,REG)
    612       VIMS(i,r,s) # imports of i from r to s valued at domestic mkt prices #;
    613   Update (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,r,REG)(all,s,REG)
    614       VIMS(i,r,s) = pms(i,r,s) * qxs(i,r,s);
    615   Read
    616       VIMS from file GTAPDATA header "VIMS";
    617    
    618   Variable (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,r,REG)(all,s,REG)
    619       pcif(i,r,s) # CIF world price of commodity i supplied from r to s #;
    620   Coefficient (ge 0)(all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,r,REG)(all,s,REG)
    621       VIWS(i,r,s) # imports of i from r to s valued CIF (tradeables only) #;
    622   Update (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,r,REG)(all,s,REG)
    623       VIWS(i,r,s) = pcif(i,r,s) * qxs(i,r,s);
    624   Read
    625       VIWS from file GTAPDATA header "VIWS";
    626    
    627   Variable (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,r,REG)(all,s,REG)
    628       pfob(i,r,s) # FOB world price of commodity i supplied from r to s #;
    629   Coefficient (ge 0)(all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,r,REG)(all,s,REG)
    630       VXWD(i,r,s) # exports of i from r to s valued FOB (tradeables only) #;
    631   Update (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,r,REG)(all,s,REG)
    632       VXWD(i,r,s) = pfob(i,r,s) * qxs(i,r,s);
    633   Read
    634       VXWD from file GTAPDATA header "VXWD";
    635    
    636   Coefficient (ge 0)(all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,r,REG)(all,s,REG)
    637       VXMD(i,r,s)
    638       # exports of i from r to s valued at mkt prices (tradeables only) #;
    639   Update (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,r,REG)(all,s,REG)
    640       VXMD(i,r,s) = pm(i,r) * qxs(i,r,s);
    641   Read
    642       VXMD from file GTAPDATA header "VXMD";
    643    
    644   Variable (orig_level=VST)(all,m,MARG_COMM)(all,r,REG)
    645       qst(m,r) # sales of m from r to international transport #;
    646   Coefficient (ge 0)(all,m,MARG_COMM)(all,r,REG)
    647       VST(m,r)
    648       # exprts of m from r for int'l trnsport valued at mkt p (tradeables only) #;
    649   Update (all,m,MARG_COMM)(all,r,REG)
    650       VST(m,r) = pm(m,r) * qst(m,r);
    651   Read
    652       VST from file GTAPDATA header "VST";
    653    
    654    
    655   !<
    656       ----------------
    657       Common VARIABLES
    658       ----------------
    659    
    660       Common variables are defined as variables which are used in more than one
    661       module.  For example, the variable y(r) is used in the Goverment
    662       Consumption, Private Consumption, Firms, Regional Household and
    663       Investment, Global Bank and Savings modules.  Appendices, e.g., Summary
    664       Indices, are not included in this definition.
    665   >!
    666    
    667   Variable (all,r,REG)
    668       y(r) # regional household income in region r #;
    669   Variable (all,h,HHLD)(all,r,REG)
    670       poph(h,r) # Population by household h in region r#;
    671   Variable (all,i,ENDWS_COMM)(all,j,PROD_COMM)(all,r,REG)
    672       qoes(i,j,r) # supply of sluggish endowment i used by j in r #;
    673   Variable (all,i,ENDW_COMM)(all,r,REG)
    674       endwslack(i,r) # slack variable in endowment market clearing condition #;
    675   !<
    676       This is exogenous, unless the user wishes to employ a partial equilibrium
    677       closure in which the price of one or more of the primary factors is fixed.
    678   >!
    679    
    680   Variable (all,r,REG)
    681       pgov(r) # price index for gov't hhld expenditure in region r #;
    682   Variable (all,r,REG)
    683       yg(r)
    684       # regional government consumption expenditure in region r #;
    685   Variable (all,r,REG)
    686       qgov(r) # real gov't expend. in region r #;
    687    
    688   Variable (all,r,REG)
    689       ppriv(r)
    690       # price index for private consumption expenditure in region r #;
    691   Variable (all,r,REG)
    692       yp(r) # regional private consumption expenditure in region r #;
    693    
    694   Variable (all,r,REG)(all,h,HHLD)
    695       pprivh(h,r)
    696       # price index for private consumption expenditure in region r by hhld h#;
    697   Variable (all,r,REG)(all,h,HHLD)
    698       ueprivh(h,r)
    699       # elasticity of cost wrt utility from private consumption by hhld h#;
    700   Variable (all,r,REG)(all,h,HHLD)
    701       yph(h,r) # regional private consumption expenditure in region r by hhld h#;
    702   Variable (all,r,REG)(all,h,HHLD)
    703       uph(h,r) # per capita utility from private expend. in region r by hhld h#;
    704    
    705   Variable (all,i,NSAV_COMM)(all,r,REG)
    706       to(i,r) # output (or income) tax in region r #;
    707   Variable (all,h,HHLD)(all,i,ENDW_COMM)(all,r,REG)
    708       toh(i,h,r) # income tax in region r on endowments owned by hhld h#;
    709   !<
    710       Note:  It is important that the user NOT shock the tax on capital goods
    711       output, as this will cause an inconsistency in the update relationship for
    712       VOM(cgds).
    713   >!
    714   Variable (orig_level=VIM)(all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,s,REG)
    715       qim(i,s) # aggregate imports of i in region s, market price weights #;
    716   Variable
    717       globalcgds # global supply of capital goods for NET investment #;
    718   Variable
    719       pcgdswld # world average price of capital goods (net investment weights) #;
    720    
    721   !<
    722       The following variables could be dropped when converting to levels
    723       equation for income.  They are only needed for the linearized equation.
    724       The idea here is to look at the ratio of taxes to income in order to
    725       preserve homogeneity in prices.  (We could also look at changes in tax
    726       revenue, but then a uniform price increase would change this variable.)
    727       Obviously a simple percentage change variable doesn't work, since many
    728       taxes are initially zero.  The basic logic of this approach is as follows:
    729    
    730       Let R be the ratio of taxes to income: R = T/Y, then:
    731           dR = d(T/Y) = R(t - y)/100
    732       multiply through by Y to get:
    733           YdR = dT - Ty/100
    734       This ratio change is computed for each tax type and for total taxes.  Then
    735       the change in tax revenue itself may be computed as:
    736           dT = YdR + Ty/100
    737       in order to determine regional income.
    738   >!
    739    
    740   Variable (change) (all,r,REG)
    741       del_taxrgc(r) # change in ratio of government consumption tax to INCOME #;
    742   Variable (change) (all,r,REG)
    743       del_taxrpc(r) # change in ratio of private consumption tax to INCOME #;
    744   Variable (change) (all,r,REG)
    745       del_taxriu(r) # change in ratio of tax on intermediate usage to INCOME #;
    746   Variable (change) (all,r,REG)
    747       del_taxrfu(r) # change in ratio of tax on primary factor usage to INCOME #;
    748   Variable (change) (all,r,REG)
    749       del_taxrout(r) # change in ratio of output tax to INCOME #;
    750   Variable (change) (all,r,REG)
    751       del_taxrexp(r) # change in ratio of export tax to INCOME #;
    752   Variable (change) (all,r,REG)
    753       del_taxrimp(r) # change in ratio of import tax to INCOME #;
    754   Variable (change) (all,r,REG)
    755       del_taxrinc(r) # change in ratio of income tax to INCOME #;
    756    
    757    
    758   !<
    759       -------------------
    760       Common COEFFICIENTS
    761       -------------------
    762    
    763       Key Derivatives of the Base Data
    764       Regional Expenditure and Income
    765       Indirect Tax Receipts
    766       Miscellaneous Coefficients
    767    
    768       Common Coefficients are defined as coefficients which are used in more
    769       than one module.  For example, ESUBD(i) is used in the Goverment
    770       Household, Private Household, and Firms modules.
    771   >!
    772    
    773    
    774   !<
    775       Key Derivatives of the Base Data
    776       --------------------------------
    777   >!
    778    
    779   Coefficient (all,i,DEMD_COMM)(all,j,PROD_COMM)(all,r,REG)
    780       VFA(i,j,r) # producer expenditure on i by j in r valued at agent's prices #;
    781   Formula (all,i,ENDW_COMM)(all,j,PROD_COMM)(all,r,REG)
    782       VFA(i,j,r) = EVFA(i,j,r);
    783   Formula (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,j,PROD_COMM)(all,s,REG)
    784       VFA(i,j,s) = VDFA(i,j,s) + VIFA(i,j,s);
    785    
    786   Coefficient (all,i,NSAV_COMM)(all,r,REG)
    787       VOA(i,r) # value of commodity i output in region r at agent's prices #;
    788   Formula (all,i,ENDW_COMM)(all,r,REG)
    789       VOA(i,r) = sum(h, HHLD, EVOAH(i,h,r));
    790   Formula (all,i,PROD_COMM)(all,r,REG)
    791       VOA(i,r) = sum(j,DEMD_COMM, VFA(j,i,r));
    792    
    793   Coefficient (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,r,REG)
    794       VDM(i,r) # domestic sales of i in r at mkt prices (tradeables only) #;
    795   Formula (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,r,REG)
    796       VDM(i,r) = VDPM(i,r) + VDGM(i,r) + sum(j,PROD_COMM, VDFM(i,j,r));
    797    
    798   Coefficient (ge 0)(all,i,ENDW_COMM)(all,h,HHLD)(all,r,REG)
    799       EVOMH(i,h,r) # value of commodity i output in region r owned by hhld h#;
    800   Read
    801       EVOMH from file GTAPDATA header "EVOM";
    802   Update (all,i,ENDW_COMM)(all,h,HHLD)(all,r,REG)
    803       EVOMH(i,h,r) = pm(i,r) * qoh(i,h,r);
    804    
    805   Coefficient (all,i,NSAV_COMM)(all,r,REG)
    806       VOM(i,r) # value of commodity i output in region r at market prices #;
    807   Formula (all,i,ENDW_COMM)(all,r,REG)
    808       VOM(i,r) = sum(h, HHLD, EVOMH(i,h,r));
    809   Formula (all,m,MARG_COMM)(all,r,REG)
    810       VOM(m,r) = VDM(m,r) + sum(s,REG, VXMD(m,r,s)) + VST(m,r);
    811   Formula (all,i,NMRG_COMM)(all,r,REG)
    812       VOM(i,r) = VDM(i,r) + sum(s,REG, VXMD(i,r,s));
    813   Formula (all,h,CGDS_COMM)(all,r,REG)
    814       VOM(h,r) = VOA(h,r);
    815    
    816    
    817   !<
    818       Regional Expenditure and Income
    819       -------------------------------
    820    
    821       Regional income is allocated between private consumption expenditure,
    822       government consumption expenditure, and saving.
    823    
    824    
    825       Expenditure of Regional Household
    826       .................................
    827    
    828                  Regional household(h.h.)
    829                   Expenditure = Income
    830                            _/|\_
    831                          _/  |  \_
    832                        _/    |    \_
    833                      _/      |      \_
    834                    _/        |        \_
    835          Private h.h.        |        Government h.h.
    836          ( PRIVEXP )         |          ( GOVEXP )
    837             _/\_             |              _/\_
    838           _/    \_           |            _/    \_
    839          /        \          |           /        \
    840       Domestic  Imported   Savings    Domestic    Imported
    841        Goods     Goods     ( SAVE )    Goods       Goods
    842       ( VDPA )  ( VIPA )              ( VDGA )    ( VIGA )
    843    
    844       Note: The coefficients at the ends of branches are
    845             Base Data, e.g., VDPA, SAVE.
    846   >!
    847    
    848   ! government consumption expenditure, GOVEXP !
    849   Coefficient (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,r,REG)
    850       VGA(i,r) # government consn expenditure on i in r at agent's prices #;
    851   Formula (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,s,REG)
    852       VGA(i,s) = VDGA(i,s) + VIGA(i,s);
    853   Coefficient (all,r,REG)
    854       GOVEXP(r) # government expenditure in region r #;
    855   Formula (all,r,REG)
    856       GOVEXP(r) = sum(i,TRAD_COMM, VGA(i,r));
    857    
    858   ! private consumption expenditure, PRIVEXP !
    859   Coefficient (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,h,HHLD)(all,r,REG)
    860       VPAH(i,h,r) # Expenditure on i in r by hhld h valued at agent's prices #;
    861   Formula (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,h,HHLD)(all,s,REG)
    862       VPAH(i,h,s) = VDPAH(i,h,s) + VIPAH(i,h,s);
    863    
    864   Coefficient (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,r,REG)
    865       VPA(i,r) # private hhld expenditure on i in r valued at agent's prices #;
    866   Formula (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,s,REG)
    867       VPA(i,s) = VDPA(i,s) + VIPA(i,s);
    868    
    869   Coefficient (all,h,HHLD)(all,r,REG)
    870       PRIVEXPH(h,r) # private consumption expenditure in region r by hhld h #;
    871   Formula (all,r,REG)(all,h,HHLD)
    872       PRIVEXPH(h,r) = sum(i,TRAD_COMM, VPAH(i,h,r));
    873    
    874   Coefficient (all,r,REG)
    875       PRIVEXP(r) # private consumption expenditure in region r #;
    876   Formula (all,r,REG)
    877       PRIVEXP(r) = sum(i,TRAD_COMM, VPA(i,r));
    878    
    879   ! aggregate expenditure + saving = aggregate income !
    880   Coefficient (all,r,REG)
    881       INCOME(r) # level of expenditure, which equals NET income in region r #;
    882   Formula (all,r,REG)
    883       INCOME(r) = PRIVEXP(r) + GOVEXP(r) + SAVE(r);
    884    
    885   Coefficient (all,r,REG)
    886       GOVINC(r) # Income earned by government in region r #;
    887   Formula (all,r,REG)
    888       GOVINC(r) = GOVEXP(r) + SAV_GOV(r);
    889    
    890   Coefficient (all,h,HHLD)(all,r,REG)
    891       HHLDINC(h,r) # Income earned by household h in region r #;
    892   Formula (all,r,REG)(all,h,HHLD)
    893       HHLDINC(h,r) = PRIVEXPH(h,r) + SAV_HHLD(h,r);
    894    
    895   !<
    896       Indirect Tax Receipts
    897       ---------------------
    898   >!
    899    
    900   Coefficient (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,r,REG)
    901       DGTAX(i,r) # tax on government consumption of domestic good i in region r #;
    902   Formula (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,r,REG)
    903       DGTAX(i,r) = VDGA(i,r) - VDGM(i,r);
    904   Coefficient (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,r,REG)
    905       IGTAX(i,r) # tax on government consumption of imported good i in region r #;
    906   Formula (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,r,REG)
    907       IGTAX(i,r) = VIGA(i,r) - VIGM(i,r);
    908   Coefficient (all,r,REG)
    909       TGC(r) # government consumption tax payments in r #;
    910   Formula (all,r,REG)
    911       TGC(r) = sum(i,TRAD_COMM, DGTAX(i,r) + IGTAX(i,r));
    912    
    913   Coefficient (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,r,REG)(all,h,HHLD)
    914       DPTAX(i,h,r) # tax on private consump of domestic good i in region r by h#;
    915   Formula (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,r,REG)(all,h,HHLD)
    916       DPTAX(i,h,r) = VDPAH(i,h,r) - VDPMH(i,h,r);
    917   Coefficient (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,r,REG)(all,h,HHLD)
    918       IPTAX(i,h,r) # tax on private consump of imported good i in region r by h#;
    919   Formula (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,r,REG)(all,h,HHLD)
    920       IPTAX(i,h,r) = VIPAH(i,h,r) - VIPMH(i,h,r);
    921   Coefficient (all,r,REG)
    922       TPC(r) # private consumption tax payments in r #;
    923   Formula (all,r,REG)
    924       TPC(r) = sum(h, HHLD, sum(i,TRAD_COMM, DPTAX(i,h,r) + IPTAX(i,h,r)));
    925    
    926   Coefficient (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,j,PROD_COMM)(all,r,REG)
    927       DFTAX(i,j,r) # tax on use of domestic intermediate good i by j in r #;
    928   Formula (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,j,PROD_COMM)(all,r,REG)
    929       DFTAX(i,j,r) = VDFA(i,j,r) - VDFM(i,j,r);
    930   Coefficient (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,j,PROD_COMM)(all,r,REG)
    931       IFTAX(i,j,r) # tax on use of imported intermediate good i by j in r #;
    932   Formula (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,j,PROD_COMM)(all,r,REG)
    933       IFTAX(i,j,r) = VIFA(i,j,r) - VIFM(i,j,r);
    934   Coefficient (all,r,REG)
    935       TIU(r) # firms' tax payments on intermediate goods usage in r #;
    936   Formula (all,r,REG)
    937       TIU(r) = sum(i,TRAD_COMM, sum(j,PROD_COMM, DFTAX(i,j,r) + IFTAX(i,j,r)));
    938    
    939   Coefficient (all,i,ENDW_COMM)(all,j,PROD_COMM)(all,r,REG)
    940       ETAX(i,j,r) # tax on use of endowment good i by industry j in region r #;
    941   Formula (all,i,ENDW_COMM)(all,j,PROD_COMM)(all,r,REG)
    942       ETAX(i,j,r) = VFA(i,j,r) - VFM(i,j,r);
    943   Coefficient (all,r,REG)
    944       TFU(r) # firms' tax payments on primary factor usage in r #;
    945   Formula (all,r,REG)
    946       TFU(r) = sum(i,ENDW_COMM, sum(j,PROD_COMM, ETAX(i,j,r)));
    947    
    948   Coefficient (all,i,ENDW_COMM)(all,h,HHLD)(all,r,REG)
    949       INCTAX(i,h,r) # output tax on good i in region r #;
    950   Formula (all,i,ENDW_COMM)(all,h,HHLD)(all,r,REG)
    951       INCTAX(i,h,r) = EVOMH(i,h,r) - EVOAH(i,h,r);
    952   Coefficient (all,i,NSAV_COMM)(all,r,REG)
    953       PTAX(i,r) # output tax on good i in region r #;
    954   Formula (all,i,NSAV_COMM)(all,r,REG)
    955       PTAX(i,r) = VOM(i,r) - VOA(i,r);
    956   Coefficient (all,r,REG)
    957       TOUT(r) # production tax payments in r #;
    958   Formula (all,r,REG)
    959       TOUT(r) = sum(i,PROD_COMM, PTAX(i,r));
    960    
    961   Coefficient (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,r,REG)(all,s,REG)
    962       XTAXD(i,r,s) # tax on exports of good i from source r to destination s #;
    963   Formula (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,r,REG)(all,s,REG)
    964       XTAXD(i,r,s) = VXWD(i,r,s) - VXMD(i,r,s);
    965   Coefficient (all,r,REG)
    966       TEX(r) # export tax payments in r #;
    967   Formula (all,r,REG)
    968       TEX(r) = sum(i,TRAD_COMM, sum(s,REG, XTAXD(i,r,s)));
    969    
    970   Coefficient (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,r,REG)(all,s,REG)
    971       MTAX(i,r,s) # tax on imports of good i from source r in destination s #;
    972   Formula (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,r,REG)(all,s,REG)
    973       MTAX(i,r,s) = VIMS(i,r,s) - VIWS(i,r,s);
    974   Coefficient (all,r,REG)
    975       TIM(r) # import tax payments in r #;
    976   Formula (all,r,REG)
    977       TIM(r) = sum(i,TRAD_COMM, sum(s,REG, MTAX(i,s,r)));
    978    
    979    
    980   !<
    981       Miscellaneous Coefficients
    982       --------------------------
    983   >!
    984    
    985   ! domestic/imported substitution elasticity !
    986   Coefficient (parameter)(all,i,TRAD_COMM)
    987       ESUBD(i)
    988       # region-generic el. of sub. domestic/imported for all agents #;
    989   Read
    990       ESUBD from file GTAPPARM header "ESBD";
    991    
    992   Coefficient (parameter)(all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,r,REG)
    993       ESUBDR(i,r)
    994       # region-specific el. of sub. among imports of i in Armington structure #;
    995   Formula (initial)(all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,r,REG)
    996       ESUBDR(i,r) = ESUBD(i) ;
    997   Read (ifheaderexists)
    998       ESUBDR from file GTAPPARM header "ESDR";
    999    
   1000   ! net global investment expenditure !
   1001   Coefficient (all,r,REG)
   1002       REGINV(r) # regional GROSS investment in r (value of "cgds" output) #;
   1003   Formula (all,r,REG)
   1004       REGINV(r) = sum(k,CGDS_COMM, VOA(k,r));
   1005   Coefficient (all,r,REG)
   1006       NETINV(r) # regional NET investment in region r #;
   1007   Formula (all,r,REG)
   1008       NETINV(r) = sum(k,CGDS_COMM, VOA(k,r)) - VDEP(r);
   1009   Coefficient
   1010       GLOBINV # global expenditures on net investment #;
   1011   Formula
   1012       GLOBINV = sum(r,REG, NETINV(r));
   1013    
   1014   ! elasticity of cost wrt utility from private consumption !
   1015   Coefficient (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,r,REG)(all,h,HHLD)
   1016       CONSHRH(i,h,r) # share of private hhld h devoted to good i in r #;
   1017   Formula (all,r,REG)(all,h,HHLD)(all,i,TRAD_COMM)
   1018       CONSHRH(i,h,r) = VPA(i,r) / PRIVEXP(r);
   1019   Formula (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,r,REG)(all,h,HHLD: PRIVEXPH(h,r)>0)
   1020       CONSHRH(i,h,r) = VPAH(i,h,r) / PRIVEXPH(h,r);
   1021    
   1022   Coefficient (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,r,REG)
   1023       CONSHR(i,r) # share of private hhld consumption devoted to good i in r #;
   1024   Formula (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,r,REG)
   1025       CONSHR(i,r) = VPA(i,r) / PRIVEXP(r);
   1026    
   1027   Coefficient (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,r,REG)(all,h,HHLD)
   1028       HHCONSSHR(i,h,r) # share of hhld consumption of i in r by each hhld #;
   1029   Formula (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,r,REG)(all,h,HHLD)
   1030       HHCONSSHR(i,h,r) = VPAH(i,h,r)/sum(k, HHLD, VPAH(i,k,r)) ;
   1031    
   1032   Coefficient (parameter)(all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,r,REG)
   1033       INCPAR(i,r)
   1034       # expansion parameter in the CDE minimum expenditure function #;
   1035   Read
   1036       INCPAR from file GTAPPARM header "INCP";
   1037    
   1038   Coefficient (all,h,HHLD)(all,r,REG)
   1039       UELASPRIVH(h,r)
   1040       # elasticity of cost wrt utility from private consumption by h#;
   1041   Formula (all,r,REG)(all,h,HHLD)
   1042       UELASPRIVH(h,r) = sum(i,TRAD_COMM, CONSHRH(i,h,r) * INCPAR(i,r));
   1043    
   1044   !<
   1045       =======
   1046       Modules
   1047       =======
   1048    
   1049       1. Government Consumption
   1050       2. Private Consumption
   1051       3. Firms
   1052       4. Investment, Global Bank, and Savings
   1053       5. International Trade
   1054       6. International Transport Services
   1055       7. Regional Household
   1056       8. Equilibrium Conditions
   1057   >!
   1058    
   1059    
   1060   !<
   1061       -------------------------
   1062       1. Government Consumption
   1063       -------------------------
   1064    
   1065       1-0. Module-Specific Variables
   1066       1-1. Demands for Composite Goods
   1067       1-2. Composite Tradeables
   1068   >!
   1069    
   1070    
   1071   !<
   1072       1-0. Module-Specific Variables
   1073       ------------------------------
   1074    
   1075       only used in this Government Consumption module
   1076   >!
   1077    
   1078   Variable (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,r,REG)
   1079       pg(i,r) # government consumption price for commodity i in region r #;
   1080   Variable (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,r,REG)
   1081       qg(i,r) # government hhld demand for commodity i in region r #;
   1082    
   1083    
   1084   !<
   1085       1-1. Demands for Composite Goods
   1086       --------------------------------
   1087   >!
   1088    
   1089   Equation GPRICEINDEX
   1090   # definition of price index for aggregate gov't purchases (HT 40) #
   1091   (all,r,REG)
   1092       pgov(r) = sum(i,TRAD_COMM, [VGA(i,r) / GOVEXP(r)] * pg(i,r));
   1093    
   1094   Equation GOVDMNDS
   1095   # government consumption demands for composite commodities (HT 41) #
   1096   (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,r,REG)
   1097       qg(i,r) = qgov(r) - [pg(i,r) - pgov(r)];
   1098    
   1099   Equation GOVU
   1100   # utility from government consumption in r #
   1101   (all,r,REG)
   1102       yg(r) = pgov(r) + qgov(r);
   1103    
   1104    
   1105   !<
   1106       1-2. Composite Tradeables
   1107       -------------------------
   1108   >!
   1109    
   1110   Variable (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,r,REG)
   1111       tgd(i,r) # tax on domestic i purchased by government hhld in r #;
   1112    
   1113   Variable (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,r,REG)
   1114       tgm(i,r) # tax on imported i purchased by gov't hhld in r #;
   1115    
   1116   Equation GHHDPRICE
   1117   # eq'n links domestic market and government consumption prices (HT 19) #
   1118   (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,r,REG)
   1119       pgd(i,r) = tgd(i,r) + pm(i,r);
   1120    
   1121   Equation GHHIPRICES
   1122   # eq'n links domestic market and government consumption prices (HT 22) #
   1123   (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,r,REG)
   1124       pgm(i,r) = tgm(i,r) + pim(i,r);
   1125    
   1126   Coefficient (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,s,REG)
   1127       GMSHR(i,s) # share of imports for gov't hhld at agent's prices #;
   1128   Formula (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,s,REG)
   1129       GMSHR(i,s) = VIGA(i,s) / VGA(i,s);
   1130    
   1131   Equation GCOMPRICE
   1132   # government consumption price for composite commodities (HT 42) #
   1133   (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,s,REG)
   1134       pg(i,s) =  GMSHR(i,s) * pgm(i,s) + [1 - GMSHR(i,s)] * pgd(i,s);
   1135    
   1136   Equation GHHLDAGRIMP
   1137   # government consumption demand for aggregate imports (HT 43) #
   1138   (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,s,REG)
   1139       qgm(i,s) = qg(i,s)
   1140                + ESUBDR(i,s) * [pg(i,s) - pgm(i,s)];
   1141    
   1142   Equation GHHLDDOM
   1143   # government consumption demand for domestic goods (HT 44) #
   1144   (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,s,REG)
   1145       qgd(i,s) = qg(i,s)
   1146                + ESUBDR(i,s) * [pg(i,s) - pgd(i,s)];
   1147    
   1148   Equation TGCRATIO
   1149   # change in ratio of government consumption tax payments to regional income #
   1150   (all,r,REG)
   1151       100.0 * INCOME(r) * del_taxrgc(r) + TGC(r) * y(r)
   1152           = sum(i,TRAD_COMM,
   1153               VDGA(i,r) * tgd(i,r) + DGTAX(i,r) * [pm(i,r) + qgd(i,r)])
   1154           + sum(i,TRAD_COMM,
   1155               VIGA(i,r) * tgm(i,r) + IGTAX(i,r) * [pim(i,r) + qgm(i,r)]);
   1156    
   1157    
   1158   !<
   1159       -----------------------------
   1160       2. Private Consumption Module
   1161       -----------------------------
   1162    
   1163       2-0. Module-Specific Variables
   1164       2-1. Utility from Private Consumption
   1165       2-2. Allen Partials, Price and Income Elasticities, Composite Demand
   1166       2-3. Composite Tradeables
   1167   >!
   1168    
   1169    
   1170   !<
   1171       2-0. Module-Specific Variables
   1172       ------------------------------
   1173    
   1174       only used in this Private Consumption module
   1175   >!
   1176    
   1177   Variable (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,r,REG)
   1178       pp(i,r) # private consumption price for commodity i in region r #;
   1179   Variable (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,r,REG)(all,h,HHLD)
   1180       pph(i,h,r) # private consumption price for commodity i in region r by h#;
   1181    
   1182   Variable (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,r,REG)
   1183       qp(i,r) # private hhld demand for commodity i in region r #;
   1184   Variable (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,r,REG)(all,h,HHLD)
   1185       qph(i,h,r) # private hhld demand for commodity i in region r by hhld h #;
   1186    
   1187    
   1188   !<
   1189       2-1. Utility from Private Consumption
   1190       -------------------------------------
   1191   >!
   1192    
   1193   Equation E_pp
   1194   # price index for private consumption expenditure #
   1195   (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,r,REG)
   1196       pp(i,r) = sum(h, HHLD, HHCONSSHR(i,h,r) * pph(i,h,r));
   1197    
   1198   Equation PHHLDINDEX
   1199   # price index for private consumption expenditure #
   1200   (all,r,REG)
   1201       ppriv(r) = sum(i,TRAD_COMM, CONSHR(i,r) * pp(i,r));
   1202    
   1203   Equation E_pprivh
   1204   # price index for private consumption expenditure by hhld h #
   1205   (all,r,REG)(all,h,HHLD)
   1206       pprivh(h,r) = sum(i,TRAD_COMM, CONSHRH(i,h,r) * pph(i,h,r));
   1207    
   1208   Equation E_yph
   1209   # computation of utility from private consumption in r by hhld h (HT 45) #
   1210   (all,r,REG)(all,h,HHLD)
   1211       yph(h,r) - poph(h,r) =
   1212                    [pprivh(h,r) + UELASPRIVH(h,r) * uph(h,r)];
   1213    
   1214   !WARNING: all poph changes with pop by the same percentages. If you want to
   1215   shock poph independently you can do so via spoph, however you will need to
   1216   ensure that pop changes by the appropriate amount or that some other households
   1217   pop changes if the popultion is shifting between households. Note also that
   1218   changing pop does not change the labour force, so if you want to examine the
   1219   impact of movement between households changes are required to the model. !
   1220    
   1221   ! Pete, I think this is not so important at this stage, but  thought I'd include
   1222   a warning. !
   1223    
   1224   Equation E_yp
   1225   # computation of utility from private consumption in r (HT 45) #
   1226   (all,r,REG)
   1227       PRIVEXP(r) * yp(r) = sum(h, HHLD, PRIVEXPH(h,r) * yph(h,r)) ;
   1228    
   1229   !<
   1230       This equation determines private consumption utility for a representative
   1231       household in region r, based on the per capita private expenditure
   1232       function.  (HT 45)
   1233   >!
   1234    
   1235   Coefficient (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,r,REG)(all,h,HHLD)
   1236       XWCONSHR(i,h,r)
   1237       # expansion-parameter-weighted consumption share #;
   1238   Formula (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,r,REG)(all,h,HHLD)
   1239       XWCONSHR(i,h,r) = CONSHRH(i,h,r) * INCPAR(i,r) / UELASPRIVH(h,r);
   1240    
   1241   Equation UTILELASPRIV
   1242   # elasticity of expenditure wrt utility from private consumption #
   1243   (all,r,REG)(all,h,HHLD)
   1244       ueprivh(h,r)
   1245       = sum(i,TRAD_COMM, XWCONSHR(i,h,r) * [pph(i,h,r) + qph(i,h,r) - yph(h,r)]);
   1246    
   1247    
   1248   !<
   1249       2-2. Allen Partials, Price and Income Elasticities,
   1250           and FRISCH parameter calibration
   1251       --------------------------------------------------------------------
   1252   >!
   1253    
   1254   Coefficient (parameter)(all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,r,REG)
   1255       SUBPAR(i,r)
   1256       # substitution parameter in CDE minimum expenditure function #;
   1257   Read
   1258       SUBPAR from file GTAPPARM header "SUBP";
   1259    
   1260   !<
   1261       (HT F1 - F3)
   1262   >!
   1263   Coefficient (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,r,REG)
   1264       ALPHA(i,r) # 1 - sub. parameter in the CDE minimum expenditure function #;
   1265   Formula (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,r,REG)
   1266       ALPHA(i,r) = 1 - SUBPAR(i,r);
   1267    
   1268   Coefficient (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,k,TRAD_COMM)(all,h,HHLD)(all,r,REG)
   1269       APE(i,k,h,r) # Allen partial elst. of sub. between composite i and k in r #;
   1270   Formula (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,k,TRAD_COMM)(all,r,REG)(all,h,HHLD)
   1271       APE(i,k,h,r)
   1272           = ALPHA(i,r) + ALPHA(k,r)
   1273           - sum(n,TRAD_COMM, CONSHRH(n,h,r) * ALPHA(n,r));
   1274   Formula (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,h,HHLD)(all,r,REG)
   1275       APE(i,i,h,r)
   1276           = 2.0 * ALPHA(i,r)
   1277           - sum(n,TRAD_COMM, CONSHRH(n,h,r) * ALPHA(n,r))
   1278           - ALPHA(i,r) / CONSHRH(i,h,r);
   1279    
   1280   Coefficient (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,h,HHLD)(all,r,REG)
   1281       EY(i,h,r) # income elast. of private hhld demand for i in r (HT F4) #;
   1282   Formula (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,h,HHLD)(all,r,REG)
   1283       EY(i,h,r)
   1284           =   [1.0 / sum(n,TRAD_COMM, CONSHRH(n,h,r) * INCPAR(n,r))]
   1285               * [INCPAR(i,r) * [1.0 - ALPHA(i,r)]
   1286                   + sum(n,TRAD_COMM, CONSHRH(n,h,r) * INCPAR(n,r) * ALPHA(n,r))]
   1287           + [ALPHA(i,r) - sum(n,TRAD_COMM, CONSHRH(n,h,r) * ALPHA(n,r))];
   1288    
   1289   Coefficient (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,k,TRAD_COMM)(all,r,REG)(all,h,HHLD)
   1290       EP(i,k,h,r)
   1291       # uncomp. elast. of private hhld demand for i wrt price of k in r (HT F5) #;
   1292   Formula (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,k,TRAD_COMM)(all,r,REG)(all,h,HHLD)
   1293       EP(i,k,h,r) = 0;
   1294   Formula (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,k,TRAD_COMM)(all,r,REG)(all,h,HHLD)
   1295       EP(i,k,h,r) = [APE(i,k,h,r) - EY(i,h,r)] * CONSHRH(k,h,r);
   1296    
   1297   Coefficient (all,h,HHLD)(all,r,REG)
   1298       FRISCH(h,r)
   1299   # Frisch LES 'parameter' dependednt on EY, EP and CONSHR #;
   1300   Formula (initial)(all,h,HHLD)(all,r,REG)
   1301       FRISCH(h,r) = sum{c, TRAD_COMM, CONSHRH(c,h,r) * EY(c,h,r) *
   1302          [1.0 - CONSHRH(c,h,r) * EY(c,h,r)]/
   1303          [EP(c,c,h,r) + CONSHRH(c,h,r) * EY(c,h,r)]};
   1304   Read (ifheaderexists)  FRISCH from file GTAPDATA header "FRSH";
   1305   ! ifheaderexists used if user wants to specify their own FRISCH parameters.!
   1306    
   1307   Coefficient (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,h,HHLD)(all,r,REG)
   1308       EPS(i,h,r) # Household expenditure elasticities - calibrated from EY #;
   1309   Formula (initial)(all,c,TRAD_COMM)(all,h,HHLD)(all,r,REG)
   1310       EPS(c,h,r) = EY(c,h,r) ;
   1311   Read (ifheaderexists) EPS from file GTAPDATA header "XPEL";
   1312   ! ifheaderexists used if user wants to specify their own EPS parameters.!
   1313    
   1314   Coefficient (all,r,REG)
   1315       CHKFRISCH(r) #Check Frisch Parm of LES country is >-1.8#;
   1316   Formula (all,r,REG)
   1317       CHKFRISCH(r) = maxs(h, HHLD, FRISCH(h,r));
   1318    
   1319   Coefficient (integer,parameter)(all,r,REG)
   1320       PRIVTYPE(r) # Use CDE or LES in private consumption #;
   1321   Formula (initial)(all,r,REG)
   1322       PRIVTYPE(r) = 0 + if(CHKFRISCH(r)<-1.8,1) ;
   1323   Read (ifheaderexists)
   1324       PRIVTYPE from file GTAPPARM header "PREG";
   1325   ! ifheaderexists used if user wants to specify which countries are to use LES !
   1326    
   1327   Set
   1328       REG_LES # Countries for which the LES system applies#
   1329       = (all,r,REG: PRIVTYPE(r)>0);
   1330    
   1331   Set
   1332       REG_CDE # Countries for which the CDE system applies#
   1333       = (all,r,REG: PRIVTYPE(r)=0);
   1334    
   1335   Assertion (all,h,HHLD)(all,r,REG_LES)
   1336       FRISCH(h,r)<-1.8 ;
   1337   ! Note that if user specifies countries as LES in PREG.  But the FRISCH
   1338   of these countries is > -1.8, then the model will stop.
   1339   FRISCH should be a large negative for LES countries. !
   1340    
   1341   !<
   1342       2-2.b CDE Household Demand System
   1343       ---------------------------------
   1344    
   1345   >!
   1346    
   1347   Equation PRIVDMNDS
   1348   # private consumption demand by hhld h for composite commodities (HT 46) #
   1349   (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,r,REG_CDE)(all,h,HHLD)
   1350       qph(i,h,r) - poph(h,r)
   1351           = sum(k,TRAD_COMM, EP(i,k,h,r) * pph(k,h,r))
   1352                  + EY(i,h,r) * [yph(h,r) - poph(h,r)];
   1353    
   1354   Equation E_qp
   1355   # private consumption demands for composite commodities (HT 46) #
   1356   (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,r,REG)
   1357       qp(i,r) = sum(h, HHLD, HHCONSSHR(i,h,r) * qph(i,h,r));
   1358   !<
   1359       Private consumption demands for composite commodities.  Demand system is
   1360       on a per capita basis.  Here, yp(r) - pop(r) is % change in per capita
   1361       income.  (HT 46)
   1362   >!
   1363    
   1364   !<
   1365       2-2.b Alternate-Household Demand System (LES) for Developing Countries.
   1366       -----------------------------------------------------------------
   1367    
   1368   >!
   1369   Variable (all,h,HHLD)(all,r,REG_LES)
   1370       Utility_LES(h,r) # Utility per household #;
   1371    
   1372   Variable (all,h,HHLD)(all,r,REG_LES)
   1373       yph_lux(h,r) # Household - supernumerary demands #;
   1374    
   1375   Variable (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,h,HHLD)(all,r,REG_LES)
   1376       qph_lux(i,h,r) # Household - supernumerary demands of commodity i #;
   1377    
   1378   Variable (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,h,HHLD)(all,r,REG_LES)
   1379       qph_sub(i,h,r)  # Household - subsistance demands of commodity i #;
   1380    
   1381   Variable (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,h,HHLD)(all,r,REG_LES)
   1382       alux(i,h,r) # Taste Change, household luxury demands#;
   1383    
   1384   Variable (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,h,HHLD)(all,r,REG_LES)
   1385       asub(i,h,r) #Taste Change, household subsistance demands#;
   1386    
   1387   Variable (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,h,HHLD)(all,r,REG_LES)
   1388       s_sub(i,h,r) #Taste change shifter for subsistence #;
   1389    
   1390   Update (change)(all,h,HHLD)(all,r,REG_LES)
   1391       FRISCH(h,r) = FRISCH(h,r) * [yph(h,r) - yph_lux(h,r)]/100.0;
   1392    
   1393   Update(change)(all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,h,HHLD)(all,r,REG_LES)
   1394       EPS(i,h,r) = EPS(i,h,r)*[qph_lux(i,h,r)-qph(i,h,r)
   1395                           + yph(h,r) - yph_lux(h,r)]/100.0;
   1396    
   1397   Coefficient (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,h,HHLD)(all,r,REG_LES)
   1398       SHR_LUX(i,h,r) # (Luxury/total expenditure) #;
   1399   Formula (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,h,HHLD)(all,r,REG_LES)
   1400       SHR_LUX(i,h,r) = EPS(i,h,r)/ABS[FRISCH(h,r)];
   1401    
   1402   Coefficient (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,h,HHLD)(all,r,REG_LES)
   1403       BETA_LUX(i,h,r) # Marginal household budget shares #;
   1404   Formula (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,h,HHLD)(all,r,REG_LES)
   1405       BETA_LUX(i,h,r) = EPS(i,h,r) * CONSHRH(i,h,r);
   1406    
   1407   Equation E_qlux
   1408   # Luxury demand for  commodities #
   1409   (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,h, HHLD)(all,r,REG_LES)
   1410       qph_lux(i,h,r) + pph(i,h,r) = yph_lux(h,r) + alux(i,h,r);
   1411    
   1412   Equation E_qsub
   1413   # Subsistence demand for  commodities #
   1414   (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,h,HHLD)(all,r,REG_LES)
   1415       qph_sub(i,h,r) = poph(h,r) + asub(i,h,r);
   1416    
   1417   Equation E_qph
   1418   #Total Household demand form composite commodities#
   1419   (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,h,HHLD)(all,r,REG_LES)
   1420       qph(i,h,r)=SHR_LUX(i,h,r)*qph_lux(i,h,r)+[1-SHR_LUX(i,h,r)]*qph_sub(i,h,r);
   1421    
   1422   Equation E_utility_LES
   1423   # Change in utility disregarding taste change terms #
   1424   (all,h,HHLD)(all,r,REG_LES)
   1425       utility_LES(h,r) = sum{i,TRAD_COMM, BETA_LUX(i,h,r)*qph_lux(i,h,r)};
   1426    
   1427   Equation E_alux
   1428   # Default setting for luxury taste shifter #
   1429   (all,i,TRAD_COMM) (all,h,HHLD)(all,r,REG_LES)
   1430       alux(i,h,r) = asub(i,h,r) - sum{k,TRAD_COMM, BETA_LUX(k,h,r)*asub(k,h,r)};
   1431    
   1432   Equation  E_asub
   1433   # Default setting for subsistence taste shifter #
   1434   (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,h,HHLD)(all,r,REG_LES)
   1435       asub(i,h,r) = s_sub(i,h,r) -
   1436                       sum{k,TRAD_COMM, CONSHRH(k,h,r)*s_sub(k,h,r)};
   1437    
   1438   Equation  E_yph_lux
   1439   # Finds yph_lux #
   1440   (all,h,HHLD)(all,r,REG_LES)
   1441       yph(h,r) =
   1442               sum(i, TRAD_COMM, CONSHRH(i,h,r) * (qph(i,h,r) + pph(i,h,r))) ;
   1443    
   1444    
   1445   !<
   1446       2-3. Composite Tradeables
   1447       -------------------------
   1448   >!
   1449    
   1450   Variable (all,r,REG)
   1451       tp(r) # comm.-, source-gen. shift in tax on private cons. #;
   1452   !<
   1453       The variable tp(r) can be swapped with del_ttaxr(r) in order to generate a
   1454       tax replacement scenario, whereby taxes remain a constant share of
   1455       national income.
   1456   >!
   1457    
   1458   Variable (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,r,REG)
   1459       tpd(i,r) # comm.-, source-spec. shift in tax on private cons. of dom. #;
   1460   Variable (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,h,HHLD)(all,r,REG)
   1461       tpdh(i,h,r)
   1462       # comm.-, source-, hhld-spec. shift in tax on priv cons. of dom. #;
   1463   Variable (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,r,REG)(all,h,HHLD)
   1464       atpdh(i,h,r)
   1465       # power of tax on domestic i purchased by private hhld h in r #;
   1466   Equation TPDSHIFT
   1467       # permits uniform consumption tax change #
   1468   (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,h,HHLD)(all,r,REG)
   1469       atpdh(i,h,r) = tpdh(i,h,r) + tpd(i,r) + tp(r);
   1470    
   1471   Equation PHHDPRICE
   1472   # eq'n links domestic market and private consumption prices (HT 18) #
   1473   (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,r,REG)(all,h,HHLD)
   1474       ppdh(i,h,r) = atpdh(i,h,r) + pm(i,r);
   1475    
   1476   Variable (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,r,REG)
   1477       tpm(i,r) # comm.-, source-spec. shift in tax on private cons. of imp. #;
   1478   Variable (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,r,REG)(all,h,HHLD)
   1479       tpmh(i,h,r)
   1480       # comm.-, source-, hhld-spec. shift in tax on priv cons. of imp. #;
   1481   Variable (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,r,REG)(all,h,HHLD)
   1482       atpmh(i,h,r) # power of tax on imported i purchased by private hhld in r #;
   1483   Equation TPMSHIFT
   1484       # permits uniform consumption tax change #
   1485   (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,r,REG)(all,h,HHLD)
   1486       atpmh(i,h,r) = tpmh(i,h,r) + tpm(i,r) + tp(r);
   1487    
   1488   Equation PHHIPRICES
   1489   # eq'n links domestic market and private consumption prices (HT 21) #
   1490   (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,r,REG)(all,h,HHLD)
   1491       ppmh(i,h,r) = atpmh(i,h,r) + pim(i,r);
   1492    
   1493   Equation TPCRATIO
   1494   # change in ratio of private consumption tax payments to regional income #
   1495   (all,r,REG)
   1496       100.0 * INCOME(r) * del_taxrpc(r) + TPC(r) * y(r)
   1497           = sum(h, HHLD, sum(i,TRAD_COMM,
   1498          VDPAH(i,h,r) * atpdh(i,h,r) + DPTAX(i,h,r) * [pm(i,r) + qpdh(i,h,r)])
   1499           + sum(i,TRAD_COMM,
   1500          VIPAH(i,h,r) * atpmh(i,h,r) + IPTAX(i,h,r) * [pim(i,r) + qpmh(i,h,r)]));
   1501    
   1502   Coefficient (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,s,REG)(all,h,HHLD)
   1503       PMSHRH(i,h,s) # share of imports for priv hhld at agent's prices #;
   1504   Formula (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,s,REG)(all,h,HHLD)
   1505       PMSHRH(i,h,s) = VIPA(i,s) / VPA(i,s);
   1506   Formula (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,s,REG)(all,h,HHLD: VPAH(i,h,s)>0)
   1507       PMSHRH(i,h,s) = VIPAH(i,h,s) / VPAH(i,h,s);
   1508    
   1509   Equation PCOMPRICE
   1510   # private consumption price for composite commodities for hhld h (HT 47) #
   1511   (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,s,REG)(all,h,HHLD)
   1512       pph(i,h,s) = PMSHRH(i,h,s) * ppmh(i,h,s) + [1 - PMSHRH(i,h,s)]*ppdh(i,h,s);
   1513    
   1514   Equation PHHLDDOM
   1515   # private consumption demand for domestic goods by hhld h (HT 48) #
   1516   (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,s,REG)(all,h,HHLD)
   1517       qpdh(i,h,s) = qph(i,h,s)
   1518                   + ESUBDR(i,s) * [pph(i,h,s) - ppdh(i,h,s)];
   1519    
   1520   Equation PHHLDAGRIMP
   1521   # private consumption demand for aggregate imports by hhld h (HT 49) #
   1522   (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,s,REG)(all,h,HHLD)
   1523       qpmh(i,h,s) = qph(i,h,s)
   1524                   + ESUBDR(i,s) * [pph(i,h,s) - ppmh(i,h,s)];
   1525    
   1526   Equation E_qpd
   1527   # private consumption demand for domestic goods (HT 48) #
   1528   (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,s,REG)
   1529       VDPA(i,s) * qpd(i,s) = sum(h, HHLD, VDPAH(i,h,s) * qpdh(i,h,s));
   1530    
   1531   Equation E_qpm
   1532   # private consumption demand for aggregate imports (HT 49) #
   1533   (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,s,REG)
   1534       VIPA(i,s) * qpm(i,s) = sum(h, HHLD, VIPAH(i,h,s) * qpmh(i,h,s));
   1535    
   1536   !<
   1537       ---------
   1538       3. Firms
   1539       ---------
   1540    
   1541       We now turn to the behavioral equations for firms.  The following picture
   1542       describes factor demands.  The first set of equations describe demands for
   1543       primary factors.  (See table 4 of Hertel and Tsigas.)
   1544    
   1545       Production structure
   1546       --------------------
   1547    
   1548                                qo(j,r)  [ao(j,r)]
   1549                                /\
   1550                               /  \  <----- CES
   1551                              /    \
   1552                             /      \
   1553                            /        \
   1554         [ava(j,r)]  qva(j,r)        qf(i,j,r)  [af(i,j,r)]
   1555                     /|\                    /\
   1556    CES ----->      / | \                  /  \  <------ CES
   1557                   /  |  \                /    \
   1558                  /   |   \              /      \
   1559                 /    |    \            /        \
   1560             Land   Labor  Capital  Domestic     Foreign
   1561                  qfe(i,j,r)         qfd(i,j,r)  qfm(i,j,r)
   1562                [afe(i,j,r)]
   1563    
   1564    
   1565    
   1566       3-0. Module-Specific Variables
   1567       3-1. Total Output Nest
   1568       3-2. Composite Intermediates Nest
   1569       3-3. Value-Added Nest
   1570       3-4. Zero Profits Equations
   1571   >!
   1572    
   1573    
   1574   !<
   1575       3-0. Module-Specific Variables
   1576       ------------------------------
   1577    
   1578       only used in this Firms module or the Summary Indices or Welfare
   1579       appendices
   1580   >!
   1581    
   1582   Variable (all,j,PROD_COMM)(all,r,REG)
   1583       pva(j,r) # firms' price of value added in industry j of region r #;
   1584   Variable (all,j,PROD_COMM)(all,r,REG)
   1585       qva(j,r) # value added in industry j of region r #;
   1586   Variable (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,j,PROD_COMM)(all,r,REG)
   1587       pf(i,j,r) # firms' price for commodity i for use by j in r #;
   1588   Variable (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,j,PROD_COMM)(all,r,REG)
   1589       qf(i,j,r) # demand for commodity i for use by j in region r #;
   1590   Variable (all,j,PROD_COMM)(all,r,REG)
   1591       ao(j,r) # output augmenting technical change in sector j of r #;
   1592   Variable (all,i,PROD_COMM)(all,r,REG)
   1593       ava(i,r) # value added augmenting tech change in sector i of r #;
   1594   Variable (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,j,PROD_COMM)(all,r,REG)
   1595       af(i,j,r) # composite intermed. input i augmenting tech change by j of r #;
   1596   Variable (all,i,ENDW_COMM)(all,j,PROD_COMM)(all,r,REG)
   1597       afe(i,j,r) # primary factor i augmenting tech change by j of r #;
   1598   Variable (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,r,REG)(all,s,REG)
   1599       ams(i,r,s) # import i from region r augmenting tech change in region s #;
   1600    
   1601   !<
   1602       3-1. Total Output Nest
   1603       ----------------------
   1604   >!
   1605    
   1606   Variable (all,j,PROD_COMM)
   1607       aosec(j) # output tech change of sector j, worldwide #;
   1608   Variable (all,r,REG)
   1609       aoreg(r) # output tech change in region r #;
   1610   Variable (all,j,PROD_COMM)(all,r,REG)
   1611       aoall(j,r) # output augmenting technical change in sector j of r #;
   1612   Equation AOWORLD
   1613   # sector/region specific average rate of output augmenting tech change #
   1614   (all,j,PROD_COMM)(all,r,REG)
   1615       ao(j,r) = aosec(j) + aoreg(r) + aoall(j,r);
   1616    
   1617   Variable (all,j,PROD_COMM)
   1618       avasec(j) # value added tech change of sector j, worldwide #;
   1619   Variable (all,r,REG)
   1620       avareg(r) # value added tech change in region r #;
   1621   Variable (all,j,PROD_COMM)(all,r,REG)
   1622       avaall(j,r) # value added augmenting technical change in sector j of r #;
   1623   Equation AVAWORLD
   1624   # sector/region specific average rate of value added augmenting tech change #
   1625   (all,j,PROD_COMM)(all,r,REG)
   1626       ava(j,r) = avasec(j) + avareg(r) + avaall(j,r);
   1627    
   1628   Coefficient (parameter)(all,j,PROD_COMM)
   1629       ESUBT(j)
   1630       # elst. of sub. among composite intermediate inputs in production #;
   1631   Read
   1632       ESUBT from file GTAPPARM header "ESBT";
   1633    
   1634   Equation VADEMAND
   1635   # sector demands for primary factor composite #
   1636   (all,j,PROD_COMM)(all,r,REG)
   1637       qva(j,r)
   1638           = -ava(j,r) + qo(j,r) - ao(j,r)
   1639           - ESUBT(j) * [pva(j,r) - ava(j,r) - ps(j,r) - ao(j,r)];
   1640   !<
   1641       Sector demands for primary factor composite.  This equation differs from
   1642       HT 35 due to the presence of intermediate input substitution.
   1643   >!
   1644    
   1645   Variable (all,i,TRAD_COMM)
   1646       afcom(i) # intermediate tech change of input i, worldwide #;
   1647   Variable (all,j,PROD_COMM)
   1648       afsec(j) # intermediate tech change of sector j, worldwide #;
   1649   Variable (all,r,REG)
   1650       afreg(r) # intermediate tech change in region r #;
   1651   Variable (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,j,PROD_COMM)(all,r,REG)
   1652       afall(i,j,r) # intermediate input i augmenting tech change by j in r #;
   1653   Equation AFWORLD
   1654   # sector/region specific average rate of intermediates augmenting tech change #
   1655   (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,j,PROD_COMM)(all,r,REG)
   1656       af(i,j,r) = afcom(i) + afsec(j) + afreg(r) + afall(i,j,r);
   1657    
   1658   Equation INTDEMAND
   1659   # industry demands for intermediate inputs, including cgds #
   1660   (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,j,PROD_COMM)(all,r,REG)
   1661       qf(i,j,r)
   1662           = - af(i,j,r) + qo(j,r) - ao(j,r)
   1663           - ESUBT(j) * [pf(i,j,r) - af(i,j,r) - ps(j,r) - ao(j,r)];
   1664   !<
   1665       Industry demands for intermediate inputs, including cgds.  This equation
   1666       differs from HT 36 due to the presence of intermediate input substitution.
   1667   >!
   1668    
   1669    
   1670   !<
   1671       3-2. Composite Intermediates Nest
   1672       ---------------------------------
   1673   >!
   1674    
   1675   Variable (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,j,PROD_COMM)(all,r,REG)
   1676       tfd(i,j,r) # tax on domestic i purchased by j in r #;
   1677   Equation DMNDDPRICE
   1678   # eq'n links domestic market and firm prices (HT 20) #
   1679   (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,j,PROD_COMM)(all,r,REG)
   1680       pfd(i,j,r) = tfd(i,j,r) + pm(i,r);
   1681   !<
   1682       This equation links domestic market and firm prices.  It holds only for
   1683       domestic goods and it captures the effect of commodity taxation of firms.
   1684       (HT 20)
   1685   >!
   1686    
   1687   Variable (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,j,PROD_COMM)(all,r,REG)
   1688       tfm(i,j,r) # tax on imported i purchased by j in r #;
   1689   Equation DMNDIPRICES
   1690   # eq'n links domestic market and firm prices (HT 23) #
   1691   (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,j,PROD_COMM)(all,r,REG)
   1692       pfm(i,j,r) = tfm(i,j,r) + pim(i,r);
   1693   !<
   1694       This equation links domestic market and firm prices.  It holds only for
   1695       imported goods and it captures the effect of commodity taxation of firms.
   1696       (HT 23)
   1697   >!
   1698    
   1699   Equation TIURATIO
   1700   # change in ratio of tax payments on intermediate goods to regional income #
   1701   (all,r,REG)
   1702       100.0 * INCOME(r) * del_taxriu(r) + TIU(r) * y(r)
   1703           = sum(i,TRAD_COMM, sum(j,PROD_COMM,
   1704               VDFA(i,j,r) * tfd(i,j,r) + DFTAX(i,j,r) * [pm(i,r) + qfd(i,j,r)]))
   1705           + sum(i,TRAD_COMM, sum(j,PROD_COMM,
   1706               VIFA(i,j,r) * tfm(i,j,r) + IFTAX(i,j,r) * [pim(i,r) + qfm(i,j,r)]));
   1707    
   1708   Coefficient (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,j,PROD_COMM)(all,s,REG)
   1709       FMSHR(i,j,s) # share of firms' imports in dom. composite, agent's prices #;
   1710   Formula (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,j,PROD_COMM)(all,s,REG)
   1711       FMSHR(i,j,s) = VIFA(i,j,s) / VFA(i,j,s);
   1712   Equation ICOMPRICE
   1713   # industry price for composite commodities (HT 30) #
   1714   (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,j,PROD_COMM)(all,r,REG)
   1715       pf(i,j,r) = FMSHR(i,j,r) * pfm(i,j,r) + [1 - FMSHR(i,j,r)] * pfd(i,j,r);
   1716    
   1717   Equation INDIMP
   1718   # industry j demands for composite import i (HT 31) #
   1719   (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,j,PROD_COMM)(all,s,REG)
   1720       qfm(i,j,s) = qf(i,j,s)
   1721                  - ESUBDR(i,s) * [pfm(i,j,s) - pf(i,j,s)];
   1722    
   1723   Equation INDDOM
   1724   # industry j demands for domestic good i (HT 32) #
   1725   (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,j,PROD_COMM)(all,s,REG)
   1726       qfd(i,j,s) = qf(i,j,s)
   1727                  - ESUBDR(i,s) * [pfd(i,j,s) - pf(i,j,s)];
   1728    
   1729   !<
   1730       3-3. Value-Added Nest
   1731       ---------------------
   1732   >!
   1733    
   1734   Variable (all,i,ENDW_COMM)(all,j,PROD_COMM)(all,r,REG)
   1735       tf(i,j,r) # tax on primary factor i used by j in region r #;
   1736    
   1737   Equation MPFACTPRICE
   1738   # eq'n links domestic and firm demand prices (HT 16) #
   1739   (all,i,ENDWM_COMM)(all,j,PROD_COMM)(all,r,REG)
   1740       pfe(i,j,r) = tf(i,j,r) + pm(i,r);
   1741    
   1742   Equation SPFACTPRICE
   1743   # eq'n links domestic and firm demand prices (HT 17) #
   1744   (all,i,ENDWS_COMM)(all,j,PROD_COMM)(all,r,REG)
   1745       pfe(i,j,r) = tf(i,j,r) + pmes(i,j,r);
   1746    
   1747   Variable (all,i,ENDW_COMM)
   1748       afecom(i) # factor input tech change of input i, worldwide #;
   1749   Variable (all,j,PROD_COMM)
   1750       afesec(j) # factor input tech change of sector j, worldwide #;
   1751   Variable (all,r,REG)
   1752       afereg(r) # factor input tech change in region r #;
   1753   Variable (all,i,ENDW_COMM)(all,j,PROD_COMM)(all,r,REG)
   1754       afeall(i,j,r) # primary factor i augmenting tech change sector j in r #;
   1755   Equation AFEWORLD
   1756   # sector/region specific average rate of prim. factor i augmenting tech change #
   1757   (all,i,ENDW_COMM)(all,j,PROD_COMM)(all,r,REG)
   1758       afe(i,j,r) = afecom(i) + afesec(j) + afereg(r) + afeall(i,j,r);
   1759    
   1760   Coefficient (all,j,PROD_COMM)(all,r,REG)
   1761       VVA(j,r) # value added in activity j in region r #;
   1762   Formula (all,j,PROD_COMM)(all,r,REG)
   1763       VVA(j,r) = sum(i,ENDW_COMM, VFA(i,j,r));
   1764   Coefficient (all,i,ENDW_COMM)
   1765       SVADEFAULT(i) #zerodivide default for SVA#;
   1766   Formula (all,i,ENDW_COMM)
   1767       SVADEFAULT(i)
   1768           = sum(j,PROD_COMM, sum(r,REG, VFA(i,j,r)))
   1769           / sum(j,PROD_COMM, sum(r,REG, VVA(j,r)));
   1770   Coefficient (all,i,ENDW_COMM)(all,j,PROD_COMM)(all,r,REG)
   1771       SVA(i,j,r) # share of i in total value added in j in r #;
   1772   Formula (all,i,ENDW_COMM)(all,j,PROD_COMM)(all,r,REG: VVA(j,r) <> 0)
   1773       SVA(i,j,r) = VFA(i,j,r) / VVA(j,r);
   1774   Formula (all,i,ENDW_COMM)(all,j,PROD_COMM)(all,r,REG: VVA(j,r) = 0)
   1775       SVA(i,j,r) = SVADEFAULT(i);
   1776   Equation VAPRICE
   1777   # effective price of primary factor composite in each sector/region (HT 33) #
   1778   (all,j,PROD_COMM)(all,r,REG)
   1779       pva(j,r) = sum(k,ENDW_COMM, SVA(k,j,r) * [pfe(k,j,r) - afe(k,j,r)]);
   1780    
   1781   Equation TFURATIO
   1782   # change in ratio of tax payments on factor usage to regional income #
   1783   (all,r,REG)
   1784       100.0 * INCOME(r) * del_taxrfu(r) + TFU(r) * y(r)
   1785           = sum(i,ENDWM_COMM, sum(j,PROD_COMM,
   1786               VFA(i,j,r) * tf(i,j,r) + ETAX(i,j,r) * [pm(i,r) + qfe(i,j,r)]))
   1787           + sum(i,ENDWS_COMM, sum(j,PROD_COMM,
   1788               VFA(i,j,r) * tf(i,j,r) + ETAX(i,j,r) * [pmes(i,j,r) + qfe(i,j,r)]));
   1789    
   1790   Coefficient (parameter)(all,j,PROD_COMM)
   1791       ESUBVA(j)
   1792       # elst. of sub. capital/labor/land, in production of value added in j #;
   1793   Read
   1794       ESUBVA from file GTAPPARM header "ESBV";
   1795    
   1796   Equation ENDWDEMAND
   1797   # demands for endowment commodities (HT 34) #
   1798   (all,i,ENDW_COMM)(all,j,PROD_COMM)(all,r,REG)
   1799       qfe(i,j,r)
   1800           = [- afe(i,j,r) + qva(j,r)
   1801           - ESUBVA(j) * [pfe(i,j,r) - afe(i,j,r) - pva(j,r)]];
   1802    
   1803    
   1804   !<
   1805       3-4. Zero Profits Equations
   1806       ---------------------------
   1807   >!
   1808    
   1809   Equation OUTPUTPRICES
   1810   # eq'n links pre- and post-tax supply prices for all industries  (HT 15) #
   1811   (all,i,PROD_COMM)(all,r,REG)
   1812       ps(i,r) = to(i,r) + pm(i,r);
   1813   !<
   1814       This equation links pre- and post-tax supply prices for all industries.
   1815       This captures the effect of output taxes.  TO(i,r) < 1 in the case of a
   1816       tax.  (HT 15)
   1817   >!
   1818    
   1819   Equation TOUTRATIO
   1820   # change in ratio of output tax payments to regional income #
   1821   (all,r,REG)
   1822       100.0 * INCOME(r) * del_taxrout(r) + TOUT(r) * y(r)
   1823           = sum(i,PROD_COMM,
   1824               VOA(i,r) * [-to(i,r)] + PTAX(i,r) * [pm(i,r) + qo(i,r)]);
   1825    
   1826   Variable (all,j,PROD_COMM)(all,r,REG)
   1827       profitslack(j,r) # slack variable in the zero profit equation #;
   1828   !<
   1829       This is exogenous, unless the user wishes to specify output in a given
   1830       region exogenously.
   1831   >!
   1832   Zerodivide (zero_by_zero) default 0;
   1833    
   1834   Coefficient (all,i,DEMD_COMM)(all,j,PROD_COMM)(all,r,REG)
   1835       STC(i,j,r) # share of i in total costs of j in r #;
   1836   Formula (all,i,DEMD_COMM)(all,j,PROD_COMM)(all,r,REG)
   1837       STC(i,j,r) = VFA(i,j,r) / sum(k,DEMD_COMM, VFA(k,j,r));
   1838    
   1839   Zerodivide (zero_by_zero) off ;
   1840    
   1841   Equation ZEROPROFITS
   1842   # industry zero pure profits condition (HT 6) #
   1843   (all,j,PROD_COMM)(all,r,REG)
   1844       ps(j,r) + ao(j,r)
   1845           = sum(i,ENDW_COMM, STC(i,j,r) * [pfe(i,j,r) - afe(i,j,r) - ava(j,r)])
   1846           + sum(i,TRAD_COMM, STC(i,j,r) * [pf(i,j,r)  - af(i,j,r)])
   1847           + profitslack(j,r);
   1848    
   1849   !<
   1850       Industry zero pure profits condition (HT 6).  This condition permits us to
   1851       determine the endogenous output level for each of the non-endowment
   1852       sectors, excepting when profitslack is itself endogenous.  The level of
   1853       activity in the endowment sectors is exogenously determined.
   1854   >!
   1855    
   1856    
   1857   !<
   1858       ---------------------------------------
   1859       4. Investment, Global Bank, and Savings
   1860       ---------------------------------------
   1861    
   1862       Capital stock and rate of return equations follow.  They correspond to the
   1863       Investment Equations of Table 8 in Hertel and Tsigas.
   1864    
   1865       4-0. Module-Specific Variables
   1866       4-1. Equations of Notational Convenience
   1867       4-2. Rate of Return Equations
   1868       4-3. Capital Accumulation
   1869       4-4. Global Bank
   1870       4-5. Price Index of Aggregate Global Composite Capital Goods
   1871       4-6. Price of Saving
   1872   >!
   1873    
   1874    
   1875   !<
   1876       4-0. Module-Specific Variables
   1877       ------------------------------
   1878    
   1879       only used in this Investment, Global Bank and Savings module
   1880   >!
   1881    
   1882   Variable (all,r,REG)
   1883       rental(r) # rental rate on capital = ps("capital",r) #;
   1884   Variable (all,r,REG)
   1885       ke(r) # end-of-period capital stock in r #;
   1886   Variable (all,r,REG)
   1887       rore(r) # expected net rate of return on capital stock in r #;
   1888   Variable (all,r,REG)
   1889       rorc(r) # current net rate of return on capital stock in r #;
   1890   Variable (all,r,REG)
   1891       qcgds(r) # output of capital goods sector = qo("cgds",r) #;
   1892    
   1893    
   1894   !<
   1895       4-1. Equations of Notational Convenience
   1896       ----------------------------------------
   1897   >!
   1898    
   1899   Coefficient (all,h,HHLD) (all,r,REG)
   1900       CAPEVOA(h,r) ;
   1901   Formula (all,h,HHLD) (all,r,REG)
   1902       CAPEVOA(h,r) = sum(k, ENDWC_COMM, EVOAH(k,h,r));
   1903    
   1904   Coefficient (all,i,ENDWC_COMM) (all,h,HHLD) (all,r,REG)
   1905       SHRCAP(i,h,r) #Share of capital i in total capital in hhld h in region r#;
   1906   Formula (all,i,ENDWC_COMM) (all,h,HHLD) (all,r,REG)
   1907       SHRCAP(i,h,r) = sum(l, HHLD, EVOAH(i,l,r))/sum(k, ENDWC_COMM,
   1908                    sum(f, HHLD, EVOAH(k,f,r))) ;
   1909   Formula (all,i,ENDWC_COMM) (all,h,HHLD) (all,r,REG: CAPEVOA(h,r)>0)
   1910       SHRCAP(i,h,r) = EVOAH(i,h,r)/CAPEVOA(h,r) ;
   1911    
   1912   Variable (all,r,REG)(all,h,HHLD)
   1913       ksvces(h,r) # capital services = qo("capital",r) #;
   1914   Equation KAPSVCES
   1915   # eq'n defines a variable for capital services (HT 52) #
   1916   (all,r,REG)(all,h,HHLD)
   1917       ksvces(h,r)
   1918           = sum(c,ENDWC_COMM, SHRCAP(c,h,r) * qoh(c,h,r));
   1919   !<
   1920       This equation defines a variable for capital services, for convenience.
   1921       (There is really only one capital services item.) (HT 52)
   1922   >!
   1923    
   1924   Equation KAPRENTAL
   1925   # eq'n defines a variable for capital rental rate (HT 53) #
   1926   (all,r,REG)
   1927       rental(r)
   1928           = sum(h,ENDWC_COMM, [VOA(h,r) / sum(k,ENDWC_COMM, VOA(k,r))] * ps(h,r));
   1929    
   1930   Equation CAPGOODS
   1931   # eq'n defines a variable for gross investment (HT 54) #
   1932   (all,r,REG)
   1933       qcgds(r)
   1934           = sum(h,CGDS_COMM, [VOA(h,r) / REGINV(r)] * qo(h,r));
   1935   !<
   1936       This equation defines a variable for gross investment, for convenience.
   1937       There is really only one capital goods item.
   1938   >!
   1939    
   1940   Equation PRCGOODS
   1941   # eq'n defines the price of cgds (HT 55) #
   1942   (all,r,REG)
   1943       pcgds(r) = sum(h,CGDS_COMM, [VOA(h,r) / REGINV(r)] * ps(h,r));
   1944    
   1945   Equation KBEGINNING
   1946   # associates change in cap. services w/ change in cap. stock (HT 56) #
   1947   (all,r,REG)(all,h,HHLD)
   1948       kbh(h,r) = ksvces(h,r);
   1949   !Pete, not sure this is important but note that households own the capital, but
   1950   government also saves, but don't own capital.  I doubt this will cause concern
   1951   since really this saving is borrowing/repaying from households who own the
   1952   capital. !
   1953    
   1954   !<
   1955       This equation associates any change in capital services during the period
   1956       with a change in capital stock.  Full capacity utilization is assumed.
   1957   >!
   1958    
   1959   Coefficient (ge 0)(all,h,HHLD)(all,r,REG)
   1960       VKBH(h,r) # value of beginning-of-period capital stock in r owed by h #;
   1961   Update (all,h,HHLD)(all,r,REG)
   1962       VKBH(h,r) = pcgds(r) * kbh(h,r);
   1963   Read
   1964       VKBH from file GTAPDATA header "VKB";
   1965    
   1966   Coefficient (all,r,REG)
   1967       VKB(r) # private consumption expenditure on domestic i in r #;
   1968   Formula (all,r,REG)
   1969       VKB(r) = sum(h, HHLD, VKBH(h,r));
   1970    
   1971   Equation E_kb (all,r,REG)
   1972       VKB(r) * kb(r) = sum(h, HHLD, VKBH(h,r) * kbh(h,r));
   1973    
   1974   !<
   1975       VKB(r) is used only in this sub-module, so its data are read here.  The
   1976       associated variables, pcgds(r) and kb(r), are used across modules, so they
   1977       have been defined as common variables.
   1978   >!
   1979    
   1980   Coefficient (all,r,REG)
   1981       INVKERATIO(r)
   1982       # ratio of gross investment to end-of-period capital stock in r #;
   1983   Formula (all,r,REG)
   1984       INVKERATIO(r) = REGINV(r) / [VKB(r) + NETINV(r)];
   1985    
   1986   Equation KEND
   1987   # Ending capital stock equals beginning stock plus net investment.  (HT 10) #
   1988   (all,r,REG)
   1989       ke(r) = INVKERATIO(r) * qcgds(r) + [1.0 - INVKERATIO(r)] * kb(r);
   1990    
   1991    
   1992   !<
   1993       4-2. Rate of Return Equations
   1994       -----------------------------
   1995   >!
   1996    
   1997   Coefficient (all,r,REG)
   1998       GRNETRATIO(r) # ratio of GROSS/NET rates of return on capital in r #;
   1999   Formula (all,r,REG)
   2000       GRNETRATIO(r)
   2001           = sum(h,ENDWC_COMM, VOA(h,r))
   2002           / [sum(h,ENDWC_COMM, VOA(h,r)) - VDEP(r)];
   2003   !<
   2004       NOTE: VOA("capital",r) is GROSS returns to capital.
   2005   >!
   2006   Equation RORCURRENT
   2007   # current rate of return on capital in region r (HT 57) #
   2008   (all,r,REG)
   2009       rorc(r) = GRNETRATIO(r) * [rental(r) - pcgds(r)];
   2010    
   2011   Coefficient (parameter)(all,r,REG)
   2012       RORFLEX(r)
   2013       # flexibility of expected net ROR on capital stock in r wrt investment #;
   2014   Read
   2015       RORFLEX from file GTAPPARM header "RFLX";
   2016   !<
   2017       RORFLEX is the flexibility of the expected net rate of return on the
   2018       capital stock, in region r, with respect to investment.  If a region's
   2019       capital stock increases by 1%, then it is expected that the net rate of
   2020       return on capital will decline by RORFLEX %.  A larger absolute value for
   2021       this parameter will reduce the tendency of international investment flows
   2022       to respond to changes in expected rates of return.
   2023   >!
   2024    
   2025   Equation ROREXPECTED
   2026   # expected rate of return depends on the current return and investment (HT 58) #
   2027   (all,r,REG)
   2028       rore(r) = rorc(r) - RORFLEX(r) * [ke(r) - kb(r)];
   2029    
   2030    
   2031   !<
   2032       4-3. Capital Accumulation
   2033       -------------------------
   2034    
   2035       based on the theory laid out in GTAP Technical Paper #7
   2036   >!
   2037    
   2038   Variable (all,i,ENDWC_COMM)(all,h,HHLD)(all,r,REG)
   2039       EXPAND(i,h,r) # change in investment levels relative to endowment stock #;
   2040   Equation BALDWIN
   2041   # change in investment levels relative to endowment stock #
   2042   (all,i,ENDWC_COMM)(all,r,REG)(all,h,HHLD)
   2043       EXPAND(i,h,r) = qcgds(r) - qoh_s(i,h,r);
   2044    
   2045    
   2046   !<
   2047       4-4. Global Bank
   2048       ----------------
   2049   >!
   2050    
   2051   Coefficient (integer,parameter)
   2052       RORDELTA
   2053       # binary coefficient to switch mechanism of allocating investment funds #;
   2054   Read
   2055       RORDELTA from file GTAPPARM header "RDLT";
   2056   !<
   2057       RORDELTA is a binary coefficient which determines the mechanism of
   2058       allocating investment funds across regions.  When RORDELTA = 1, investment
   2059       funds are allocated across regions to equate the change in the expected
   2060       rates of return (i.e., rore(r)).  When RORDELTA = 0, investment funds are
   2061       allocated across regions to maintain the existing composition of capital
   2062       stocks.
   2063   >!
   2064    
   2065   Variable
   2066       rorg # global net rate of return on capital stock #;
   2067   Variable (all,r,REG)
   2068       cgdslack(r) # slack variable for qcgds(r) #;
   2069   !<
   2070       This is exogenous, unless the user wishes to exogenously fix the level of
   2071       gross investment in a region, in which case it can be swapped with
   2072       cgdslack.
   2073   >!
   2074   Equation RORGLOBAL
   2075   # either gross investment or expected rate of return in region r (HT 59) #
   2076   (all,r,REG)
   2077       RORDELTA * [rore(r)]
   2078       + [1 - RORDELTA]
   2079       * [[REGINV(r) / NETINV(r)] * qcgds(r) - [VDEP(r) / NETINV(r)] * kb(r)]
   2080           = RORDELTA * rorg + [1 - RORDELTA] * globalcgds + cgdslack(r);
   2081   !<
   2082       This equation determines either gross investment or the expected rate of
   2083       return in each region, depending on the setting for the binary RORDELTA
   2084       parameter.
   2085   >!
   2086    
   2087   Equation GLOBALINV
   2088   # either expected global rate of return or global net investment (HT 11) #
   2089       RORDELTA * globalcgds + [1 - RORDELTA] * rorg
   2090           = RORDELTA
   2091           * sum(r,REG,
   2092               [REGINV(r) / GLOBINV] * qcgds(r) - [VDEP(r) / GLOBINV] * kb(r))
   2093           + [1 - RORDELTA] * sum(r,REG, [NETINV(r) / GLOBINV] * rore(r));
   2094   !<
   2095       This equation computes either the change in global net investment (when
   2096       RORDELTA = 1), or the change in the expected global rate of return on
   2097       capital (when RORDELTA = 0).
   2098   >!
   2099    
   2100    
   2101   !<
   2102       4-5. Price Index of Aggregate Global Composite Capital Goods
   2103       ------------------------------------------------------------
   2104   >!
   2105    
   2106   Equation PRICGDS
   2107   # eq'n generates a price index for the aggregate global cgds composite (HT 60) #
   2108       pcgdswld = sum(r,REG, [NETINV(r) / GLOBINV] * pcgds(r));
   2109    
   2110    
   2111   !<
   2112       4-6. Price of Saving
   2113       --------------------
   2114   >!
   2115    
   2116   Variable (all,r,REG)
   2117       psaveslack(r) # slack variable for the savings price equation #;
   2118   !<
   2119       This is exogenous under the normal closure.  However, in order to
   2120       replicate simulations from the GTAP book, where there was a single savings
   2121       price, psaveslack may be swapped with psave in order to fix the latter.
   2122       In this case, pcgdswld must be the numeraire so that each region faces the
   2123       same price of savings.
   2124   >!
   2125    
   2126   Equation SAVEPRICE
   2127   # savings price #
   2128   (all,r,REG)
   2129       psave(r)
   2130           = pcgds(r)
   2131           + sum(s,REG, [[NETINV(s) - SAVE(s)] / GLOBINV] * pcgds(s))
   2132           + psaveslack(r);
   2133    
   2134   !<
   2135       In contrast to the GTAP book, the price of savings is now region-specific
   2136       and it changes at the same rate as the price of regional investment, plus
   2137       an adjustment factor which accounts for the fact that savings and
   2138       investment are not equal at the regional level.
   2139   >!
   2140    
   2141   !<
   2142       ----------------------
   2143       5. International Trade
   2144       ----------------------
   2145    
   2146       5-1. Export Prices
   2147       5-2. Demand for Imports
   2148   >!
   2149    
   2150    
   2151   !<
   2152       5-1. Export Prices
   2153       ------------------
   2154   >!
   2155    
   2156   Variable (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,r,REG)
   2157       tx(i,r) # dest.-gen. change in subsidy on exports of i from r #;
   2158   Variable (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,r,REG)(all,s,REG)
   2159       txs(i,r,s) # dest.-spec. change in subsidy on exports of i from r to s #;
   2160   !<
   2161       The variable txs captures changes in the power of bilateral export taxes.
   2162       However, the presence of a destination-generic export subsidy shift (tx)
   2163       also permits the user to swap a single export tax shock with another
   2164       target variable.  It is most naturally swapped with the variable qo to
   2165       insulate domestic producers from the world market.
   2166   >!
   2167    
   2168   Equation EXPRICES
   2169   # eq'n links agent's and world prices (HT 27) #
   2170   (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,r,REG)(all,s,REG)
   2171       pfob(i,r,s) = pm(i,r) - tx(i,r) - txs(i,r,s);
   2172    
   2173   Equation TEXPRATIO
   2174   # change in ratio of export tax payments to regional income #
   2175   (all,r,REG)
   2176       100.0 * INCOME(r) * del_taxrexp(r) + TEX(r) * y(r)
   2177           = sum(i,TRAD_COMM, sum(s,REG,
   2178               VXMD(i,r,s) * [-tx(i,r) - txs(i,r,s)]
   2179               + XTAXD(i,r,s) * [pfob(i,r,s) + qxs(i,r,s)]));
   2180    
   2181    
   2182   !<
   2183       5-2. Demand for Imports
   2184       -----------------------
   2185    
   2186       Composite Imports Nest: Table 3 of Hertel and Tsigas
   2187   >!
   2188    
   2189   Variable (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,s,REG)
   2190       tm(i,s) # source-gen. change in tax on imports of i into s #;
   2191   Variable (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,r,REG)(all,s,REG)
   2192       tms(i,r,s) # source-spec. change in tax on imports of i from r into s #;
   2193   !<
   2194       The variable tms captures changes in the power of bilateral import taxes.
   2195       However, the presence of a source-generic import tariff shift (tm) also
   2196       permits the user to swap a single import tariff shock with another target
   2197       variable.  In particular, to insulate domestic producers from import price
   2198       changes, it may be swapped with the relative price variable pr -- see
   2199       below.
   2200   >!
   2201    
   2202   Equation MKTPRICES
   2203   # eq'n links domestic and world prices (HT 24) #
   2204   (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,r,REG)(all,s,REG)
   2205       pms(i,r,s) = tm(i,s) + tms(i,r,s) + pcif(i,r,s);
   2206    
   2207   Coefficient (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,r,REG)(all,s,REG)
   2208       MSHRS(i,r,s) # share of imports from r in import bill of s at mkt prices #;
   2209   Formula (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,r,REG)(all,s,REG)
   2210       MSHRS(i,r,s) = VIMS(i,r,s) / sum(k,REG, VIMS(i,k,s));
   2211   Equation DPRICEIMP
   2212   # price for aggregate imports (HT 28) #
   2213   (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,s,REG)
   2214       pim(i,s) = sum(k,REG, MSHRS(i,k,s) * [pms(i,k,s) - ams(i,k,s)]);
   2215    
   2216   Variable (orig_level=1.0)(all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,r,REG)
   2217       pr(i,r) # ratio of domestic to imported prices in r #;
   2218   Equation PRICETGT
   2219   # eq'n defines target price ratio to be attained via the variable levy (HT 25) #
   2220   (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,s,REG)
   2221       pr(i,s) = pm(i,s) - pim(i,s);
   2222   !<
   2223       This equation defines the target price ratio to be attained via the
   2224       variable levy.  This price ratio is the ratio of domestic to average
   2225       imported goods' price.  Note that the way this price ratio is defined, it
   2226       includes intraregional imports as well.  In most applications, regions
   2227       will represent groups of individual countries.  However, in the case of
   2228       the EU, this is problematic, since recent versions of the database have
   2229       incorporated intra-EU trade flows.  Therefore, when aggregated to the EU
   2230       level, the composite import price includes both intra-EU and outside
   2231       imports.  So some modification is needed to handle the EU case.
   2232   >!
   2233    
   2234   Coefficient (parameter)(all,i,TRAD_COMM)
   2235       ESUBM(i)
   2236       # region-generic el. of sub. among imports of i in Armington structure #;
   2237   Read
   2238       ESUBM from file GTAPPARM header "ESBM";
   2239    
   2240   Coefficient (parameter)(all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,r,REG)
   2241       ESUBMR(i,r)
   2242       # region-specific el. of sub. among imports of i in Armington structure #;
   2243   Formula (initial)(all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,r,REG)
   2244       ESUBMR(i,r) = ESUBM(i) ;
   2245   Read (ifheaderexists)
   2246       ESUBMR from file GTAPPARM header "ESMR";
   2247    
   2248   Equation IMPORTDEMAND
   2249   # regional demand for disaggregated imported commodities by source (HT 29)  #
   2250   (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,r,REG)(all,s,REG)
   2251       qxs(i,r,s)
   2252           = -ams(i,r,s) + qim(i,s)
   2253           - ESUBMR(i,s) * [pms(i,r,s) - ams(i,r,s) - pim(i,s)];
   2254    
   2255   Equation TIMPRATIO
   2256   # change in ratio of import tax payments to regional income #
   2257   (all,r,REG)
   2258       100.0 * INCOME(r) * del_taxrimp(r) + TIM(r) * y(r)
   2259           = sum(i,TRAD_COMM, sum(s,REG,
   2260               VIMS(i,s,r) * [tm(i,r) + tms(i,s,r)]
   2261               + MTAX(i,s,r) * [pcif(i,s,r) + qxs(i,s,r)]));
   2262    
   2263    
   2264   !<
   2265       -----------------------------------
   2266       6. International Transport Services
   2267       -----------------------------------
   2268    
   2269       6-0. Module-Specific Variables and Coefficients
   2270       6-1. Demand for Global Transport Services
   2271       6-2. Supply of Transport Services
   2272   >!
   2273    
   2274    
   2275   !<
   2276       6-0. Module-Specific Variables and Coefficients
   2277       -----------------------------------------------
   2278    
   2279       only used in this International Transport Services module
   2280   >!
   2281    
   2282   Variable (all,m,MARG_COMM)(all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,r,REG)(all,s,REG)
   2283       qtmfsd(m,i,r,s) # international usage margin m on i from r to s #;
   2284   !<
   2285       International margin usage, by Margin, Freight, Source, and Destination,
   2286       i.e., the percent change in usage of m in transport of i from r to s.
   2287   >!
   2288   Variable (all,m,MARG_COMM)(all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,r,REG)(all,s,REG)
   2289       atmfsd(m,i,r,s) # tech change in m's shipping of i from region r to s #;
   2290   !<
   2291       Technical progress in shipping by Margin, Freight, Source, and
   2292       Destination.  This is endogenous and driven by the following mode-,
   2293       product-, source-, and destination-specific determinants.
   2294   >!
   2295   Variable (all,m,TRAD_COMM)
   2296       atm(m) # tech change in mode m, worldwide #;
   2297   Variable (all,i,TRAD_COMM)
   2298       atf(i) # tech change shipping of i, worldwide #;
   2299   Variable (all,r,REG)
   2300       ats(r) # tech change shipping from region r #;
   2301   Variable (all,s,REG)
   2302       atd(s) # tech change shipping to s #;
   2303   Variable (all,m,MARG_COMM)(all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,r,REG)(all,s,REG)
   2304       atall(m,i,r,s) # tech change in m's shipping of i from region r to s #;
   2305   Variable (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,r,REG)(all,s,REG)
   2306       ptrans(i,r,s) # cost index for international transport of i from r to s #;
   2307   !<
   2308       average cost index for margin services used in getting i from r to s
   2309   >!
   2310   Variable (all,m,MARG_COMM)
   2311       qtm(m) # global margin usage #;
   2312   Variable (all,m,MARG_COMM)
   2313       pt(m) # price of composite margins services, type #;
   2314   !<
   2315       price index for commodity m in margin services usage
   2316   >!
   2317    
   2318   Coefficient (ge 0) (all,m,MARG_COMM)(all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,r,REG)(all,s,REG)
   2319       VTMFSD(m,i,r,s)
   2320       # int'l margin usage, by margin, freight, source, and destination #;
   2321   Update (all,m,MARG_COMM)(all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,r,REG)(all,s,REG)
   2322       VTMFSD(m,i,r,s) = pt(m) * qtmfsd(m,i,r,s);
   2323   Read
   2324       VTMFSD from file GTAPDATA header "VTWR";
   2325    
   2326   Coefficient (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,r,REG)(all,s,REG)
   2327       VTFSD(i,r,s) # aggregate value of svces in the shipment of i from r to s #;
   2328   Formula (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,r,REG)(all,s,REG)
   2329       VTFSD(i,r,s) = sum(m,MARG_COMM, VTMFSD(m,i,r,s));
   2330   !<
   2331       In a balanced data base, (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,r,REG)(all,s,REG),
   2332       VIWS(i,r,s) = VXWD(i,r,s) + VTFSD(i,r,s).
   2333   >!
   2334    
   2335   Coefficient (all,m,MARG_COMM)
   2336       VTMUSE(m) # international margin services usage, by type #;
   2337   Formula (all,m,MARG_COMM)
   2338       VTMUSE(m) = sum(i,TRAD_COMM, sum(r,REG, sum(s,REG, VTMFSD(m,i,r,s))));
   2339    
   2340   Coefficient (all,m,MARG_COMM)
   2341       VTMPROV(m) # international margin services provision #;
   2342   Formula (all,m,MARG_COMM)
   2343       VTMPROV(m) = sum(r,REG, VST(m,r));
   2344   !<
   2345       In a balanced data base, VTMPROV = VTMUSE.
   2346   >!
   2347    
   2348   Coefficient (all,r,REG)
   2349       VTRPROV(r) # international margin supply, by region #;
   2350   Formula (all,r,REG)
   2351       VTRPROV(r) = sum(m,MARG_COMM, VST(m,r));
   2352    
   2353   Coefficient
   2354       VT # international margin supply #;
   2355   Formula
   2356       VT = sum(m,MARG_COMM, sum(r,REG, VST(m,r)));
   2357    
   2358    
   2359   !<
   2360       6-1. Demand for Global Transport Services
   2361       -----------------------------------------
   2362   >!
   2363    
   2364   Equation QTRANS_MFSD
   2365   # bilateral demand for transport services  #
   2366   (all,m,MARG_COMM)(all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,r,REG)(all,s,REG)
   2367       qtmfsd(m,i,r,s) = qxs(i,r,s) - atmfsd(m,i,r,s);
   2368   !<
   2369       This equation computes the bilateral demand for international
   2370       transportation services.  It reflects the fact that the demand for
   2371       services along any particular route is proportional to the quantity of
   2372       merchandise shipped [i.e., QXS(i,r,s)].  It is here that we introduce the
   2373       potential for input-augmenting tech change, atmfsd(m,i,r,s), which is
   2374       commodity- and route-specific.  Thus, in the levels:
   2375               ATMFSD(m,i,r,s) * QTMFSD(m,i,r,s) = QXS(i,r,s)
   2376       where QTMFSD is the amount of composite margins services m used along this
   2377       route.  Technological improvements are reflected by atmfsd(i,r,s) > 0, and
   2378       these reduce the margins services required for this i,r,s triplet.  Tech.
   2379       change also dampens the cost of shipping, thereby lowering the CIF price
   2380       implied by a given FOB value (see 6-2).
   2381   >!
   2382    
   2383   Coefficient (all,m,MARG_COMM)(all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,r,REG)(all,s,REG)
   2384       VTMUSESHR(m,i,r,s) # share of i,r,s usage in global demand for m #;
   2385   Formula (all,m,MARG_COMM)(all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,r,REG)(all,s,REG)
   2386       VTMUSESHR(m,i,r,s) = VTFSD(i,r,s) / VT;
   2387   Formula
   2388       (all,m,MARG_COMM: VTMUSE(m) <> 0.0)(all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,r,REG)(all,s,REG)
   2389       VTMUSESHR(m,i,r,s) = VTMFSD(m,i,r,s) / VTMUSE(m);
   2390    
   2391   Equation TRANS_DEMAND
   2392   # global demand for margin m #
   2393   (all,m,MARG_COMM)
   2394       qtm(m)
   2395           = sum(i,TRAD_COMM, sum(r,REG, sum(s,REG,
   2396             VTMUSESHR(m,i,r,s) * qtmfsd(m,i,r,s))));
   2397    
   2398    
   2399   !<
   2400       6-2. Supply of Transport Services
   2401       ---------------------------------
   2402   >!
   2403    
   2404   Coefficient (all,m,MARG_COMM)(all,r,REG)
   2405       VTSUPPSHR(m,r) # share of region r in global supply of margin m #;
   2406   Formula (all,m,MARG_COMM)(all,r,REG)
   2407       VTSUPPSHR(m,r) = VTRPROV(r) / VT;
   2408   Formula (all,m,MARG_COMM: VTMPROV(m) <> 0.0)(all,r,REG)
   2409       VTSUPPSHR(m,r) = VST(m,r) / VTMPROV(m);
   2410    
   2411   Equation PTRANSPORT
   2412   # generate price index for composite transportation services #
   2413   (all,m,MARG_COMM)
   2414       pt(m) = sum(r,REG, VTSUPPSHR(m,r) * pm(m,r));
   2415   !<
   2416       This equation generates a price index for transportation services based on
   2417       zero profits.  NOTE:
   2418       (1) Sales to international transportation are not subject to export tax.
   2419           This is why we base the costs to the transport sector on market prices
   2420           of the goods sold to international transportation.
   2421       (2) We assume that the supply shares for margin services are uniform
   2422           across freight, source of freight, and destination.
   2423       (cf. HT#7)
   2424   >!
   2425    
   2426   Coefficient
   2427       VTUSE # international margin services usage #;
   2428   Formula
   2429       VTUSE
   2430           = sum(m,MARG_COMM, sum(i,TRAD_COMM, sum(r,REG, sum(s,REG,
   2431               VTMFSD(m,i,r,s)))));
   2432    
   2433   Coefficient (all,m,MARG_COMM)(all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,r,REG)(all,s,REG)
   2434       VTFSD_MSH(m,i,r,s) # share of margin m in cost of getting i from r to s #;
   2435   Formula (all,m,MARG_COMM)(all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,r,REG)
   2436           (all,s,REG: VTFSD(i,r,s) > 0.0)
   2437       VTFSD_MSH(m,i,r,s) = VTMFSD(m,i,r,s) / VTFSD(i,r,s);
   2438   Formula (all,m,MARG_COMM)(all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,r,REG)
   2439           (all,s,REG: VTFSD(i,r,s) = 0.0)
   2440       VTFSD_MSH(m,i,r,s) = VTMUSE(m) / VTUSE;
   2441    
   2442   Equation TRANSCOSTINDEX
   2443   #  generates flow-specific modal average cost of transport index (cf. HT7) #
   2444   (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,r,REG)(all,s,REG)
   2445       ptrans(i,r,s)
   2446           = sum(m,MARG_COMM, VTFSD_MSH(m,i,r,s) * [pt(m) - atmfsd(m,i,r,s)]);
   2447    
   2448   Equation TRANSTECHANGE
   2449   #  generates flow-specific average rate of technical change #
   2450   (all,m,MARG_COMM)(all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,r,REG)(all,s,REG)
   2451       atmfsd(m,i,r,s) = atm(m) + atf(i) + ats(r) + atd(s) + atall(m,i,r,s);
   2452    
   2453   Equation TRANSVCES
   2454   # generate demand for regional supply of global transportation service (HT 61) #
   2455   (all,m,MARG_COMM)(all,r,REG)
   2456       qst(m,r) = qtm(m) + [pt(m) - pm(m,r)];
   2457   !<
   2458       This equation generates the international transport sector's derived
   2459       demand for regional supplies of transportation services.  It reflects a
   2460       unitary elasticity of substitution between transportation services inputs
   2461       from different regions.
   2462   >!
   2463    
   2464   Coefficient (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,r,REG)(all,s,REG)
   2465       VIWSCOST(i,r,s) # value of imports calculated as total cost of imports #;
   2466   Formula (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,r,REG)(all,s,REG)
   2467       VIWSCOST(i,r,s) = VXWD(i,r,s) + VTFSD(i,r,s);
   2468    
   2469   Coefficient (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,r,REG)(all,s,REG)
   2470       FOBSHR(i,r,s) # FOB share in VIW #;
   2471   Formula (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,r,REG)(all,s,REG)
   2472       FOBSHR(i,r,s) = VXWD(i,r,s) / VIWSCOST(i,r,s);
   2473    
   2474   Coefficient (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,r,REG)(all,s,REG)
   2475       TRNSHR(i,r,s) # transport share in VIW #;
   2476   Formula (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,r,REG)(all,s,REG)
   2477       TRNSHR(i,r,s) = VTFSD(i,r,s) / VIWSCOST(i,r,s);
   2478    
   2479   Equation FOBCIF
   2480   # eq'n links FOB and CIF prices for good i shipped from region r to s (HT 26') #
   2481   (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,r,REG)(all,s,REG)
   2482       pcif(i,r,s)
   2483          = FOBSHR(i,r,s) * pfob(i,r,s)
   2484          + TRNSHR(i,r,s) * ptrans(i,r,s);
   2485   !<
   2486       This equation links export and import prices for each commodity/route
   2487       triplet.  Note that technical change is embodied in ptrans(i,r,s) which is
   2488       now a cost index, as opposed to (HT 26') where it represented the price of
   2489       margins services.
   2490   >!
   2491    
   2492    
   2493   !<
   2494       ---------------------
   2495       7. Regional Household
   2496       ---------------------
   2497    
   2498       7-0. Module-Specific Coefficients
   2499       7-1. Supply of Endowments by the Regional Household
   2500       7-2. Computation of Regional Income
   2501       7-3. Regional Household Demand System
   2502       7-4. Aggregate Utility
   2503   >!
   2504    
   2505    
   2506   !<
   2507       7-0. Module-Specific Coefficients
   2508       ---------------------------------
   2509    
   2510       only used in this Regional Household module
   2511   >!
   2512    
   2513   Coefficient (all,r,REG)(all,h,HHLD)
   2514       XSHRPRIVH(h,r) # private expenditure share in household income #;
   2515   Formula (all,r,REG)(all,h,HHLD)
   2516       XSHRPRIVH(h,r) = sum(k, HHLD, PRIVEXPH(k,r)) / sum(k, HHLD, HHLDINC(k,r));
   2517   Formula (all,r,REG)(all,h,HHLD: HHLDINC(h,r)>0)
   2518       XSHRPRIVH(h,r) = PRIVEXPH(h,r) / HHLDINC(h,r);
   2519    
   2520   Coefficient (all,r,REG)(all,h,HHLD)
   2521       XSHRSAVH(h,r) # saving share in household income #;
   2522   Formula (all,r,REG)(all,h,HHLD)
   2523       XSHRSAVH(h,r) = sum(k, HHLD, SAV_HHLD(k,r)) / sum(k, HHLD, HHLDINC(k,r));
   2524   Formula (all,r,REG)(all,h,HHLD:HHLDINC(h,r)>0)
   2525       XSHRSAVH(h,r) = SAV_HHLD(h,r) / HHLDINC(h,r);
   2526    
   2527   Coefficient (all,r,REG)(all,h,HHLD)
   2528       DUMSAVH(h,r) # Dummy on savings by household #;
   2529   Formula (all,r,REG)(all,h,HHLD)
   2530       DUMSAVH(h,r) = 0 ;
   2531   Formula (all,r,REG)(all,h,HHLD:SAV_HHLD(h,r)>0)
   2532       DUMSAVH(h,r) = 1 ;
   2533    
   2534   Coefficient (all,r,REG)
   2535       XSHRGOV(r) # government expenditure share in government income #;
   2536   Formula (all,r,REG)
   2537       XSHRGOV(r) = GOVEXP(r) / GOVINC(r);
   2538    
   2539   Coefficient (all,r,REG)
   2540       XSHRSAVG(r) # saving share in government income #;
   2541   Formula (all,r,REG)
   2542       XSHRSAVG(r) = SAV_GOV(r) / GOVINC(r);
   2543    
   2544   Variable (all,r,REG)(all,h,HHLD)
   2545       uelash(h,r) # elasticity of cost of utility wrt utility for hhld h#;
   2546    
   2547    
   2548   !<
   2549       7-1. Supply of Endowments by the Regional Household
   2550       ---------------------------------------------------
   2551   >!
   2552    
   2553   Equation FACTORINCPRICES
   2554   # eq'n links pre- and post-tax endowment supply prices by hhld h(HT 15) #
   2555   (all,i,ENDW_COMM)(all,r,REG)(all,h,HHLD)
   2556       psh(i,h,r) = to(i,r) + toh(i,h,r) + pm(i,r);
   2557    
   2558   coefficient (all,i,ENDW_COMM) (all,h,HHLD)(all,r,REG)
   2559       SHREVOAH(i,h,r);
   2560   Formula (all,i,ENDW_COMM)(all,h,HHLD)(all,r,REG)
   2561       SHREVOAH(i,h,r) = sum(k, ENDW_COMM: MAPENDW(k)=MAPENDW(i), EVOAH(k,h,r))
   2562             /sum(k, HHLD, sum(l, ENDW_COMM: MAPENDW(l)=MAPENDW(i), EVOAH(l,k,r)));
   2563   Formula (all,i,ENDW_COMM)(all,h,HHLD)(all,r,REG: VOA(i,r)>0)
   2564       SHREVOAH(i,h,r) = EVOAH(i,h,r)/sum(k, HHLD, EVOAH(i,k,r));
   2565    
   2566   Equation E_ps
   2567   # Average supply price of endowments (HT 15) #
   2568   (all,i,ENDW_COMM)(all,r,REG)
   2569       ps(i,r)
   2570               = sum(h, HHLD, SHREVOAH(i,h,r) * psh(i,h,r));
   2571    
   2572   coefficient (all,i,ENDW_COMM) (all,h,HHLD)(all,r,REG)
   2573       SHREVOMH(i,h,r) #share of household h in value of endowment i in r#;
   2574   Formula (all,i,ENDW_COMM)(all,h,HHLD)(all,r,REG)
   2575       SHREVOMH(i,h,r) = sum(k, ENDW_COMM: MAPENDW(k)=MAPENDW(i), EVOMH(k,h,r))
   2576           /sum(k, HHLD, sum(l, ENDW_COMM: MAPENDW(l)=MAPENDW(i), EVOMH(l,k,r)));
   2577   Formula (all,i,ENDW_COMM) (all,h,HHLD)(all,r,REG: VOM(i,r) > 0)
   2578       SHREVOMH(i,h,r) = EVOMH(i,h,r)/sum(k, HHLD, EVOMH(i,k,r));
   2579    
   2580   Variable (all,i,ENDW_COMM)(all,h,HHLD)(all,r,REG)
   2581       semplh(i,h,r) # employment of endowment i from household h in region r #;
   2582   Variable (all,i,ENDW_COMM)(all,h,HHLD)(all,r,REG)
   2583       emplh(i,h,r) # shifter on employment of endow i from hhld h in region r #;
   2584   Variable (all,i,ENDW_COMM)(all,r,REG)
   2585       empl(i,r) # shifter on employment of endowment i in region r #;
   2586   Equation E_semplh
   2587   # Employment #
   2588   (all,i,ENDW_COMM)(all,h,HHLD)(all,r,REG)
   2589       semplh(i,h,r) = emplh(i,h,r) + empl(i,r) ;
   2590    
   2591   Equation E_qoh
   2592   # Total supply of endowment i #
   2593   (all,i,ENDW_COMM)(all,h,HHLD)(all,r,REG)
   2594       qoh(i,h,r) = qoh_s(i,h,r) + semplh(i,h,r) ;
   2595    
   2596   Equation E_qo
   2597   # Total supply of endowment i #
   2598   (all,i,ENDW_COMM)(all,r,REG)
   2599       qo(i,r) = sum(h, HHLD, SHREVOMH(i,h,r) * qoh(i,h,r));
   2600    
   2601   Coefficient (all,r,REG)
   2602       TINC(r) # income tax payments in r #;
   2603   Formula (all,r,REG)
   2604       TINC(r) = sum(i,ENDW_COMM, sum(h, HHLD, INCTAX(i,h,r)));
   2605    
   2606   Equation TINCRATIO
   2607   # change in ratio of income tax payments to regional income #
   2608   (all,r,REG)
   2609       100.0 * INCOME(r) * del_taxrinc(r) + TINC(r) * y(r)
   2610           = sum(h, HHLD, sum(i,ENDW_COMM,
   2611               EVOAH(i,h,r) * [-toh(i,h,r)-to(i,r)]
   2612               + INCTAX(i,h,r) * [pm(i,r) + qoh(i,h,r)]));
   2613    
   2614   Coefficient (all,i,ENDW_COMM)(all,j,PROD_COMM)(all,r,REG)
   2615       REVSHR(i,j,r);
   2616   Formula (all,i,ENDW_COMM)(all,j,PROD_COMM)(all,r,REG)
   2617       REVSHR(i,j,r) = sum(k, ENDW_COMM: MAPENDW(k)=MAPENDW(i), VFM(k,j,r))
   2618          / sum(k,PROD_COMM, sum(l, ENDW_COMM: MAPENDW(l)=MAPENDW(i), VFM(l,k,r)));
   2619   Formula (all,i,ENDW_COMM)(all,j,PROD_COMM)(all,r,REG:VOM(i,r)>0)
   2620       REVSHR(i,j,r) = VFM(i,j,r) / sum(k,PROD_COMM, VFM(i,k,r));
   2621    
   2622   Equation ENDW_PRICE
   2623   # eq'n generates the composite price for sluggish endowments (HT 50) #
   2624   (all,i,ENDWS_COMM)(all,r,REG)
   2625       pm(i,r) = sum(k,PROD_COMM, REVSHR(i,k,r) * pmes(i,k,r));
   2626    
   2627   Coefficient (parameter)(all,i,ENDW_COMM)
   2628       ETRAE(i)
   2629       # elst. of transformation for sluggish primary factor endowments #;
   2630   Read
   2631       ETRAE from file GTAPPARM header "ETRE";
   2632   !<
   2633       ETRAE is the elasticity of transformation for sluggish primary factor
   2634       endowments.  It is non-positive, by definition.
   2635   >!
   2636   Equation ENDW_SUPPLY
   2637   # eq'n distributes the sluggish endowments across sectors (HT 51) #
   2638   (all,i,ENDWS_COMM)(all,j,PROD_COMM)(all,r,REG)
   2639       qoes(i,j,r) = qo(i,r) - endwslack(i,r) + ETRAE(i) * [pm(i,r) - pmes(i,j,r)];
   2640    
   2641    
   2642   !<
   2643       7-2. Computation of Regional Income
   2644       -----------------------------------
   2645   >!
   2646    
   2647   Variable (ORIG_LEVEL=HHLDINC)(all,r,REG)(all,h,HHLD)
   2648       hhldincome (h,r)
   2649    # Income of household h in region r net of depreciation #;
   2650    
   2651   !<
   2652       Remitances, Aid, Foreign Income and Transfer
   2653       ---------------------------------------------
   2654   >!
   2655    
   2656   !Remitances!
   2657   Variable (all,h,HHLD) (all,r,REG)
   2658       remih(h,r) #Remittances into household h in region r#;
   2659   Variable (all,h,HHLD) (all,r,REG)
   2660       remoh(h,r) #Remittances out of household h in region r#;
   2661   Variable (all,h,HHLD) (all,r,REG)
   2662       sremoh(h,r) #Shifter to change the rate of remittances out#;
   2663   Variable (all,h,HHLD) (all,r,REG)
   2664       sremih(h,r) #Shifter to change the rate of remittances in#;
   2665   Variable
   2666       remavo #Average rate of remittances out#;
   2667   Variable
   2668       remavi #Average rate of remittances in#;
   2669    
   2670   Coefficient (all,h,HHLD) (all,r,REG)
   2671       REMI(h,r) #value of remittances into hhld h in region r#;
   2672   Read REMI from file GTAPDATA header "REMI";
   2673   Update (all,h,HHLD) (all,r,REG)
   2674       REMI(h,r) = remih(h,r) ;
   2675    
   2676   Coefficient (all,h,HHLD) (all,r,REG)
   2677       REMO(h,r)#value of remittances out of hhld h in region r#;
   2678   Read REMO from file GTAPDATA header "REMO";
   2679   Update (all,h,HHLD) (all,r,REG)
   2680       REMO(h,r) = remoh(h,r) ;
   2681    
   2682   Equation E_remih (all,h,HHLD) (all,r,REG)
   2683       remih(h,r) = remavi + sremih(h,r);
   2684    
   2685   Equation E_remav
   2686       sum(h, HHLD, sum(r, REG, REMI(h,r) * remih(h,r)))
   2687             = sum(h, HHLD, sum(r, REG, REMO(h,r) * remoh(h,r))) ;
   2688    
   2689   Coefficient (all,h,HHLD) (all,r,REG)
   2690       LABEVOA(h,r) ;
   2691   Formula (all,h,HHLD) (all,r,REG)
   2692       LABEVOA(h,r) = sum(k, ENDWL_COMM, EVOAH(k,h,r));
   2693    
   2694   Coefficient (all,i,ENDWL_COMM) (all,h,HHLD) (all,r,REG)
   2695       SHRLAB(i,h,r) #Share of labor i in total labor in household h in region r #;
   2696   Formula (all,i,ENDWL_COMM) (all,h,HHLD) (all,r,REG)
   2697       SHRLAB(i,h,r) = sum(l, HHLD, EVOAH(i,l,r))/sum(k, ENDWL_COMM,
   2698                    sum(f, HHLD, EVOAH(k,f,r))) ;
   2699   Formula (all,i,ENDWL_COMM) (all,h,HHLD) (all,r,REG: LABEVOA(h,r)>0)
   2700       SHRLAB(i,h,r) = EVOAH(i,h,r)/LABEVOA(h,r) ;
   2701    
   2702   Equation E_remoh (all,h,HHLD) (all,r,REG)
   2703       remoh(h,r) = sum(i, ENDWL_COMM, SHRLAB(i,h,r) * [psh(i,h,r) + qoh(i,h,r)])
   2704                     + sremoh(h,r) + remavo ;
   2705    
   2706   !Foreign Income!
   2707   Variable (all,h,HHLD) (all,r,REG)
   2708       fyih(h,r) #Foreign income in household h in region r#;
   2709   Variable (all,h,HHLD) (all,r,REG)
   2710       fyoh(h,r) #Foreign income out household h in region r#;
   2711   Variable (all,h,HHLD) (all,r,REG)
   2712       sfyoh(h,r) #shifter Foreign income out household h in region r#;
   2713   Variable (all,h,HHLD) (all,r,REG)
   2714       sfyih(h,r) #shifter Foreign income in household h in region r#;
   2715   Variable
   2716       fyavo #Average Foreign income out household h in region r#;
   2717   Variable
   2718       fyavi #Average Foreign income into household h in region r#;
   2719    
   2720   Coefficient (all,h,HHLD) (all,r,REG)
   2721       FYI(h,r) #Value of Foreign income in household h in region r#;
   2722   Read FYI from file GTAPDATA header "FYI";
   2723   Update (all,h,HHLD) (all,r,REG)
   2724       FYI(h,r) = fyih(h,r) ;
   2725    
   2726   Coefficient (all,h,HHLD) (all,r,REG)
   2727       FYO(h,r) #Value of Foreign income paid by household h in region r#;
   2728   Read FYO from file GTAPDATA header "FYO";
   2729   Update (all,h,HHLD) (all,r,REG)
   2730       FYO(h,r) = fyoh(h,r) ;
   2731    
   2732   Equation E_fyih (all,h,HHLD) (all,r,REG)
   2733       fyih(h,r) = fyavi + sfyih(h,r)  ;
   2734    
   2735   Equation E_fyav
   2736             sum(h, HHLD, sum(r, REG, FYI(h,r) * fyih(h,r)))
   2737             = sum(h, HHLD, sum(r, REG, FYO(h,r) * fyoh(h,r))) ;
   2738    
   2739   Equation E_fyoh (all,h,HHLD) (all,r,REG)
   2740       fyoh(h,r) = sum(i, ENDWC_COMM, SHRCAP(i,h,r) * [psh(i,h,r) + qoh(i,h,r)])
   2741                   + sfyoh(h,r) + fyavo ;
   2742    
   2743    
   2744   !AID!
   2745   Variable (all,r,REG)
   2746       gincome(r) # Government income in region r#;
   2747   Variable (all,r,REG)
   2748       aidin(r)#Foreign aid in region r#;
   2749   Variable (all,r,REG)
   2750       aidout(r)#Foreign aid out region r#;
   2751   Variable (all,r,REG)
   2752       saidout(r) #shifter on aid out of region r#;
   2753   Variable (all,r,REG)
   2754       saidin(r) #shifter on aid into region r#;
   2755   Variable
   2756       aidavi #Average Foreign aid in#;
   2757   Variable
   2758       aidavo #Average Foreign aid out#;
   2759    
   2760   Coefficient (all,r,REG)
   2761       AIDI(r) #Value of foreign aid flowing into region r# ;
   2762   Read AIDI from file GTAPDATA header "AIDI";
   2763   Update (all,r,REG)
   2764       AIDI(r) = aidin(r) ;
   2765    
   2766   Coefficient (all,r,REG)
   2767       AIDO(r) #Value of foreign aid flowing out of region r# ;
   2768   Read AIDO from file GTAPDATA header "AIDO";
   2769   Update (all,r,REG)
   2770       AIDO(r) = aidout(r) ;
   2771    
   2772   Equation E_aidin (all,r,REG)
   2773       aidin(r) = aidavi + saidin(r);
   2774    
   2775   Equation E_aidout (all,r,REG)
   2776       aidout(r) = gincome(r) + saidout(r) + aidavo ;
   2777    
   2778   Equation E_aidav
   2779             sum(r, REG, AIDI(r) * aidin(r))
   2780             = sum(r, REG, AIDO(r) * aidout(r)) ;
   2781    
   2782   !Transfers - household and government!
   2783   Variable (change) (all,h1,HHLD)(all,h2,HHLD)(all,r,REG)
   2784       realTRNH(h1,h2,r)
   2785   #change in transfers from h1 to h2 in region r rel. to income#;
   2786   Variable (change, levels) (all,h1,HHLD)(all,h2,HHLD)(all,r,REG)
   2787       TRNH(h1,h2,r) #value of transfers from h1 to h2 in region r#;
   2788   Read TRNH from file GTAPDATA header "TRNH";
   2789   Equation E_cTRNH (all,h1,HHLD)(all,h2,HHLD)(all,r,REG)
   2790       c_TRNH(h1,h2,r) = TRNH(h1,h2,r)/100 * hhldincome(h1,r)
   2791                       + realTRNH(h1,h2,r) ;
   2792    
   2793   Variable (change) (all,h,HHLD)(all,r,REG)
   2794       realTRNG(h,r)
   2795   #change in transfers from govt to hhld h rel. to Govt income#;
   2796   Variable (change, levels) (all,h,HHLD)(all,r,REG)
   2797       TRNG(h,r) #value of transfers from government to household h#;
   2798   Read TRNG from file GTAPDATA header "TRNG";
   2799   Equation E_cTRNG (all,h,HHLD)(all,r,REG)
   2800       c_TRNG(h,r) = TRNG(h,r)/100 * gincome(r)
   2801                       + realTRNG(h,r) ;
   2802    
   2803   Coefficient (all,r,REG)
   2804       FY(r) # primary factor income in r net of depreciation #;
   2805   Formula (all,r,REG)
   2806       FY(r) = sum(i,ENDW_COMM, VOM(i,r)) - VDEP(r)
   2807               + sum(h, HHLD, REMI(h,r) - REMO(h,r) + FYI(h,r) - FYO(h,r))
   2808               + AIDI(r) - AIDO(r) ;
   2809   Variable (all,r,REG)
   2810       fincome(r) # factor income at market prices net of depreciation #;
   2811   Equation FACTORINCOME
   2812   # factor income at market prices net of depreciation #
   2813   (all,r,REG)
   2814       FY(r) * fincome(r)
   2815           = sum(i,ENDW_COMM, VOM(i,r) * [pm(i,r) + qo(i,r)])
   2816           - VDEP(r)  * [pcgds(r) + kb(r)]
   2817           + sum(h, HHLD, REMI(h,r) * [remih(h,r)])
   2818           - sum(h, HHLD, REMO(h,r) * [remoh(h,r)])
   2819           + sum(h, HHLD, FYI(h,r) * [fyih(h,r)])
   2820           - sum(h, HHLD, FYO(h,r) * [fyoh(h,r)])
   2821           + AIDI(r) * [aidin(r)]
   2822           - AIDO(r) * [aidout(r)];
   2823    
   2824   Variable (change)(all,r,REG)
   2825       del_indtaxr(r) # change in ratio of indirect taxes to INCOME in r #;
   2826   Equation DINDTAXRATIO
   2827   # change in ratio of indirect taxes to INCOME in r #
   2828   (all,r,REG)
   2829       del_indtaxr(r)
   2830           = del_taxrpc(r) + del_taxrgc(r) + del_taxriu(r) + del_taxrfu(r)
   2831           + del_taxrout(r) + del_taxrexp(r) + del_taxrimp(r);
   2832    
   2833   Variable (change)(all,r,REG)
   2834       del_ttaxr(r) # change in ratio of taxes to INCOME in r #;
   2835   Equation DTAXRATIO
   2836   # change in ratio of taxes to INCOME in r #
   2837   (all,r,REG)
   2838       del_ttaxr(r)
   2839           = del_taxrpc(r) + del_taxrgc(r) + del_taxriu(r) + del_taxrfu(r)
   2840           + del_taxrout(r) + del_taxrexp(r) + del_taxrimp(r) + del_taxrinc(r);
   2841   !<
   2842      This variable can be swapped with the commodity- and source-generic
   2843      consumption tax shift, tp(r), in order to generate a tax replacement
   2844      scenario, whereby taxes remain a constant share of national income.
   2845   >!
   2846    
   2847   Variable (all,r,REG)
   2848       incomeslack(r) # slack variable in the expression for regional income #;
   2849   !<
   2850       This is exogenous, unless the user wishes to fix regional income.
   2851   >!
   2852    
   2853   Coefficient (all,r,REG)
   2854       INDTAX(r) # indirect tax receipts in r #;
   2855   Formula (all,r,REG)
   2856       INDTAX(r) = TPC(r) + TGC(r) + TIU(r) + TFU(r) + TOUT(r) + TEX(r) + TIM(r);
   2857    
   2858   Coefficient (all,r,REG)
   2859       TTAX(r) # tax receipts in r #;
   2860   Formula (all,r,REG)
   2861       TTAX(r) = TPC(r) + TGC(r) + TIU(r) + TFU(r) + TOUT(r) + TEX(r) + TIM(r)
   2862               + TINC(r) ;
   2863    
   2864   Equation REGIONALINCOME
   2865   # regional income = sum of primary factor income and indirect tax receipts #
   2866   (all,r,REG)
   2867       INCOME(r) * y(r)
   2868           = FY(r) * fincome(r)
   2869           + 100.0 * INCOME(r) * del_indtaxr(r)
   2870           + INDTAX(r) * y(r)
   2871           + INCOME(r) * incomeslack(r);
   2872   !<
   2873       This equation computes regional income as the sum of primary factor
   2874       payment and indirect tax receipts.  The first term computes the change in
   2875       endowment income, net of depreciation.  The subsequent terms compute the
   2876       change in indirect tax receipts for various transactions taxes.
   2877   >!
   2878    
   2879   Variable (all,r,REG)
   2880       gincomeslack(r) # slack variable in the expression for government income #;
   2881   Equation E_GINCOME
   2882   # Government income #
   2883   (all,r,REG)
   2884       GOVINC(r) * gincome(r)
   2885           = AIDI(r) * [aidin(r)]
   2886           - AIDO(r) * [aidout(r)]
   2887           + 100.0 * INCOME(r) * del_ttaxr(r)
   2888           + TTAX(r) * y(r)
   2889           - sum(h, HHLD, 100 * c_TRNG(h,r))
   2890           + GOVINC(r) * gincomeslack(r);
   2891    
   2892   Coefficient (all,e,ENDW_COMM)(all,r,REG)(all,h,HHLD)
   2893       SHEVOAY(e,h,r) #Share of endwoments in hhld income# ;
   2894   Formula (all,e,ENDW_COMM)(all,r,REG)(all,h,HHLD)
   2895       SHEVOAY(e,h,r) = sum(k, HHLD, EVOAH(e,k,r))/sum(k, HHLD, HHLDINC(k,r));
   2896   Formula (all,e,ENDW_COMM)(all,r,REG)(all,h,HHLD: HHLDINC(h,r)>0)
   2897       SHEVOAY(e,h,r) = EVOAH(e,h,r)/HHLDINC(h,r);
   2898    
   2899   Coefficient (all,r,REG)(all,h,HHLD)
   2900       SHDEPY(h,r) #Share of depreciation in hhld income# ;
   2901   Formula (all,r,REG)(all,h,HHLD)
   2902       SHDEPY(h,r) = sum(k, HHLD, VDEPH(k,r))/sum(k, HHLD, HHLDINC(k,r));
   2903   Formula (all,r,REG)(all,h,HHLD: HHLDINC(h,r)>0)
   2904       SHDEPY(h,r)= VDEPH(h,r)/HHLDINC(h,r);
   2905    
   2906   Coefficient (all,r,REG)(all,h,HHLD)
   2907       SHREMIY(h,r) #Share of remittances in in hhld income# ;
   2908   Formula (all,r,REG)(all,h,HHLD)
   2909       SHREMIY(h,r) = sum(k, HHLD, REMI(k,r))/sum(k, HHLD, HHLDINC(k,r));
   2910   Formula (all,r,REG)(all,h,HHLD: HHLDINC(h,r)>0)
   2911       SHREMIY(h,r) = REMI(h,r)/HHLDINC(h,r);
   2912    
   2913   Coefficient (all,r,REG)(all,h,HHLD)
   2914       SHREMOY(h,r) #Share of remittances out in hhld income# ;
   2915   Formula (all,r,REG)(all,h,HHLD)
   2916       SHREMOY(h,r) = sum(k, HHLD, REMO(k,r))/sum(k, HHLD, HHLDINC(k,r));
   2917   Formula (all,r,REG)(all,h,HHLD: HHLDINC(h,r)>0)
   2918       SHREMOY(h,r) = REMO(h,r)/HHLDINC(h,r);
   2919    
   2920   Coefficient (all,r,REG)(all,h,HHLD)
   2921       SHFYIY(h,r) #Share of foreign income in hhld income# ;
   2922   Formula (all,r,REG)(all,h,HHLD)
   2923       SHFYIY(h,r) = sum(k, HHLD, FYI(k,r))/sum(k, HHLD, HHLDINC(k,r)) ;
   2924   Formula (all,r,REG)(all,h,HHLD: HHLDINC(h,r)>0)
   2925       SHFYIY(h,r)= FYI(h,r)/HHLDINC(h,r) ;
   2926    
   2927   Coefficient (all,r,REG)(all,h,HHLD)
   2928       SHFYOY(h,r) #Share of foregin income out in hhld income# ;
   2929   Formula (all,r,REG)(all,h,HHLD)
   2930       SHFYOY(h,r) = sum(k, HHLD, FYO(k,r))/sum(k, HHLD, HHLDINC(k,r)) ;
   2931   Formula (all,r,REG)(all,h,HHLD: HHLDINC(h,r)>0)
   2932       SHFYOY(h,r) = FYO(h,r)/HHLDINC(h,r) ;
   2933    
   2934   Coefficient (all,r,REG)(all,h,HHLD)
   2935       HHLDINC00(h,r) #Share of transfers in hhld income# ;
   2936   Formula (all,r,REG)(all,h,HHLD)
   2937       HHLDINC00(h,r) = 0;
   2938   Formula (all,r,REG)(all,h,HHLD: HHLDINC(h,r)>0)
   2939       HHLDINC00(h,r)= 100/HHLDINC(h,r) ;
   2940    
   2941   Variable (all,r,REG)(all,h,HHLD)
   2942       hincomeslack(h,r) # slack variable in the expression for regional income #;
   2943   Equation E_HHLDINCOME
   2944    # Household income of hhld h at market prices net of depreciation #
   2945   (all,r,REG)(all,h,HHLD)
   2946       hhldincome(h,r)
   2947           = sum(i,ENDW_COMM, SHEVOAY(i,h,r) * [psh(i,h,r) + qoh(i,h,r)])
   2948           - SHDEPY(h,r) * [pcgds(r) + kbh(h,r)]
   2949           + SHREMIY(h,r) * [remih(h,r)]
   2950           - SHREMOY(h,r) * [remoh(h,r)]
   2951           + SHFYIY(h,r) * [fyih(h,r)]
   2952           - SHFYOY(h,r) * [fyoh(h,r)]
   2953           + HHLDINC00(h,r) * sum(k, HHLD, c_TRNH(k,h,r))
   2954           - HHLDINC00(h,r) * sum(k, HHLD, c_TRNH(h,k,r))
   2955           + HHLDINC00(h,r) * c_TRNG(h,r)
   2956           + hincomeslack(h,r) ;
   2957    
   2958   Variable (all,r,REG)(all,h,HHLD)
   2959       realpchhinc(h,r) # Real per capital household income #;
   2960   Equation E_RHHLDINCOME
   2961    # Household income of hhld h at market prices net of depreciation #
   2962   (all,r,REG)(all,h,HHLD)
   2963       realpchhinc(h,r)
   2964           = hhldincome(h,r) - pprivh(h,r) - poph(h,r) ;
   2965    
   2966   !<
   2967       7-3. Regional Household Demand System
   2968       -------------------------------------
   2969   >!
   2970    
   2971   Variable (all,r,REG)
   2972       dpgav(r) # average distribution parameter shift for Government #;
   2973   Equation DPARGAV
   2974   # average distribution parameter shift for government #
   2975   (all,r,REG)
   2976       dpgav(r)
   2977           = XSHRGOV(r) * dpgov(r)
   2978           + XSHRSAVG(r) * dpgsave(r);
   2979    
   2980   Variable (all,r,REG)(all,h,HHLD)
   2981       dphav(h,r) # average distribution parameter shift, for hhld income #;
   2982   Equation DPARHAV
   2983   # average distribution parameter shift for hhld income#
   2984   (all,r,REG)(all,h,HHLD)
   2985       dphav(h,r)
   2986           = XSHRPRIVH(h,r) * dpprivh(h,r)
   2987           + DUMSAVH(h,r) * XSHRSAVH(h,r) * (dphsave(h,r) + dphsave_all(r))
   2988           + (1-DUMSAVH(h,r)) * XSHRSAVH(h,r) * dphsave(h,r) ;
   2989    
   2990   Equation DPARSAV
   2991   # average savings distribution parameter shift #
   2992   (all,r,REG)
   2993       SAVE(r) * dpsave(r)
   2994           = SAV_GOV(r) * dpgsave(r)
   2995           + sum(h, HHLD, DUMSAVH(h,r) * SAV_HHLD(h,r) * (dphsave(h,r)
   2996                         + dphsave_all(r)))
   2997           + sum(h, HHLD, (1-DUMSAVH(h,r)) * SAV_HHLD(h,r) * dphsave(h,r)) ;
   2998    
   2999   Equation E_dppriv
   3000   # average savings distribution parameter shift #
   3001   (all,r,REG)
   3002       PRIVEXP(r) * dppriv(r)
   3003           = sum(h, HHLD, PRIVEXPH(h,r) * dpprivh(h,r)) ;
   3004    
   3005   Equation UTILITELASTIC
   3006   # elasticity of cost of utility wrt utility #
   3007   (all,r,REG)(all,h,HHLD)
   3008       uelash(h,r) = XSHRPRIVH(h,r) * ueprivh(h,r) - dphav(h,r);
   3009    
   3010   Equation PRIVCONSEXP
   3011   # private consumption expenditure by hhld h #
   3012   (all,r,REG)(all,h,HHLD)
   3013       yph(h,r) - hhldincome(h,r) = -[ueprivh(h,r) - uelash(h,r)] + dpprivh(h,r);
   3014    
   3015   Equation GOVCONSEXP
   3016   # government consumption expenditure #
   3017   (all,r,REG)
   3018       yg(r) - gincome(r) = dpgov(r) - dpgav(r) ;
   3019    
   3020   Equation SAVING
   3021   # total saving #
   3022   (all,r,REG)
   3023       SAVE(r) * qsave(r) = SAV_GOV(r) * qgsave(r)
   3024                  + sum(h, HHLD, SAV_HHLD(h,r) * qhsave(h,r)) ;
   3025    
   3026   Equation GSAVING
   3027   # Government saving #
   3028   (all,r,REG)
   3029       psave(r) + qgsave(r) - gincome(r) = dpgsave(r) - dpgav(r) ;
   3030    
   3031   Coefficient(all,r,REG)
   3032       GBAL(r) # government deficit in region r #;
   3033   Formula
   3034   # Government deficit #
   3035   (all,r,REG)
   3036       GBAL(r) = GOVINC(r) - GOVEXP(r)  ;
   3037    
   3038   Variable (change)(all,r,REG)
   3039       DGOVTBAL(r) # Change in government deficit in region r #;
   3040   Equation E_GOVDEF
   3041   # Government deficit #
   3042   (all,r,REG)
   3043       DGOVTBAL(r) = [GOVINC(r)/100] * gincome(r) - [GOVEXP(r)/100] * yg(r)  ;
   3044    
   3045   Variable (change)(all,r,REG)
   3046       DGOVTBALR(r) # Change in the ratio of the government deficit to income #;
   3047   Equation E_GOVDEFR
   3048   # Government deficit #
   3049   (all,r,REG)
   3050       100 * GOVINC(r) * DGOVTBALR(r) = 100 * DGOVTBAL(r) - GBAL(r) * gincome(r);
   3051    
   3052   Equation HSAVING
   3053   # Household saving #
   3054   (all,h,HHLD)(all,r,REG)
   3055       psave(r) + qhsave(h,r) - hhldincome(h,r) = uelash(h,r) + dphsave(h,r)
   3056            + DUMSAVH(h,r) * dphsave_all(r) ;
   3057    
   3058   !<
   3059       7-4. Aggregate Utility
   3060       ----------------------
   3061   >!
   3062    
   3063   Coefficient (all,r,REG)
   3064       XSHRPRIV(r) # private expenditure share in regional income #;
   3065   Formula (all,r,REG)
   3066       XSHRPRIV(r) = PRIVEXP(r) / INCOME(r);
   3067    
   3068   Coefficient (all,r,REG)
   3069       XSHRGOVY(r) # government expenditure share in regional income #;
   3070   Formula (all,r,REG)
   3071       XSHRGOVY(r) = GOVEXP(r) / INCOME(r);
   3072    
   3073   Coefficient (all,r,REG)
   3074       XSHRSAVE(r) # saving share in regional income #;
   3075   Formula (all,r,REG)
   3076       XSHRSAVE(r) = SAVE(r) / INCOME(r);
   3077    
   3078   Variable (all,r,REG)
   3079       p(r) # price index for disposition of income by regional household #;
   3080   Equation PRICEINDEXREG
   3081       # price index for disposition of income by regional household #
   3082       (all,r,REG)
   3083       p(r)
   3084           = XSHRPRIV(r) * ppriv(r)
   3085           + XSHRGOVY(r) * pgov(r)
   3086           + XSHRSAVE(r) * psave(r);
   3087    
   3088   Variable (all,r,REG)
   3089       au(r) # input-neutral shift in utility function #;
   3090   Variable (all,r,REG)
   3091       dpsum(r) # sum of the distribution parameters #;
   3092    
   3093   Coefficient (all,r,REG)
   3094       DPARSUM(r) # sum of distribution parameters #;
   3095   Read
   3096       DPARSUM from file GTAPDATA header "DPSM";
   3097   Update (all,r,REG)
   3098       DPARSUM(r) = dpsum(r);
   3099    
   3100   Coefficient (all,r,REG)
   3101       UELASPRIV(r)
   3102       # elasticity of cost wrt utility from private consumption by h#;
   3103   Formula (all,r,REG)
   3104       UELASPRIV(r) = sum(h, HHLD, PRIVEXPH(h,r)/PRIVEXP(r)
   3105                    * sum(i,TRAD_COMM, CONSHRH(i,h,r) * INCPAR(i,r)));
   3106    
   3107   Coefficient (all,r,REG)
   3108       UTILELAS(r) # elasticity of cost of utility wrt utility #;
   3109   Formula (all,r,REG)
   3110       UTILELAS(r)
   3111           = [UELASPRIV(r) * XSHRPRIV(r) + XSHRGOV(r) + XSHRSAVE(r)] / DPARSUM(r);
   3112    
   3113   Coefficient (all,r,REG)
   3114       DPARPRIV(r) # private consumption distribution parameter #;
   3115   Formula (all,r,REG)
   3116       DPARPRIV(r) = UELASPRIV(r) * XSHRPRIV(r) / UTILELAS(r);
   3117    
   3118   Coefficient (all,r,REG)
   3119       DPARGOV(r) # government consumption distribution parameter #;
   3120   Formula (all,r,REG)
   3121       DPARGOV(r) = XSHRGOV(r) / UTILELAS(r);
   3122    
   3123   Coefficient (all,r,REG)
   3124       DPARSAVE(r) # saving distribution parameter #;
   3125   Formula (all,r,REG)
   3126       DPARSAVE(r) = XSHRSAVE(r) / UTILELAS(r);
   3127    
   3128   Variable (all,r,REG)
   3129       up(r) ;
   3130   Equation E_up (all,r,REG)
   3131       up(r) = sum(h, HHLD, PRIVEXPH(h,r)/PRIVEXP(r) * uph(h,r));
   3132    
   3133   Coefficient (all,h,HHLD)(all,r,REG)
   3134       UTILPRIVH(h,r) # utility from private consumption #;
   3135   Formula (initial)(all,h,HHLD)(all,r,REG)
   3136       UTILPRIVH(h,r) = 1.0;
   3137   Update (all,h,HHLD)(all,r,REG)
   3138       UTILPRIVH(h,r) = uph(h,r);
   3139    
   3140   Coefficient (all,r,REG)
   3141       UTILPRIV(r) # utility from private consumption #;
   3142   Formula (all,r,REG)
   3143       UTILPRIV(r) = sum(h, HHLD, PRIVEXPH(h,r)/PRIVEXP(r) * UTILPRIVH(h,r));
   3144    
   3145   Coefficient (all,h,HHLD)(all,r,REG)
   3146       POPHHLD(h,r);
   3147   read (ifheaderexists) POPHHLD from file GTAPDATA header "POP";
   3148   update (all,h,HHLD)(all,r,REG)
   3149       POPHHLD(h,r) = poph(h,r) ;
   3150    
   3151   Variable (all,r,REG)
   3152       pop(r) ;
   3153   Equation E_pop (all,r,REG)
   3154       pop(r) = sum(h, HHLD, POPHHLD(h,r)/sum(k, HHLD, POPHHLD(k,r)) * poph(h,r));
   3155    
   3156   Variable (all,r,REG)
   3157       ug(r) ;
   3158   Equation E_ug (all,r,REG)
   3159       ug(r) = qgov(r) - pop(r);
   3160    
   3161   Coefficient (all,r,REG)
   3162       UTILGOV(r) # utility from government consumption #;
   3163   Formula (initial)(all,r,REG)
   3164       UTILGOV(r) = 1.0;
   3165   Update (all,r,REG)
   3166       UTILGOV(r) = ug(r);
   3167    
   3168   Coefficient (all,r,REG)
   3169       UTILGSAVE(r) # utility from saving #;
   3170   Formula (initial)(all,r,REG)
   3171       UTILGSAVE(r) = 1.0;
   3172   Update (change) (all,r,REG)
   3173       UTILGSAVE(r) = [[qgsave(r) - pop(r)] / 100] * UTILGSAVE(r);
   3174    
   3175   Coefficient (all,h,HHLD)(all,r,REG)
   3176       UTILHSAVE(h,r) # utility from saving #;
   3177   Formula (initial)(all,h,HHLD)(all,r,REG)
   3178       UTILHSAVE(h,r) = 1.0;
   3179   Update (change) (all,h,HHLD)(all,r,REG)
   3180       UTILHSAVE(h,r) = [[qhsave(h,r) - poph(h,r)] / 100] * UTILHSAVE(h,r);
   3181    
   3182   Coefficient (all,r,REG)
   3183       UTILSAVE(r) # utility from saving #;
   3184   Formula (all,r,REG)
   3185       UTILSAVE(r) = SAV_GOV(r)/SAVE(r) * UTILGSAVE(r)
   3186                   + sum(h, HHLD, SAV_HHLD(h,r)/SAVE(r) * UTILHSAVE(h,r))  ;
   3187    
   3188   Variable (all,r,REG)
   3189       u(r) # per capita utility from aggregate hhld expend. in region r #;
   3190   Equation UTILITY
   3191   # regional household utility #
   3192   (all,r,REG)
   3193       u(r)
   3194           = au(r)
   3195           + DPARPRIV(r) * loge(UTILPRIV(r)) * dppriv(r)
   3196           + DPARGOV(r) * loge(UTILGOV(r)) * dpgov(r)
   3197           + DPARSAVE(r) * loge(UTILSAVE(r)) * dpsave(r)
   3198           + [1.0 / UTILELAS(r)] * [y(r) - pop(r) - p(r)];
   3199    
   3200   Equation DISTPARSUM
   3201   # sum of the distribution parameters #
   3202   (all,r,REG)
   3203       DPARSUM(r) * dpsum(r)
   3204           = DPARPRIV(r) * dppriv(r)
   3205           + DPARGOV(r) * dpgov(r)
   3206           + DPARSAVE(r) * dpsave(r);
   3207    
   3208    
   3209   !<
   3210       -------------------------
   3211       8. Equilibrium Conditions
   3212       -------------------------
   3213    
   3214       8-1. Market Clearing Conditions
   3215       8-2. Walras' Law
   3216   >!
   3217    
   3218    
   3219   !<
   3220       8-1. Market Clearing Conditions
   3221       -------------------------------
   3222   >!
   3223    
   3224   Coefficient (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,j,PROD_COMM)(all,r,REG)
   3225       SHRDFM(i,j,r) # share of dom. prod. i used by sector j in r at mkt prices #;
   3226   Formula (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,j,PROD_COMM)(all,r,REG)
   3227       SHRDFM(i,j,r) = VDFM(i,j,r) / VDM(i,r);
   3228    
   3229   Coefficient (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,r,REG)
   3230       SHRDPM(i,r) # share of domestic prod. of i used by private hhlds in r #;
   3231   Formula (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,r,REG)
   3232       SHRDPM(i,r) = VDPM(i,r) / VDM(i,r);
   3233    
   3234   Coefficient (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,r,REG)
   3235       SHRDGM(i,r) # share of imports of i used by gov't hhlds in r #;
   3236   Formula (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,r,REG)
   3237       SHRDGM(i,r) = VDGM(i,r) / VDM(i,r);
   3238    
   3239   Variable (orig_level=VDM)(all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,r,REG)
   3240       qds(i,r) # domestic sales of commodity i in r #;
   3241   Equation MKTCLDOM
   3242   # eq'n assures market clearing for domestic sales (HT 3) #
   3243   (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,r,REG)
   3244       qds(i,r)
   3245           = sum(j,PROD_COMM, SHRDFM(i,j,r) * qfd(i,j,r))
   3246           + SHRDPM(i,r) * qpd(i,r)
   3247           + SHRDGM(i,r) * qgd(i,r);
   3248    
   3249   Coefficient (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,r,REG)
   3250       SHRDM(i,r) # share of domestic sales of i in r #;
   3251   Formula (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,r,REG)
   3252       SHRDM(i,r) = VDM(i,r) / VOM(i,r);
   3253    
   3254   Coefficient (all,m,MARG_COMM)(all,r,REG)
   3255       SHRST(m,r) # share of sales of m to global transport services in r #;
   3256   Formula (all,m,MARG_COMM)(all,r,REG)
   3257       SHRST(m,r) = VST(m,r) / VOM(m,r);
   3258    
   3259   Coefficient (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,r,REG)(all,s,REG)
   3260       SHRXMD(i,r,s) # share of export sales of i to s in r #;
   3261   Formula (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,r,REG)(all,s,REG)
   3262       SHRXMD(i,r,s) = VXMD(i,r,s) / VOM(i,r);
   3263    
   3264   Variable (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,r,REG)
   3265       tradslack(i,r) # slack variable in tradeables market clearing condition #;
   3266   !<
   3267       This is exogenous unless the user wishes to specify the price of
   3268       tradeables exogenously, in which case the analysis becomes partial
   3269       equilibrium and walraslack must be exogenized.
   3270   >!
   3271    
   3272   Equation MKTCLTRD_MARG
   3273   # eq'n assures market clearing for margins commodities (HT 1) #
   3274   (all,m,MARG_COMM)(all,r,REG)
   3275       qo(m,r)
   3276           = SHRDM(m,r) * qds(m,r)
   3277           + SHRST(m,r) * qst(m,r)
   3278           + sum(s,REG, SHRXMD(m,r,s) * qxs(m,r,s))
   3279           + tradslack(m,r);
   3280   Equation MKTCLTRD_NMRG
   3281   # eq'n assures market clearing for the non-margins commodities (HT 1) #
   3282   (all,i,NMRG_COMM)(all,r,REG)
   3283       qo(i,r)
   3284           = SHRDM(i,r) * qds(i,r)
   3285           + sum(s,REG, SHRXMD(i,r,s) * qxs(i,r,s))
   3286           + tradslack(i,r);
   3287    
   3288   Coefficient (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,r,REG)
   3289       VIM(i,r) # value of imports of commodity i in r at domestic market prices #;
   3290   Formula (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,r,REG)
   3291       VIM(i,r) = sum(j,PROD_COMM, VIFM(i,j,r)) + VIPM(i,r) + VIGM(i,r);
   3292    
   3293   Coefficient (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,j,PROD_COMM)(all,r,REG)
   3294       SHRIFM(i,j,r) # share of import i used by sector j in r  #;
   3295   Formula (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,j,PROD_COMM)(all,r,REG)
   3296       SHRIFM(i,j,r) = VIFM(i,j,r) / VIM(i,r);
   3297    
   3298   Coefficient (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,r,REG)
   3299       SHRIPM(i,r) # share of import i used by private hhlds in r #;
   3300   Formula (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,r,REG)
   3301       SHRIPM(i,r) = VIPM(i,r) / VIM(i,r);
   3302    
   3303   Coefficient (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,r,REG)
   3304       SHRIGM(i,r) # the share of import i used by gov't hhlds in r #;
   3305   Formula (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,r,REG)
   3306       SHRIGM(i,r) = VIGM(i,r) / VIM(i,r);
   3307    
   3308   Equation MKTCLIMP
   3309   # eq'n assures mkt clearing for imported goods entering each region (HT 2) #
   3310   (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,r,REG)
   3311       qim(i,r)
   3312           = sum(j,PROD_COMM, SHRIFM(i,j,r) * qfm(i,j,r))
   3313           + SHRIPM(i,r) * qpm(i,r)
   3314           + SHRIGM(i,r) * qgm(i,r);
   3315    
   3316   Coefficient (all,i,ENDWM_COMM)(all,j,PROD_COMM)(all,r,REG)
   3317       SHREM(i,j,r) # share of mobile endowment i used by sector j at mkt prices #;
   3318   Formula (all,i,ENDWM_COMM)(all,j,PROD_COMM)(all,r,REG)
   3319       SHREM(i,j,r) = sum(k, ENDW_COMM: MAPENDW(k)=MAPENDW(i), VFM(k,j,r))
   3320                       / sum(k, ENDW_COMM: MAPENDW(k)=MAPENDW(i), VOM(k,r));
   3321   Formula (all,i,ENDWM_COMM)(all,j,PROD_COMM)(all,r,REG: VOM(i,r)>0)
   3322       SHREM(i,j,r) = VFM(i,j,r) / VOM(i,r);
   3323    
   3324   Equation MKTCLENDWM
   3325   # eq'n assures mkt clearing for perfectly mobile endowments in each r (HT 4) #
   3326   (all,i,ENDWM_COMM)(all,r,REG)
   3327       qo(i,r) = sum(j,PROD_COMM, SHREM(i,j,r) * qfe(i,j,r)) + endwslack(i,r);
   3328   !<
   3329       This equation assures market clearing for perfectly mobile endowments (HT
   3330       4)
   3331   >!
   3332    
   3333   Equation MKTCLENDWS
   3334   # eq'n assures mkt clearing for imperfectly mobile endowments in each r (HT 5) #
   3335   (all,i,ENDWS_COMM)(all,j,PROD_COMM)(all,r,REG)
   3336       qoes(i,j,r) = qfe(i,j,r);
   3337   !<
   3338       This equation assures market clearing for sluggish endowments (HT 5)
   3339   >!
   3340    
   3341    
   3342   !<
   3343       8-2. Walras' Law
   3344       ----------------
   3345   >!
   3346    
   3347   Variable
   3348       walras_sup # supply in omitted market--global supply of cgds composite #;
   3349   Equation WALRAS_S
   3350   # Extra eq'n computes change in supply in the omitted market. #
   3351       walras_sup = pcgdswld + globalcgds;
   3352   !<
   3353       This is an extra equation which simply computes change in supply in the
   3354       omitted market.  (modified from HT 12 to reflect the value as opposed to
   3355       quantity change, in light of the new treatment of psave(r))
   3356   >!
   3357    
   3358   Variable
   3359       walras_dem # demand in the omitted market--global demand for savings #;
   3360   Equation WALRAS_D
   3361   # Extra eq'n computes change in demand in the omitted market. #
   3362       GLOBINV * walras_dem = sum(r,REG, SAV_GOV(r) * [qgsave(r) + psave(r)]
   3363                  + sum(h, HHLD, SAV_HHLD(h,r) * [qhsave(h,r) + psave(r)]));
   3364    
   3365   !<
   3366       This is an extra equation which simply computes change in demand in the
   3367       omitted market.  (modified from HT 13 to reflect the value as opposed to
   3368       quantity change)
   3369   >!
   3370    
   3371   Variable
   3372       walraslack # slack variable in the omitted market #;
   3373   !<
   3374       This is endogenous under normal, GE closure.  If the GE links are broken,
   3375       then this must be swapped with the numeraire, thereby forcing global
   3376       savings to explicitly equal global investment.
   3377   >!
   3378   Equation WALRAS
   3379   # Check Walras' Law.  Value of "walraslack" should be zero. (HT 14) #
   3380       walras_sup = walras_dem + walraslack;
   3381   !<
   3382       This equation checks Walras' Law.  The value of walraslack should be zero
   3383       in any GE simulation.  (HT 14)
   3384   >!
   3385    
   3386    
   3387   !<
   3388       ==========
   3389       Appendices
   3390       ==========
   3391    
   3392       A. Summary Indices
   3393       B. Equivalent Variation - removed
   3394       C. Welfare Decomposition
   3395       D. Terms of Trade Decomposition
   3396   >!
   3397    
   3398    
   3399   !<
   3400       ------------------
   3401       A. Summary Indices
   3402       ------------------
   3403    
   3404       The following equations calculate many useful summary statistics.  They do
   3405       not generally affect the equilibrium structure of the model, although they
   3406       do include the equation for the usual numeraire variable, "pfactwld". Some
   3407       are documented in Hertel and Tsigas, many are new.
   3408    
   3409       A-0. Appendix-Specific Variables and Coefficients
   3410       A-1. Factor Price Indices
   3411       A-2. Regional Terms of Trade
   3412       A-3. GDP Indices (Value, Price and Quantity)
   3413       A-4. Aggregate Trade Indices (Value, Price and Quantity)
   3414       A-5. Trade Balance Indices
   3415   >!
   3416    
   3417    
   3418   !<
   3419       A-0. Appendix-Specific Variables and Coefficients
   3420       -------------------------------------------------
   3421    
   3422       only used in this Summary Indices appendix
   3423   >!
   3424    
   3425   Variable (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,s,REG)
   3426       vxwfob(i,s) # value of merchandise regional exports, by commodity, FOB #;
   3427   Variable (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,s,REG)
   3428       viwcif(i,s) # value of merchandise regional imports, by commodity, CIF #;
   3429   Variable (all,r,REG)
   3430       vxwreg(r) # value of merchandise exports, by region #;
   3431   Variable (all,r,REG)
   3432       viwreg(r) # value of merchandise imports, by region, at world prices #;
   3433    
   3434   Coefficient (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,r,REG)
   3435       VXW(i,r) # value of exports by comm. i and region r at FOB prices #;
   3436   Formula (all,m,MARG_COMM)(all,r,REG)
   3437       VXW(m,r) = sum(s,REG, VXWD(m,r,s)) + VST(m,r);
   3438   Formula (all,i,NMRG_COMM)(all,r,REG)
   3439       VXW(i,r) = sum(s,REG, VXWD(i,r,s));
   3440    
   3441   Coefficient (all,r,REG)
   3442       VXWREGION(r) # value of exports by region r at FOB prices #;
   3443   Formula (all,r,REG)
   3444       VXWREGION(r) = sum(i,TRAD_COMM, VXW(i,r));
   3445    
   3446   Coefficient (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,s,REG)
   3447       VIW(i,s) # value of commodity imports i into s at CIF prices #;
   3448   Formula (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,s,REG)
   3449       VIW(i,s) = sum(r,REG, VIWS(i,r,s));
   3450   Coefficient (all,r,REG)
   3451       VIWREGION(r) # value of commodity imports by region r at CIF prices #;
   3452   Formula (all,r,REG)
   3453       VIWREGION(r) = sum(i,TRAD_COMM, VIW(i,r));
   3454    
   3455    
   3456   !<
   3457       A-1. Factor Price Indices
   3458       -------------------------
   3459   >!
   3460    
   3461   Variable (orig_level=1.0)(all,i,ENDW_COMM)(all,r,REG)
   3462       pfactreal(i,r) # ratio of return to primary factor i to CPI in r #;
   3463   Equation REALRETURN
   3464   # eq'n defines the real rate of return to primary factor i in region r #
   3465   (all,i,ENDW_COMM)(all,s,REG)
   3466       pfactreal(i,s) = [pm(i,s) - ppriv(s)];
   3467   !<
   3468       This equation defines the real rate of return to primary factor i in
   3469       region r (new).
   3470   >!
   3471    
   3472   Coefficient (all,r,REG)
   3473       VENDWREG(r) # value of primary factors, at mkt prices, by region #;
   3474   Formula (all,r,REG)
   3475       VENDWREG(r) = sum(i,ENDW_COMM, VOM(i,r));
   3476    
   3477   Variable (orig_level=1.0)(all,r,REG)
   3478       pfactor(r) # market price index of primary factors, by region #;
   3479   Equation PRIMFACTPR
   3480   # computes % change in price index of primary factors, by region #
   3481   (all,r,REG)
   3482       VENDWREG(r) * pfactor(r) = sum(i,ENDW_COMM, VOM(i,r) * pm(i,r));
   3483    
   3484   Coefficient
   3485       VENDWWLD # value of primary factors, at mkt prices, worldwide #;
   3486   Formula
   3487       VENDWWLD = sum(r,REG, VENDWREG(r));
   3488   Variable (orig_level=1.0)
   3489       pfactwld # world price index of primary factors #;
   3490   Equation PRIMFACTPRWLD
   3491   # computes % change in global price index of primary factors #
   3492       VENDWWLD * pfactwld = sum(r,REG, VENDWREG(r) * pfactor(r));
   3493    
   3494    
   3495   !<
   3496       A-2. Regional Terms of Trade
   3497       ----------------------------
   3498    
   3499       The next three equations correspond to Table 10 of Hertel and Tsigas on
   3500       Regional Terms of Trade.
   3501   >!
   3502    
   3503   Variable (orig_level=1.0)(all,r,REG)
   3504       psw(r) # index of prices received for tradeables produced in r #;
   3505   Equation REGSUPRICE
   3506   # estimate change in index of prices received for tradeables i produced in r #
   3507   (all,r,REG)
   3508       VXWREGION(r) * psw(r)
   3509           = sum(i,TRAD_COMM, sum(s,REG, VXWD(i,r,s) * pfob(i,r,s)))
   3510           + sum(m,MARG_COMM, VST(m,r) * pm(m,r));
   3511   !<
   3512       This equation estimates the change in the index of prices received for
   3513       tradeable products produced in r.  (modified from HT 64 to eliminate the
   3514       investment component)
   3515   >!
   3516    
   3517   Variable (orig_level=1.0)(all,r,REG)
   3518       pdw(r) # index of prices paid for tradeables used in region r #;
   3519   Equation REGDEMPRICE
   3520   # estimate change in index of prices paid for tradeable products used in r #
   3521   (all,r,REG)
   3522       VIWREGION(r) * pdw(r)
   3523           = sum(i,TRAD_COMM, sum(k,REG, VIWS(i,k,r) * pcif(i,k,r)));
   3524   !<
   3525       This equation estimates the change in the index of prices paid for
   3526       tradeable products used in r.  (modified from HT 65 to eliminate savings)
   3527   >!
   3528    
   3529   Variable (orig_level=1.0)(all,r,REG)
   3530       tot(r) # terms of trade for region r: tot(r) = psw(r) - pdw(r) #;
   3531   Equation TOTeq
   3532   # terms of trade equation computed as difference in psw and pdw (HT 66) #
   3533   (all,r,REG)
   3534       tot(r) = psw(r) - pdw(r);
   3535    
   3536    
   3537   !<
   3538       A-3. GDP Indices (Value, Price and Quantity)
   3539       --------------------------------------------
   3540   >!
   3541    
   3542   Coefficient (all,r,REG)
   3543       GDP(r) # Gross Domestic Product in region r #;
   3544   Formula (all,s,REG)
   3545       GDP(s)
   3546           = sum(i,TRAD_COMM, VPA(i,s))
   3547           + sum(i,TRAD_COMM, VGA(i,s))
   3548           + sum(k,CGDS_COMM, VOA(k,s))
   3549           + sum(i,TRAD_COMM, sum(r,REG, VXWD(i,s,r)))
   3550           + sum(m,MARG_COMM, VST(m,s))
   3551           - sum(i,TRAD_COMM, sum(r,REG, VIWS(i,r,s)));
   3552   !<
   3553       Gross Domestic Product in region r.  Trade is valued at FOB and CIF
   3554       prices.
   3555   >!
   3556    
   3557   Variable (all,r,REG)
   3558       vgdp(r) # change in value of GDP #;
   3559   Equation VGDP_r
   3560   # change in value of GDP (HT 70) #
   3561   (all,r,REG)
   3562       GDP(r) * vgdp(r)
   3563           = sum(i,TRAD_COMM, VGA(i,r) * [qg(i,r) + pg(i,r)])
   3564           + sum(i,TRAD_COMM, VPA(i,r) * [qp(i,r) + pp(i,r)])
   3565           + REGINV(r) * [qcgds(r) + pcgds(r)]
   3566           + sum(i,TRAD_COMM, sum(s,REG, VXWD(i,r,s) * [qxs(i,r,s) + pfob(i,r,s)]))
   3567           + sum(m,MARG_COMM, VST(m,r) * [qst(m,r) + pm(m,r)])
   3568           - sum(i,TRAD_COMM, sum(s,REG,
   3569               VIWS(i,s,r) * [qxs(i,s,r) + pcif(i,s,r)]));
   3570    
   3571   Variable (orig_level=1.0)(all,r,REG)
   3572       pgdp(r) # GDP price index #;
   3573   Equation PGDP_r
   3574   # GDP price index (HT 71) #
   3575   (all,r,REG)
   3576       GDP(r) * pgdp(r)
   3577           = sum(i,TRAD_COMM, VGA(i,r) * pg(i,r))
   3578           + sum(i,TRAD_COMM, VPA(i,r) * pp(i,r))
   3579           + REGINV(r) * pcgds(r)
   3580           + sum(i,TRAD_COMM, sum(s,REG, VXWD(i,r,s) * pfob(i,r,s)))
   3581           + sum(m,MARG_COMM, VST(m,r) * pm(m,r))
   3582           - sum(i,TRAD_COMM, sum(s,REG, VIWS(i,s,r) * pcif(i,s,r)));
   3583    
   3584   Variable (orig_level=GDP)(all,r,REG)
   3585       qgdp(r) # GDP quantity index #;
   3586   Equation QGDP_r
   3587   # GDP quantity index #
   3588   (all,r,REG)
   3589       GDP(r) * qgdp(r)
   3590           = sum(i,TRAD_COMM, VGA(i,r) * qg(i,r))
   3591           + sum(i,TRAD_COMM, VPA(i,r) * qp(i,r))
   3592           + REGINV(r) * qcgds(r)
   3593           + sum(i,TRAD_COMM, sum(s,REG, VXWD(i,r,s) * qxs(i,r,s)))
   3594           + sum(m,MARG_COMM, VST(m,r) * qst(m,r))
   3595           - sum(i,TRAD_COMM, sum(s,REG, VIWS(i,s,r)
   3596              * (qxs(i,s,r))));
   3597    
   3598   Coefficient (all,r,REG)
   3599       GDPva(r) # Gross Domestic Product in region r #;
   3600   Formula (all,r,REG)
   3601       GDPva(r)
   3602           = sum(i,ENDW_COMM, VOA(i,r))
   3603           + sum{i,NSAV_COMM, VOM(i,r) - VOA(i,r)}
   3604           + sum{j,PROD_COMM, sum{i,ENDW_COMM, VFA(i,j,r) - VFM(i,j,r)}}
   3605           + sum{i,TRAD_COMM, VIPA(i,r) - VIPM(i,r)}
   3606           + sum{i,TRAD_COMM, VDPA(i,r) - VDPM(i,r)}
   3607           + sum{i,TRAD_COMM, VIGA(i,r) - VIGM(i,r)}
   3608           + sum{i,TRAD_COMM, VDGA(i,r) - VDGM(i,r)}
   3609           + sum{j,PROD_COMM, sum{i,TRAD_COMM, VIFA(i,j,r) - VIFM(i,j,r)}}
   3610           + sum{j,PROD_COMM, sum{i,TRAD_COMM, VDFA(i,j,r) - VDFM(i,j,r)}}
   3611           + sum{i,TRAD_COMM, sum{s,REG, VXWD(i,r,s) - VXMD(i,r,s)}}
   3612           + sum{i,TRAD_COMM, sum{s,REG, VIMS(i,s,r) - VIWS(i,s,r)}}
   3613   ;
   3614    
   3615   Variable (orig_level=GDP)(all,r,REG)
   3616       qgdpva(r) # GDP quantity index #;
   3617   Equation QGDPva_r
   3618   # GDP quantity index #
   3619   (all,r,REG)
   3620       GDPva(r) * qgdpva(r)
   3621           = sum(i,ENDW_COMM, sum(h, HHLD, EVOAH(i,h,r)
   3622                   * (qoh(i,h,r))))
   3623           + sum{i,NSAV_COMM, VOM(i,r) * (qo(i,r))
   3624               - VOA(i,r) * (qo(i,r))}
   3625           + sum{j,PROD_COMM, sum{i,ENDWM_COMM, VFA(i,j,r)
   3626                   * (qfe(i,j,r))
   3627               - VFM(i,j,r) * (qfe(i,j,r))}}
   3628           + sum{j,PROD_COMM, sum{i,ENDWS_COMM, VFA(i,j,r)
   3629                   * (qfe(i,j,r))
   3630               - VFM(i,j,r) * (qfe(i,j,r))}}
   3631           + sum{i,TRAD_COMM, sum(h, HHLD, VIPAH(i,h,r)
   3632                   * (qpmh(i,h,r))
   3633               - VIPMH(i,h,r) * (qpmh(i,h,r)))}
   3634           + sum{i,TRAD_COMM, sum(h, HHLD, VDPAH(i,h,r)
   3635                   * (qpdh(i,h,r))
   3636               - VDPMH(i,h,r) * (qpdh(i,h,r)))}
   3637           + sum{i,TRAD_COMM, VIGA(i,r) * (qgm(i,r))
   3638               - VIGM(i,r) * (qgm(i,r))}
   3639           + sum{i,TRAD_COMM, VDGA(i,r) * (qgd(i,r))
   3640               - VDGM(i,r) * (qgd(i,r))}
   3641           + sum{j,PROD_COMM, sum{i,TRAD_COMM,
   3642                 VIFA(i,j,r) * (qfm(i,j,r))
   3643               - VIFM(i,j,r) * (qfm(i,j,r))}}
   3644           + sum{j,PROD_COMM, sum{i,TRAD_COMM, VDFA(i,j,r)
   3645                   * (qfd(i,j,r))
   3646               - VDFM(i,j,r) * (qfd(i,j,r))}}
   3647           + sum{i,TRAD_COMM, sum{s,REG, VXWD(i,r,s)
   3648                   * (qxs(i,r,s))
   3649               - VXMD(i,r,s) * (qxs(i,r,s))}}
   3650           + sum{i,TRAD_COMM, sum{s,REG,
   3651                 VIMS(i,s,r) * (qxs(i,s,r))
   3652               - VIWS(i,s,r) * (qxs(i,s,r))}}
   3653           + sum(i,PROD_COMM, VOA(i,r) * ao(i,r))
   3654           + sum(j,PROD_COMM, sum(i,ENDW_COMM, VFA(i,j,r) * afe(i,j,r)))
   3655           + sum(j,PROD_COMM, VVA(j,r) * ava(j,r))
   3656           + sum(j,PROD_COMM, sum(i,TRAD_COMM,
   3657                   [VIFA(i,j,r) + VDFA(i,j,r)] * af(i,j,r)))
   3658           + sum(m,MARG_COMM, sum(i,TRAD_COMM, sum(s,REG,
   3659                   VTMFSD(m,i,s,r) * atmfsd(m,i,s,r))))
   3660           + sum(i,TRAD_COMM, sum(s,REG, VIMS(i,s,r) * ams(i,s,r))) ;
   3661   !<
   3662       modified from HT 72 for use with AnalyzeGE
   3663   >!
   3664    
   3665   Variable (all,i,PROD_COMM)(all,r,REG)
   3666       compvalad(i,r) # composition of value added for good i and region r #;
   3667   Equation COMPVALADEQ
   3668   # track change in composition of value added #
   3669   (all,i,PROD_COMM)(all,r,REG)
   3670       compvalad(i,r) = qo(i,r) - qgdp(r);
   3671    
   3672    
   3673   !<
   3674       A-4. Aggregate Trade Indices (Value, Price and Quantity)
   3675       --------------------------------------------------------
   3676   >!
   3677    
   3678    
   3679   !<
   3680       Common Variables and Coefficients
   3681       Value Indices for Aggregate Trade
   3682       Price Indices for Aggregate Trade
   3683       Quantity Indices for Aggregate Trade
   3684   >!
   3685    
   3686    
   3687   !<
   3688       Common Variables and Coefficients
   3689       .................................
   3690    
   3691       only used in this Aggregate Trade Indices section
   3692   >!
   3693    
   3694   Variable (orig_level=1.0)(all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,r,REG)
   3695       pxw(i,r) # aggregate exports price index of i from region r #;
   3696    
   3697   Coefficient (all,i,TRAD_COMM)
   3698       VXWCOMMOD(i) # value of world exports by commodity i at FOB prices #;
   3699   Formula (all,i,TRAD_COMM)
   3700       VXWCOMMOD(i) = sum(r,REG, VXW(i,r));
   3701    
   3702   Coefficient
   3703       VXWLD # value of commodity exports, FOB, globally #;
   3704   Formula
   3705       VXWLD = sum(r,REG, VXWREGION(r));
   3706    
   3707   Coefficient (all,i,TRAD_COMM)
   3708       VIWCOMMOD(i) # global value of commodity imports, CIF, by commodity #;
   3709   Formula (all,i,TRAD_COMM)
   3710       VIWCOMMOD(i) = sum(r,REG, VIW(i,r));
   3711    
   3712   Coefficient (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,r,REG)
   3713       PW_PM(i,r) # ratio of world to domestic prices #;
   3714   Formula (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,r,REG)
   3715       PW_PM(i,r) = sum(s,REG, VXWD(i,r,s)) / sum(s,REG, VXMD(i,r,s));
   3716   Coefficient (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,r,REG)
   3717       VOW(i,r) # value of output in r at FOB including transportation services #;
   3718   Formula (all,m,MARG_COMM)(all,r,REG)
   3719       VOW(m,r) = VDM(m,r) * PW_PM(m,r) + sum(s,REG, VXWD(m,r,s)) + VST(m,r);
   3720   Formula (all,i,NMRG_COMM)(all,r,REG)
   3721       VOW(i,r) = VDM(i,r) * PW_PM(i,r) + sum(s,REG, VXWD(i,r,s));
   3722    
   3723   Coefficient (all,i,TRAD_COMM)
   3724       VWOW(i) # value of world supply at world prices for i #;
   3725   Formula (all,i,TRAD_COMM)
   3726       VWOW(i) = sum(r,REG, VOW(i,r));
   3727    
   3728   Coefficient (all,i,TRAD_COMM)
   3729       VWOU(i) # value of world output of i at user prices #;
   3730   Formula (all,i,TRAD_COMM)
   3731       VWOU(i) = sum(s,REG, [VPA(i,s) + VGA(i,s)] + sum(j,PROD_COMM, VFA(i,j,s)));
   3732    
   3733    
   3734   !<
   3735       Value Indices for Aggregate Trade
   3736       .................................
   3737   >!
   3738    
   3739   Equation VREGEX_ir_MARG
   3740   # the change in FOB value of exports of m from r #
   3741   (all,m,MARG_COMM)(all,r,REG)
   3742       VXW(m,r) * vxwfob(m,r)
   3743           = sum(s,REG, VXWD(m,r,s) * [qxs(m,r,s) + pfob(m,r,s)])
   3744           + VST(m,r) * [qst(m,r) + pm(m,r)];
   3745   Equation VREGEX_ir_NMRG
   3746   # the change in FOB value of exports of commodity i from r (HT 73) #
   3747   (all,i,NMRG_COMM)(all,r,REG)
   3748       VXW(i,r) * vxwfob(i,r)
   3749           = sum(s,REG, VXWD(i,r,s) * [qxs(i,r,s) + pfob(i,r,s)]);
   3750    
   3751   Equation VREGEX_r
   3752   # computes % change in value of merchandise exports, by region (HT 75) #
   3753   (all,r,REG)
   3754       VXWREGION(r) * vxwreg(r) = sum(i,TRAD_COMM, VXW(i,r) * vxwfob(i,r));
   3755    
   3756   Variable (all,i,TRAD_COMM)
   3757       vxwcom(i) # value of global merchandise exports by commodity #;
   3758   Equation VWLDEX_i
   3759   # computes % change in FOB value of global exports, by commodity (HT 77) #
   3760   (all,i,TRAD_COMM)
   3761       VXWCOMMOD(i) * vxwcom(i) = sum(r,REG, VXW(i,r) * vxwfob(i,r));
   3762    
   3763   Variable
   3764       vxwwld # value of world trade #;
   3765   Equation VWLDEX
   3766   # computes % change in value of global exports (HT 79) #
   3767       VXWLD * vxwwld = sum(r,REG, VXWREGION(r) * vxwreg(r));
   3768    
   3769   Equation VREGIM_is
   3770   # the change in CIF value of imports of commodity i into s (HT 74) #
   3771   (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,s,REG)
   3772       VIW(i,s) * viwcif(i,s)
   3773           = sum(r,REG, VIWS(i,r,s) * [pcif(i,r,s) + qxs(i,r,s)]);
   3774    
   3775   Equation VREGIM_s
   3776   # computes % change in value of imports, CIF basis, by region (HT 76) #
   3777   (all,s,REG)
   3778       VIWREGION(s) * viwreg(s) = sum(i,TRAD_COMM, VIW(i,s) * viwcif(i,s));
   3779    
   3780   Variable (all,i,TRAD_COMM)
   3781       viwcom(i) # value of global merchandise imports i, at world prices #;
   3782   Equation VWLDIM_i
   3783   # computes % change in value of global imports, by commodity (HT 78) #
   3784   (all,i,TRAD_COMM)
   3785       VIWCOMMOD(i) * viwcom(i) = sum(s,REG, VIW(i,s) * viwcif(i,s));
   3786    
   3787   Variable (all,i,TRAD_COMM)
   3788       valuew(i) # value of world supply of good i #;
   3789   Equation VWLDOUT
   3790   # change in value of world output of comm. i at FOB prices (HT 80) #
   3791   (all,i,TRAD_COMM)
   3792       VWOW(i) * valuew(i) = sum(r,REG, VOW(i,r) * [pxw(i,r) + qo(i,r)]);
   3793    
   3794   Variable (all,i,TRAD_COMM)
   3795       valuewu(i) # value of world supply of good i at user prices #;
   3796   Equation VWLDOUTUSE
   3797   # change in value of world output of commodity i at user prices #
   3798   (all,i,TRAD_COMM)
   3799       VWOU(i) * valuewu(i)
   3800           = sum(s,REG, VPA(i,s) * [pp(i,s) + qp(i,s)]
   3801           + VGA(i,s) * [pg(i,s) + qg(i,s)]
   3802           + sum(j,PROD_COMM, VFA(i,j,s) * [pf(i,j,s) + qf(i,j,s)]));
   3803    
   3804    
   3805   !<
   3806       Price Indices for Aggregate Trade
   3807       .................................
   3808   >!
   3809    
   3810   Equation PREGEX_ir_MARG
   3811   # change in FOB price index of exports of m from r #
   3812   (all,m,MARG_COMM)(all,r,REG)
   3813       VXW(m,r) * pxw(m,r)
   3814           = sum(s,REG, VXWD(m,r,s) * pfob(m,r,s)) + VST(m,r) * pm(m,r);
   3815    
   3816   Equation PREGEX_ir_NMRG
   3817   # change in FOB price index of exports of commodity i from r (HT 81) #
   3818   (all,i,NMRG_COMM)(all,r,REG)
   3819       VXW(i,r) * pxw(i,r) = sum(s,REG, VXWD(i,r,s) * pfob(i,r,s));
   3820    
   3821   Variable (orig_level=1.0)(all,r,REG)
   3822       pxwreg(r) # price index of merchandise exports, by region #;
   3823   Equation PREGEX_r
   3824   # computes % change in price index of exports, by region (HT 83) #
   3825   (all,r,REG)
   3826       VXWREGION(r) * pxwreg(r) = sum(i,TRAD_COMM, VXW(i,r) * pxw(i,r));
   3827    
   3828   Variable (orig_level=1.0)(all,i,TRAD_COMM)
   3829       pxwcom(i) # price index of global merchandise exports by commodity #;
   3830   Equation PWLDEX_i
   3831   # computes % change in price index of exports, by commodity (HT 85) #
   3832   (all,i,TRAD_COMM)
   3833       VXWCOMMOD(i) * pxwcom(i) = sum(r,REG, VXW(i,r) * pxw(i,r));
   3834    
   3835   Variable (orig_level=1.0)
   3836       pxwwld # price index of world trade #;
   3837   Equation PWLDEX
   3838   # computes % change in price index of global exports (HT 87) #
   3839       VXWLD * pxwwld = sum(r,REG, VXWREGION(r) * pxwreg(r));
   3840    
   3841   Variable (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,r,REG)
   3842       piw(i,r) # world price of composite import i in region r #;
   3843   Equation PREGIM_is
   3844   # change in CIF price index of imports of commodity i into s (HT 82) #
   3845   (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,s,REG)
   3846       VIW(i,s) * piw(i,s) = sum(r,REG, VIWS(i,r,s) * pcif(i,r,s));
   3847    
   3848   Variable (orig_level=1.0)(all,r,REG)
   3849       piwreg(r) # price index of merchandise imports, by region #;
   3850   Equation PREGIM_s
   3851   # computes % change in price index of imports, by region (HT 84) #
   3852   (all,s,REG)
   3853       VIWREGION(s) * piwreg(s) = sum(i,TRAD_COMM, VIW(i,s) * piw(i,s));
   3854    
   3855   Variable (orig_level=1.0)(all,i,TRAD_COMM)
   3856       piwcom(i) # price index of global merchandise imports by commodity #;
   3857   Equation PWLDIM_i
   3858   # computes % change in price index of imports, by commodity (HT 86) #
   3859   (all,i,TRAD_COMM)
   3860       VIWCOMMOD(i) * piwcom(i) = sum(s,REG, VIW(i,s) * piw(i,s));
   3861    
   3862   Variable (all,i,TRAD_COMM)
   3863       pw(i) # world price index for total good i supplies #;
   3864   Equation PWLDOUT
   3865   # change in index of world prices, FOB, for total production of i (HT 88) #
   3866   (all,i,TRAD_COMM)
   3867       VWOW(i) * pw(i) = sum(r,REG, VOW(i,r) * pxw(i,r));
   3868    
   3869   Variable (orig_level=1.0)(all,i,TRAD_COMM)
   3870       pwu(i) # world price index for total good i supplies at user prices #;
   3871   Equation PWLDUSE
   3872   # change in index of user prices for deflating world production of i #
   3873   (all,i,TRAD_COMM)
   3874       VWOU(i) * pwu(i)
   3875           = sum(s,REG, VPA(i,s) * pp(i,s)
   3876           + VGA(i,s) * pg(i,s)
   3877           + sum(j,PROD_COMM, VFA(i,j,s) * pf(i,j,s)));
   3878    
   3879    
   3880   !<
   3881       Quantity Indices for Aggregate Trade
   3882       ....................................
   3883   >!
   3884    
   3885   Variable (orig_level=VXW)(all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,r,REG)
   3886       qxw(i,r) # aggregate exports of i from region r, FOB weights #;
   3887   Equation QREGEX_ir_MARG
   3888   # change in volume of exports of margin commodity m from r #
   3889   (all,m,MARG_COMM)(all,r,REG)
   3890       VXW(m,r) * qxw(m,r)
   3891           = sum(s,REG, VXWD(m,r,s) * qxs(m,r,s)) + VST(m,r) * qst(m,r);
   3892   Equation QREGEX_ir_NMRG
   3893   # change in volume of exports of non-margin commodity i from r #
   3894   (all,i,NMRG_COMM)(all,r,REG)
   3895       VXW(i,r) * qxw(i,r) = sum(s,REG, VXWD(i,r,s) * qxs(i,r,s));
   3896   !<
   3897       modified from HT 89 for use with AnalyzeGE
   3898   >!
   3899    
   3900   Variable (orig_level=VXWREGION)(all,r,REG)
   3901       qxwreg(r) # volume of merchandise exports, by region #;
   3902   Equation QREGEX_r
   3903   # computes % change in quantity index of exports, by region #
   3904   (all,r,REG)
   3905       VXWREGION(r) * qxwreg(r) = sum(i,TRAD_COMM, VXW(i,r) * qxw(i,r));
   3906   !<
   3907       modified from HT 91 for use with AnalyzeGE
   3908   >!
   3909    
   3910   Variable (orig_level=VXWCOMMOD)(all,i,TRAD_COMM)
   3911       qxwcom(i) # volume of global merchandise exports by commodity #;
   3912   Equation QWLDEX_i
   3913   # computes % change in quantity index of exports, by commodity #
   3914   (all,i,TRAD_COMM)
   3915       VXWCOMMOD(i) * qxwcom(i) = sum(r,REG, VXW(i,r) * qxw(i,r));
   3916   !<
   3917       modified from HT 93 for use with AnalyzeGE
   3918   >!
   3919    
   3920   Variable (orig_level=VXWLD)
   3921       qxwwld # volume of world trade #;
   3922   Equation QWLDEX
   3923   # computes % change in quantity index of global exports #
   3924       VXWLD * qxwwld = sum(r,REG, VXWREGION(r) * qxwreg(r));
   3925   !<
   3926       modified from HT 95 for use with AnalyzeGE
   3927   >!
   3928    
   3929   Variable (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,s,REG)
   3930       qiw(i,s) # aggregate imports of i into region s, CIF weights #;
   3931   Equation QREGIM_is
   3932   # change in volume of imports of commodity i into s #
   3933   (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,s,REG)
   3934       VIW(i,s) * qiw(i,s) = sum(r,REG, VIWS(i,r,s) * qxs(i,r,s));
   3935   !<
   3936       modified from HT 90 for use with AnalyzeGE
   3937   >!
   3938    
   3939   Variable (orig_level=VIWREGION)(all,r,REG)
   3940       qiwreg(r) # volume of merchandise imports, by region #;
   3941   Equation QREGIM_s
   3942   # computes % change in quantity index of imports, by region #
   3943   (all,s,REG)
   3944       VIWREGION(s) * qiwreg(s) = sum(i,TRAD_COMM, VIW(i,s) * qiw(i,s));
   3945   !<
   3946       modified from HT 92 for use with AnalyzeGE
   3947   >!
   3948    
   3949   Variable (orig_level=VIWCOMMOD)(all,i,TRAD_COMM)
   3950       qiwcom(i) # volume of global merchandise imports by commodity #;
   3951   Equation QWLDIM_i
   3952   # computes % change in quantity index of imports, by commodity #
   3953   (all,i,TRAD_COMM)
   3954       VIWCOMMOD(i) * qiwcom(i) = sum(s,REG, VIW(i,s) * qiw(i,s));
   3955   !<
   3956       modified from HT 94 for use with AnalyzeGE
   3957   >!
   3958    
   3959   Variable (all,i,TRAD_COMM)
   3960       qow(i) # quantity index for world supply of good i #;
   3961   Equation QWLDOUT
   3962   # change in index of world production of i #
   3963   (all,i,TRAD_COMM)
   3964       VWOW(i) * qow(i) = sum(r,REG, VOW(i,r) * qo(i,r));
   3965   !<
   3966       modified from HT 96 for use with AnalyzeGE
   3967   >!
   3968    
   3969   Variable (orig_level=VWOU)(all,i,TRAD_COMM)
   3970       qowu(i) # quantity index for world supply of good i at user prices #;
   3971   Equation QWLDOUTU
   3972   # change in index of world production of i evaluated at user prices #
   3973   (all,i,TRAD_COMM)
   3974       VWOU(i) * qowu(i)
   3975           = sum(s,REG, VPA(i,s) * qp(i,s)
   3976           + VGA(i,s) * qg(i,s)
   3977           + sum(j,PROD_COMM, VFA(i,j,s) * qf(i,j,s)));
   3978    
   3979    
   3980   !<
   3981       A-5. Trade Balance Indices
   3982       --------------------------
   3983   >!
   3984    
   3985   Variable (change)(all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,r,REG)
   3986       DTBALi(i,r) # change in trade balance by i and by r, $ US million #;
   3987   !<
   3988       A positive value indicates that the change in exports exceeds the change
   3989       in imports.
   3990   >!
   3991   Equation TRADEBAL_i
   3992   # computes change in trade balance by commodity and by region (HT 97) #
   3993   (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,r,REG)
   3994       DTBALi(i,r)
   3995           = [VXW(i,r) / 100] * vxwfob(i,r) - [VIW(i,r) / 100] * viwcif(i,r);
   3996    
   3997   Variable (change)(all,r,REG)
   3998       DTBAL(r) # change in trade balance X - M, $ US million #;
   3999   Equation TRADEBALANCE
   4000   # computes change in trade balance (X - M), by region (HT 98) #
   4001   (all,r,REG)
   4002       DTBAL(r)
   4003           = [VXWREGION(r) / 100] * vxwreg(r) - [VIWREGION(r) / 100] * viwreg(r);
   4004    
   4005   !<
   4006       In order to maintain homogeneity in the presence of a fixed trade balance,
   4007       it is useful to have a nominal variable which this is measured against.
   4008       The next equation provides this, and we recommend users fix DTBALR instead
   4009       of fixing DTBAL in future simulations.  The strategy is the same one used
   4010       above for taxes.
   4011   >!
   4012    
   4013   Coefficient (all,r,REG)
   4014       TBAL(r) # trade balance for region r #;
   4015   Formula (all,r,REG)
   4016       TBAL(r) = VXWREGION(r) - VIWREGION(r);
   4017    
   4018   Variable (change)(all,r,REG)
   4019       DTBALR(r) # change in ratio of trade balance to regional income #;
   4020   Equation DTBALRATIO
   4021   # change in ratio of trade balance to regional income #
   4022   (all,r,REG)
   4023       100 * INCOME(r) * DTBALR(r) = 100 * DTBAL(r) - TBAL(r) * y(r);
   4024    
   4025   !<
   4026       A-5. Foreign savings
   4027       --------------------
   4028   >!
   4029    
   4030   Variable (levels, change) (all,r,REG)
   4031       SAV_FOR(r) # Foreign savings #;
   4032    
   4033   formula (initial)(all,r,REG)
   4034       SAV_FOR(r) = sum(i, TRAD_COMM, sum(s, REG, VXWD(i,r,s)))
   4035                  + sum(i, MARG_COMM, VST(i,r))
   4036                  - sum(i, TRAD_COMM, sum(s, REG, VIWS(i,s,r)))
   4037                  + sum(h, HHLD, REMI(h,r) - REMO(h,r))
   4038                  + sum(h, HHLD, FYI(h,r) - FYO(h,r))
   4039                  + AIDI(r) - AIDO(r) ;
   4040    
   4041   !< also equal to
   4042       SAV_FOR(r) = (sum(h, HHLD, SAV_HHLD(h,r)) + SAV_GOV(r)) + VDEP(r)
   4043                     - REGINV(r) ;>!
   4044    
   4045   equation E_SAV_FOR (all,r,REG)
   4046       100 * c_SAV_FOR(r) = (sum(h, HHLD, SAV_HHLD(h,r) * (psave(r) + qhsave(h,r)))
   4047                    + SAV_GOV(r) * (psave(r) + qgsave(r)))
   4048                     + VDEP(r) * (pcgds(r) + kb(r))
   4049                    - REGINV(r) * (pcgds(r) + qcgds(r));
   4050   !<
   4051       -----------------------
   4052       B. Equivalent Variation
   4053       -----------------------
   4054    
   4055       B-0. Appendix-Specific Variables and Coefficients
   4056       B-1. Government Consumption Shadow Demand System
   4057       B-2. Private Consumption Shadow Demand System
   4058       B-3. Regional Household Shadow Demand System
   4059       B-4. Equivalent Variation
   4060    
   4061       This appendix calculates equivalent variation "EV" and world equivalent
   4062       variation, "WEV", by determining the income "yev" that would be required
   4063       to achieve the current actual utility level "u" in a shadow demand system
   4064       in which prices are fixed.
   4065    
   4066       Section B-2 calculates the utility elasticity of private consumption
   4067       expenditure, "ueprivev", within a shadow demand system for private
   4068       consumption, for use in section B-3.  B-3 calculates private consumption
   4069       expenditure "ypev" for use in B-2, and regional income "yev" for use in
   4070       B-4, within a shadow demand system for the regional household.  B-4
   4071       calculates "EV" and "WEV".
   4072    
   4073   >!
   4074   !<
   4075       B-0. Appendix-Specific Variables and Coefficients
   4076       -------------------------------------------------
   4077    
   4078       only used in this Equivalent Variation section of the Summary Indices
   4079       appendix
   4080   >!
   4081    
   4082   Variable (all,r,REG)
   4083       uelasev(r)
   4084       # elasticity of cost of utility wrt utility, for EV calc. #;
   4085   Variable (all,h,HHLD)(all,r,REG)
   4086       ueprivhev(h,r)
   4087       # utility elasticity of private consn expenditure, for EV calc. #;
   4088   Variable (all,r,REG)
   4089       ueprivev(r)
   4090       # utility elasticity of private consn expenditure, for EV calc. #;
   4091   Variable (all,r,REG)
   4092       ugev(r) # per capita utility from gov't expend., for EV calc. #;
   4093   Variable (all,h,HHLD)(all,r,REG)
   4094       uphev(h,r) # per capita utility from private expend., for EV calc. #;
   4095   Variable (all,r,REG)
   4096       qsaveev(r) # total quantity of savings demanded, for EV calc. #;
   4097   Variable (all,r,REG)
   4098       yev(r) # regional household income in region r, for EV calc. #;
   4099   Variable (all,h,HHLD)(all,r,REG)
   4100       yphev(h,r)
   4101       # private consumption expenditure in region r, for EV calc. #;
   4102   Variable (all,r,REG)
   4103       ygev(r)
   4104       # government consumption expenditure in region r, for EV calc. #;
   4105    
   4106   Coefficient (all,r,REG)
   4107       INCOMEEV(r) # regional income, for EV calc. #;
   4108   Formula (initial) (all,r,REG)
   4109       INCOMEEV(r) = INCOME(r);
   4110   Update (all,r,REG)
   4111       INCOMEEV(r) = yev(r);
   4112    
   4113   Coefficient (all,h,HHLD)(all,r,REG)
   4114       UTILPRIVHEV(h,r) # utility from private consumption, for EV calcs #;
   4115   Formula (initial) (all,h,HHLD)(all,r,REG)
   4116       UTILPRIVHEV(h,r) = UTILPRIVH(h,r);
   4117   Update (all,h,HHLD)(all,r,REG)
   4118       UTILPRIVHEV(h,r) = uphev(h,r);
   4119    
   4120   Coefficient (all,r,REG)
   4121       UTILPRIVEV(r) # utility from private consumption #;
   4122   Formula (all,r,REG)
   4123       UTILPRIVEV(r) = sum(h, HHLD, PRIVEXPH(h,r)/PRIVEXP(r) * UTILPRIVHEV(h,r));
   4124    
   4125   Coefficient (all,r,REG)
   4126       UTILGOVEV(r) # utility from private consumption, for EV calcs #;
   4127   Formula (initial) (all,r,REG)
   4128       UTILGOVEV(r) = UTILGOV(r);
   4129   Update (all,r,REG)
   4130       UTILGOVEV(r) = ugev(r);
   4131    
   4132   Coefficient (all,r,REG)
   4133       UTILSAVEEV(r) # utility from private consumption, for EV calcs #;
   4134   Formula (initial) (all,r,REG)
   4135       UTILSAVEEV(r) = UTILSAVE(r);
   4136   Update (change) (all,r,REG)
   4137       UTILSAVEEV(r) = [[qsaveev(r) - pop(r)] / 100] * UTILSAVEEV(r);
   4138    
   4139   !<
   4140       B-1. Government Consumption Shadow Demand System
   4141       ------------------------------------------------
   4142   >!
   4143    
   4144   Equation GOVUSHD
   4145   # utility from government consumption in r #
   4146   (all,r,REG)
   4147       ygev(r) - pop(r) = ugev(r);
   4148    
   4149   !<
   4150       B-2. Private Consumption Shadow Demand System
   4151       ---------------------------------------------
   4152   >!
   4153    
   4154   Variable (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,h,HHLD)(all,r,REG)
   4155       qphev(i,h,r)
   4156       # private hhld demand for commodity i in region r, for EV calc. #;
   4157    
   4158   Coefficient (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,h,HHLD)(all,r,REG)
   4159       VPAHEV(i,h,r)
   4160       # private hhld expend. on i in r valued at agent's prices, for EV calc. #;
   4161   Formula (initial) (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,h,HHLD)(all,r,REG)
   4162       VPAHEV(i,h,r) = VPAH(i,h,r);
   4163   Update (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,h,HHLD)(all,r,REG)
   4164       VPAHEV(i,h,r) = qphev(i,h,r);
   4165    
   4166   Coefficient (all,h,HHLD)(all,r,REG)
   4167       VPAHREGEV(h,r) # private consumption expenditure in region r, for EV calc. #;
   4168   Formula (all,h,HHLD)(all,r,REG)
   4169       VPAHREGEV(h,r) = sum(i,TRAD_COMM, VPAHEV(i,h,r));
   4170   !<
   4171       VPAREGEV should agree with PRIVEXPEV.
   4172   >!
   4173    
   4174   Coefficient (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,h,HHLD)(all,r,REG)
   4175       CONSHRHEV(i,h,r)
   4176       # share of private hhld consn devoted to good i in r, for EV calc. #;
   4177   Formula (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,h,HHLD)(all,r,REG)
   4178       CONSHRHEV(i,h,r) = 0;
   4179   Formula (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,h,HHLD)(all,r,REG: VPAHREGEV(h,r)>0)
   4180       CONSHRHEV(i,h,r) = VPAHEV(i,h,r) / VPAHREGEV(h,r);
   4181   Coefficient (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,h,HHLD)(all,r,REG)
   4182       EYHEV(i,h,r)
   4183       # expend. elast. of private hhld demand for i in r, for EV calc. #;
   4184   Formula (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,h,HHLD)(all,r,REG)
   4185       EYHEV(i,h,r) = 0 ;
   4186   Formula (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,h,HHLD)(all,r,REG
   4187   : sum(n,TRAD_COMM, CONSHRHEV(n,h,r) * INCPAR(n,r))>0)
   4188       EYHEV(i,h,r)
   4189           = [1.0 / sum(n,TRAD_COMM, CONSHRHEV(n,h,r) * INCPAR(n,r))]
   4190           * [INCPAR(i,r) * [1.0 - ALPHA(i,r)]
   4191               + sum(n,TRAD_COMM, CONSHRHEV(n,h,r) * INCPAR(n,r) * ALPHA(n,r))]
   4192           + ALPHA(i,r)
   4193           - sum(n,TRAD_COMM, CONSHRHEV(n,h,r) * ALPHA(n,r));
   4194    
   4195   Equation PRIVDMNDSEV
   4196       # private hhld demands for composite commodities, for EV calc. #
   4197       (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,h,HHLD)(all,r,REG)
   4198       qphev(i,h,r) - poph(h,r) = EYHEV(i,h,r) * [yphev(h,r) - poph(h,r)];
   4199   !<
   4200       Prices are held constant for the EV calculation and so do not appear here.
   4201   >!
   4202    
   4203   Coefficient (all,h,HHLD)(all,r,REG)
   4204       UELASPRIVHEV(h,r)
   4205       # elast. of cost wrt utility from private consn, for EV calc. #;
   4206   Formula (all,h,HHLD)(all,r,REG)
   4207       UELASPRIVHEV(h,r) = sum(i,TRAD_COMM, CONSHRHEV(i,h,r) * INCPAR(i,r));
   4208   Formula (all,h,HHLD)(all,r,REG
   4209   : sum(i,TRAD_COMM, CONSHRHEV(i,h,r) * INCPAR(i,r))=0)
   4210       UELASPRIVHEV(h,r) = 1 ;
   4211    
   4212   Equation PRIVATEUEV
   4213   # computation of utility from private consumption in r (HT 45) #
   4214   (all,r,REG)(all,h,HHLD)
   4215       yphev(h,r) - pop(r) = UELASPRIVHEV(h,r) * uphev(h,r);
   4216    
   4217   Coefficient (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,h,HHLD)(all,r,REG)
   4218       XWCONSHRHEV(i,h,r)
   4219       # expansion-parameter-weighted consumption share, for EV calc. #;
   4220   Formula (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,h,HHLD)(all,r,REG)
   4221       XWCONSHRHEV(i,h,r) = 0;
   4222   Formula (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,h,HHLD)(all,r,REG: UELASPRIVHEV(h,r)>0)
   4223       XWCONSHRHEV(i,h,r) = CONSHRHEV(i,h,r) * INCPAR(i,r) / UELASPRIVHEV(h,r);
   4224    
   4225   Equation UTILELASPRIVHEV
   4226       # elasticity of cost wrt utility from private consn, for EV calc. #
   4227       (all,h,HHLD)(all,r,REG)
   4228       ueprivhev(h,r)
   4229           = sum(i,TRAD_COMM, XWCONSHRHEV(i,h,r) * [qphev(i,h,r) - yphev(h,r)]);
   4230    
   4231   Equation UTILELASPRIVEV
   4232       # elasticity of cost wrt utility from private consn, for EV calc. #
   4233       (all,r,REG)
   4234       ueprivev(r)
   4235           = sum(h, HHLD, VPAHREGEV(h,r)/sum(k, HHLD, VPAHREGEV(k,r))
   4236                 * ueprivhev(h,r));
   4237   !<
   4238       Prices are held constant for the EV calculation and so do not appear here.
   4239   >!
   4240    
   4241   !<
   4242    
   4243       B-3. Regional Household Shadow Demand System
   4244       --------------------------------------------
   4245   >!
   4246    
   4247   Variable (all,r,REG)
   4248       ysaveev(r) # NET savings expenditure, for EV calc. #;
   4249    
   4250   Coefficient (all,h,HHLD)(all,r,REG)
   4251       PRIVEXPHEV(h,r)
   4252       # private consumption expenditure in region r, for EV calc. #;
   4253   Formula (initial) (all,h,HHLD)(all,r,REG)
   4254       PRIVEXPHEV(h,r) = PRIVEXPH(h,r);
   4255   Update (all,h,HHLD)(all,r,REG)
   4256       PRIVEXPHEV(h,r) = yphev(h,r);
   4257    
   4258   Coefficient (all,r,REG)
   4259       PRIVEXPEV(r)
   4260       # private consumption expenditure in region r, for EV calc. #;
   4261   Formula (all,r,REG)
   4262       PRIVEXPEV(r) = sum(h, HHLD, PRIVEXPHEV(h,r));
   4263   !<
   4264       PRIVEXPEV should agree with VPAREGEV.
   4265   >!
   4266    
   4267   Coefficient (all,r,REG)
   4268       GOVEXPEV(r)
   4269       # government consumption expenditure in region r, for EV calc. #;
   4270   Formula (initial) (all,r,REG)
   4271       GOVEXPEV(r) = GOVEXP(r);
   4272   Update (all,r,REG)
   4273       GOVEXPEV(r) = ygev(r);
   4274    
   4275   Coefficient (all,r,REG)
   4276       SAVEEV(r)
   4277       # saving in region r, for EV calc. #;
   4278   Formula (initial) (all,r,REG)
   4279       SAVEEV(r) = SAVE(r);
   4280   Update (all,r,REG)
   4281       SAVEEV(r) = ysaveev(r);
   4282    
   4283   Coefficient (all,r,REG)
   4284       XSHRPRIVEV(r)
   4285       # private expenditure share in regional income, for EV calc. #;
   4286   Formula (all,r,REG)
   4287       XSHRPRIVEV(r) = PRIVEXPEV(r) / INCOMEEV(r);
   4288    
   4289   Coefficient (all,r,REG)
   4290       XSHRGOVEV(r)
   4291       # government expenditure share in regional income, for EV calc. #;
   4292   Formula (all,r,REG)
   4293       XSHRGOVEV(r) = GOVEXPEV(r) / INCOMEEV(r);
   4294    
   4295   Coefficient (all,r,REG)
   4296       XSHRSAVEEV(r) # saving share in regional income, for EV calc. #;
   4297   Formula (all,r,REG)
   4298       XSHRSAVEEV(r) = SAVEEV(r) / INCOMEEV(r);
   4299    
   4300   Variable (all,r,REG)
   4301       dpavev(r) # average distribution parameter shift, for EV calc. #;
   4302   Equation DPARAVEV
   4303   # average distribution parameter shift, for EV calc. #
   4304       (all,r,REG)
   4305       dpavev(r)
   4306           = XSHRPRIVEV(r) * dppriv(r)
   4307           + XSHRGOVEV(r) * dpgov(r)
   4308           + XSHRSAVEEV(r) * dpsave(r);
   4309    
   4310   Equation UTILITELASTICEV
   4311       # elasticity of cost of utility wrt utility, for EV calc. #
   4312       (all,r,REG)
   4313       uelasev(r) = XSHRPRIV(r) * ueprivev(r) - dpavev(r);
   4314    
   4315   Equation PCONSEXPEV
   4316   # private consumption expenditure, for EV calc. #
   4317       (all,h,HHLD)(all,r,REG)
   4318       yphev(h,r) - yev(r) = -[ueprivhev(h,r) - uelasev(r)] + dpprivh(h,r);
   4319    
   4320   Equation GOVCONSEXPEV
   4321   # government consumption expenditure #
   4322   (all,r,REG)
   4323       ygev(r) - yev(r) = uelasev(r) + dpgov(r);
   4324    
   4325   Equation SAVINGEV
   4326   # saving #
   4327   (all,r,REG)
   4328       ysaveev(r) - yev(r) = uelasev(r) + dpsave(r);
   4329    
   4330   Equation SAVEUEV
   4331   # saving #
   4332   (all,r,REG)
   4333       qsaveev(r) = ysaveev(r);
   4334    
   4335   !<
   4336       Note that because psave doesn't change, qsaveev moves with ysaveev.
   4337   >!
   4338    
   4339   Coefficient (all,r,REG)
   4340       UTILELASEV(r)
   4341       # elasticity of cost of utility wrt utility, for EV calc. #;
   4342   Formula (initial) (all,r,REG)
   4343       UTILELASEV(r) = UTILELAS(r);
   4344   Update (all,r,REG)
   4345       UTILELASEV(r) = uelasev(r);
   4346    
   4347   Equation INCOME_EQUIV
   4348   # equivalent income #
   4349   (all,r,REG)
   4350       u(r)
   4351           = au(r)
   4352           + DPARPRIV(r) * loge(UTILPRIVEV(r)) * dppriv(r)
   4353           + DPARGOV(r) * loge(UTILGOVEV(r)) * dpgov(r)
   4354           + DPARSAVE(r) * loge(UTILSAVEEV(r)) * dpsave(r)
   4355           + [1.0 / UTILELASEV(r)] * [yev(r) - pop(r)];
   4356    
   4357   !<
   4358       B-4. Equivalent Variation
   4359       -------------------------
   4360   >!
   4361    
   4362   Variable (change)(all,r,REG)
   4363       EV(r) # equivalent variation, $ US million #;
   4364   Equation EVREG
   4365   # regional EV (HT 67) #
   4366   (all,r,REG)
   4367       EV(r) = [INCOMEEV(r) / 100] * yev(r);
   4368    
   4369   Variable (change)
   4370       WEV # equivalent variation for the world #;
   4371   Equation EVWLD
   4372   # EV for the world (HT 68) #
   4373       WEV = sum(r,REG, EV(r));
   4374    
   4375   !<
   4376       ------------------------
   4377       C. Welfare Decomposition
   4378       ------------------------
   4379       See GTAP Technical Paper No. 5 for derivation and interpretation.
   4380   >!
   4381    
   4382   Coefficient (all,r,REG)
   4383       EVSCALFACT(r) # equivalent variation scaling factor #;
   4384   Formula (all,r,REG)
   4385       EVSCALFACT(r) = [UTILELASEV(r) / UTILELAS(r)] * [INCOMEEV(r) / INCOME(r)];
   4386    
   4387   Coefficient (all,m,MARG_COMM)(all,s,REG)
   4388       VTMD(m,s) # aggregate value of svce m in shipments to s #;
   4389   Formula (all,m,MARG_COMM)(all,s,REG)
   4390       VTMD(m,s) = sum(i,TRAD_COMM, sum(r,REG, VTMFSD(m,i,r,s)));
   4391    
   4392   Variable (linear,change)(all,r,REG)
   4393       EV_ALT(r) # regional EV computed in alternative way #;
   4394   Equation EV_DECOMPOSITION
   4395   # decomposition of Equivalent Variation #
   4396   (all,r,REG)
   4397       EV_ALT(r)
   4398           = -[0.01 * UTILELASEV(r) * INCOMEEV(r)]
   4399           * [DPARPRIV(r) * loge(UTILPRIVEV(r) / UTILPRIV(r)) * dppriv(r)
   4400               + DPARGOV(r) * loge(UTILGOVEV(r) / UTILGOV(r)) * dpgov(r)
   4401               + DPARSAVE(r) * loge(UTILSAVEEV(r) / UTILSAVE(r)) * dpsave(r)]
   4402           + [0.01 * EVSCALFACT(r)]
   4403           * [sum(i,NSAV_COMM, PTAX(i,r) * [qo(i,r) - pop(r)])
   4404               + sum(i,ENDW_COMM, sum(j,PROD_COMM,
   4405                   ETAX(i,j,r) * [qfe(i,j,r) - pop(r)]))
   4406               + sum(i,TRAD_COMM, sum(j,PROD_COMM,
   4407                   IFTAX(i,j,r) * [qfm(i,j,r) - pop(r)]))
   4408               + sum(i,TRAD_COMM, sum(j,PROD_COMM,
   4409                   DFTAX(i,j,r) * [qfd(i,j,r) - pop(r)]))
   4410               + sum(i,TRAD_COMM, sum(h, HHLD,
   4411                   IPTAX(i,h,r) * [qpmh(i,h,r) - poph(h,r)]))
   4412               + sum(i,TRAD_COMM, sum(h, HHLD,
   4413                   DPTAX(i,h,r) * [qpdh(i,h,r) - poph(h,r)]))
   4414               + sum(i,TRAD_COMM, IGTAX(i,r) * [qgm(i,r) - pop(r)])
   4415               + sum(i,TRAD_COMM, DGTAX(i,r) * [qgd(i,r) - pop(r)])
   4416               + sum(i,TRAD_COMM, sum(s,REG, XTAXD(i,r,s) * [qxs(i,r,s) - pop(r)]))
   4417               + sum(i,TRAD_COMM, sum(s,REG, MTAX(i,s,r) * [qxs(i,s,r) - pop(r)]))
   4418               + sum(i,ENDW_COMM, VOA(i,r) * [qo(i,r) - pop(r)])
   4419               - VDEP(r) * [kb(r) - pop(r)]
   4420               + sum(h, HHLD, REMI(h,r) * (remih(h,r) - poph(h,r)))
   4421               - sum(h, HHLD, REMO(h,r) * (remoh(h,r) - poph(h,r)))
   4422               + sum(h, HHLD, FYI(h,r) * (fyih(h,r) - poph(h,r)))
   4423               - sum(h, HHLD, FYO(h,r) * (fyoh(h,r) - poph(h,r)))
   4424               + AIDI(r) * (aidin(r) - pop(r)) - AIDO(r) * (aidout(r) - pop(r))
   4425               + sum(i,PROD_COMM, VOA(i,r) * ao(i,r))
   4426               + sum(j,PROD_COMM, VVA(j,r) * ava(j,r))
   4427               + sum(j,PROD_COMM, sum(i,ENDW_COMM, VFA(i,j,r) * afe(i,j,r)))
   4428               + sum(j,PROD_COMM, sum(i,TRAD_COMM, VFA(i,j,r) * af(i,j,r)))
   4429               + sum(m,MARG_COMM, sum(i,TRAD_COMM, sum(s,REG,
   4430                   VTMFSD(m,i,s,r) * atmfsd(m,i,s,r))))
   4431               + sum(i,TRAD_COMM, sum(s,REG, VIMS(i,s,r) * ams(i,s,r)))
   4432               + sum(i,TRAD_COMM, sum(s,REG, VXWD(i,r,s) * pfob(i,r,s)))
   4433               + sum(m,MARG_COMM, VST(m,r) * pm(m,r))
   4434               + NETINV(r) * pcgds(r)
   4435               - sum(i,TRAD_COMM, sum(s,REG, VXWD(i,s,r) * pfob(i,s,r)))
   4436               - sum(m,MARG_COMM, VTMD(m,r) * pt(m))
   4437               - SAVE(r) * psave(r)]
   4438           + 0.01 * [sum(i,NSAV_COMM, PTAX(i,r) * [pop(r)])
   4439               + sum(i,ENDW_COMM, sum(j,PROD_COMM,
   4440                   ETAX(i,j,r) * [pop(r)]))
   4441               + sum(i,TRAD_COMM, sum(j,PROD_COMM,
   4442                   IFTAX(i,j,r) * [pop(r)]))
   4443               + sum(i,TRAD_COMM, sum(j,PROD_COMM,
   4444                   DFTAX(i,j,r) * [pop(r)]))
   4445               + sum(i,TRAD_COMM, sum(h, HHLD,
   4446                   IPTAX(i,h,r) * [poph(h,r)]))
   4447               + sum(i,TRAD_COMM, sum(h, HHLD,
   4448                   DPTAX(i,h,r) * [poph(h,r)]))
   4449               + sum(i,TRAD_COMM, IGTAX(i,r) * [pop(r)])
   4450               + sum(i,TRAD_COMM, DGTAX(i,r) * [pop(r)])
   4451               + sum(i,TRAD_COMM, sum(s,REG, XTAXD(i,r,s) * [pop(r)]))
   4452               + sum(i,TRAD_COMM, sum(s,REG, MTAX(i,s,r) * [pop(r)]))
   4453               + sum(i,ENDW_COMM, VOA(i,r) * [pop(r)])
   4454               - VDEP(r) * [pop(r)]
   4455               + sum(h, HHLD, REMI(h,r) * (poph(h,r)))
   4456               - sum(h, HHLD, REMO(h,r) * (poph(h,r)))
   4457               + sum(h, HHLD, FYI(h,r) * (poph(h,r)))
   4458               - sum(h, HHLD, FYO(h,r) * (poph(h,r)))
   4459               + AIDI(r) * (pop(r)) - AIDO(r) * (pop(r))];
   4460    
   4461   Variable (linear,change)
   4462       WEV_ALT # expression for WEV computed in alternative way #;
   4463   Equation WORLDEV
   4464   # Equivalent Variation for the world #
   4465       WEV_ALT = sum(r,REG, EV_ALT(r));
   4466    
   4467   Variable (linear,change) (all,r,REG)
   4468       CNTdpar(r) # contribution to EV of change in distribution parameters #;
   4469   Equation CNT_WEV_dpar
   4470   (all,r,REG)
   4471       CNTdpar(r)
   4472           = -[0.01 * UTILELASEV(r) * INCOMEEV(r)]
   4473           * [DPARPRIV(r) * loge(UTILPRIVEV(r) / UTILPRIV(r)) * dppriv(r)
   4474               + DPARGOV(r) * loge(UTILGOVEV(r) / UTILGOV(r)) * dpgov(r)
   4475               + DPARSAVE(r) * loge(UTILSAVEEV(r) / UTILSAVE(r)) * dpsave(r)];
   4476    
   4477   Variable (linear,change) (all,r,REG)
   4478       CNTpopr(r) # contribution to EV in region r of change in population #;
   4479   Equation CONT_EV_pop
   4480   (all,r,REG)
   4481       CNTpopr(r) = 0.01 * [sum(i,NSAV_COMM, PTAX(i,r) * [pop(r)])
   4482               + sum(i,ENDW_COMM, sum(j,PROD_COMM,
   4483                   ETAX(i,j,r) * [pop(r)]))
   4484               + sum(i,TRAD_COMM, sum(j,PROD_COMM,
   4485                   IFTAX(i,j,r) * [pop(r)]))
   4486               + sum(i,TRAD_COMM, sum(j,PROD_COMM,
   4487                   DFTAX(i,j,r) * [pop(r)]))
   4488               + sum(i,TRAD_COMM, sum(h, HHLD,
   4489                   IPTAX(i,h,r) * [poph(h,r)]))
   4490               + sum(i,TRAD_COMM, sum(h, HHLD,
   4491                   DPTAX(i,h,r) * [poph(h,r)]))
   4492               + sum(i,TRAD_COMM, IGTAX(i,r) * [pop(r)])
   4493               + sum(i,TRAD_COMM, DGTAX(i,r) * [pop(r)])
   4494               + sum(i,TRAD_COMM, sum(s,REG, XTAXD(i,r,s) * [pop(r)]))
   4495               + sum(i,TRAD_COMM, sum(s,REG, MTAX(i,s,r) * [pop(r)]))
   4496               + sum(i,ENDW_COMM, VOA(i,r) * [pop(r)])
   4497               - VDEP(r) * [pop(r)]
   4498               + sum(h, HHLD, REMI(h,r) * (poph(h,r)))
   4499               - sum(h, HHLD, REMO(h,r) * (poph(h,r)))
   4500               + sum(h, HHLD, FYI(h,r) * (poph(h,r)))
   4501               - sum(h, HHLD, FYO(h,r) * (poph(h,r)))
   4502               + AIDI(r) * (pop(r)) - AIDO(r) * (pop(r))];
   4503    
   4504   Variable (linear,change) (all,r,REG)
   4505       CNTqor(r) # contribution to EV in region r of output changes #;
   4506   Equation CONT_EV_qor
   4507   (all,r,REG)
   4508       CNTqor(r)
   4509           = sum(i,NSAV_COMM,
   4510               0.01 * EVSCALFACT(r) * PTAX(i,r) * [qo(i,r) - pop(r)]);
   4511    
   4512   Variable (linear,change) (all,i,NSAV_COMM)(all,r,REG)
   4513       CNTqoir(i,r)
   4514       # contribution to EV of changes in output of NSAV_COMM i in reg. r #;
   4515   Equation CONT_EV_qoir
   4516   (all,i,NSAV_COMM)(all,r,REG)
   4517       CNTqoir(i,r) = PTAX(i,r) * [0.01 * EVSCALFACT(r)] * [qo(i,r) - pop(r)];
   4518    
   4519   Variable (linear,change) (all,r,REG)
   4520       CNTqfer(r)
   4521       # cont. to EV of changes in use of all ENDW_COMM in all ind. in reg. r #;
   4522   Equation CONT_EV_qfer
   4523   (all,r,REG)
   4524       CNTqfer(r)
   4525           = sum(i,ENDW_COMM, sum(j,PROD_COMM,
   4526               ETAX(i,j,r) * [0.01 * EVSCALFACT(r)] * [qfe(i,j,r) - pop(r)]));
   4527    
   4528   Variable (linear,change) (all,i,ENDW_COMM)(all,r,REG)
   4529       CNTqfeir(i,r)
   4530       # contribution to EV of changes in use of ENDW_COMM i in all ind. in r #;
   4531   Equation CONT_EV_qfeir
   4532   (all,i,ENDW_COMM)(all,r,REG)
   4533       CNTqfeir(i,r)
   4534           = sum(j,PROD_COMM,
   4535               ETAX(i,j,r) * [0.01 * EVSCALFACT(r)] * [qfe(i,j,r) - pop(r)]);
   4536    
   4537   Variable (linear,change) (all,i,ENDW_COMM)(all,j,PROD_COMM)(all,r,REG)
   4538       CNTqfeijr(i,j,r)
   4539       # cont. to EV of changes in use of ENDW_COMM i in ind. j of reg. r #;
   4540   Equation CONT_EV_qfeijr
   4541   (all,i,ENDW_COMM)(all,j,PROD_COMM)(all,r,REG)
   4542       CNTqfeijr(i,j,r)
   4543           = ETAX(i,j,r) * [0.01 * EVSCALFACT(r)] * [qfe(i,j,r) - pop(r)];
   4544    
   4545   Variable (linear,change) (all,r,REG)
   4546       CNTqfmr(r)
   4547       # cont. to EV of changes in use of imported int. in all ind. in reg. r #;
   4548   Equation CONT_EV_qfmr
   4549   (all,r,REG)
   4550       CNTqfmr(r)
   4551           = sum(i,TRAD_COMM, sum(j,PROD_COMM,
   4552               IFTAX(i,j,r) * [0.01 * EVSCALFACT(r)] * [qfm(i,j,r) - pop(r)]));
   4553    
   4554   Variable (linear,change) (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,r,REG)
   4555       CNTqfmir(i,r)
   4556       # cont. to EV of changes in use of imported int. i in all ind. in r #;
   4557   Equation CONT_EV_qfmir
   4558   (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,r,REG)
   4559       CNTqfmir(i,r)
   4560           = sum(j,PROD_COMM,
   4561               IFTAX(i,j,r) * [0.01 * EVSCALFACT(r)] * [qfm(i,j,r) - pop(r)]);
   4562    
   4563   Variable (linear,change) (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,j,PROD_COMM)(all,r,REG)
   4564       CNTqfmijr(i,j,r)
   4565       # cont. to EV of changes in use of imported int. i in ind. j of reg. r #;
   4566   Equation CONT_EV_qfmijr
   4567   (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,j,PROD_COMM)(all,r,REG)
   4568       CNTqfmijr(i,j,r)
   4569           = IFTAX(i,j,r) * [0.01 * EVSCALFACT(r)] * [qfm(i,j,r) - pop(r)];
   4570    
   4571   Variable (linear,change) (all,r,REG)
   4572       CNTqfdr(r)
   4573       # cont. to EV of changes in use of domestic int. in all ind. in reg. r #;
   4574   Equation CONT_EV_qfdr
   4575   (all,r,REG)
   4576       CNTqfdr(r)
   4577           = sum(i,TRAD_COMM, sum(j,PROD_COMM,
   4578               DFTAX(i,j,r) * [0.01 * EVSCALFACT(r)] * [qfd(i,j,r) - pop(r)]));
   4579    
   4580   Variable (linear,change) (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,r,REG)
   4581       CNTqfdir(i,r)
   4582       # contribution to EV of changes in use of domestic i in all ind. in r #;
   4583   Equation CONT_EV_qfdir
   4584   (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,r,REG)
   4585       CNTqfdir(i,r)
   4586           = sum(j,PROD_COMM,
   4587               DFTAX(i,j,r) * [0.01 * EVSCALFACT(r)] * [qfd(i,j,r) - pop(r)]);
   4588    
   4589   Variable (linear,change) (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,j,PROD_COMM)(all,r,REG)
   4590       CNTqfdijr(i,j,r)
   4591       # cont. to EV of changes in use of domestic int. i in ind. j of reg. r #;
   4592   Equation CONT_EV_qfdijr
   4593   (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,j,PROD_COMM)(all,r,REG)
   4594       CNTqfdijr(i,j,r)
   4595           = DFTAX(i,j,r) * [0.01 * EVSCALFACT(r)] * [qfd(i,j,r) - pop(r)];
   4596    
   4597   Variable (linear,change) (all,r,REG)
   4598       CNTqpmr(r)
   4599       # contribution to EV of changes in consumption of imported goods in r #;
   4600   Equation CONT_EV_qpmr
   4601   (all,r,REG)
   4602       CNTqpmr(r)
   4603           = sum(i,TRAD_COMM, sum(h, HHLD,
   4604               IPTAX(i,h,r) * [0.01 * EVSCALFACT(r)] * [qpmh(i,h,r) - poph(h,r)]));
   4605    
   4606   Variable (linear,change) (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,r,REG)
   4607       CNTqpmir(i,r)
   4608       # cont. to EV of changes in consumption of imported good i in reg. r #;
   4609   Equation CONT_EV_qpmir
   4610   (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,r,REG)
   4611       CNTqpmir(i,r) = sum(h, HHLD, IPTAX(i,h,r)
   4612                     * [0.01 * EVSCALFACT(r)] * [qpmh(i,h,r) - poph(h,r)]);
   4613    
   4614   Variable (linear,change) (all,r,REG)
   4615       CNTqpdr(r)
   4616       # contribution to EV of changes in consumption of domestic goods in r #;
   4617   Equation CONT_EV_qpdr
   4618   (all,r,REG)
   4619       CNTqpdr(r)
   4620           = sum(i,TRAD_COMM, sum(h, HHLD,
   4621               DPTAX(i,h,r) * [0.01 * EVSCALFACT(r)] * [qpdh(i,h,r) - poph(h,r)]));
   4622    
   4623   Variable (linear,change) (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,r,REG)
   4624       CNTqpdir(i,r)
   4625       # cont. to EV of changes in consumption of domestic good i in reg. r #;
   4626   Equation CONT_EV_qpdir
   4627   (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,r,REG)
   4628       CNTqpdir(i,r) = sum(h, HHLD, DPTAX(i,h,r)
   4629                    * [0.01 * EVSCALFACT(r)] * [qpdh(i,h,r) - poph(h,r)]);
   4630    
   4631   Variable (linear,change) (all,r,REG)
   4632       CNTqgmr(r)
   4633       # cont. to EV of changes in gov't consumption of imports in reg. r #;
   4634   Equation CONT_EV_qgmr
   4635   (all,r,REG)
   4636       CNTqgmr(r)
   4637           = sum(i,TRAD_COMM,
   4638               IGTAX(i,r) * [0.01 * EVSCALFACT(r)] * [qgm(i,r) - pop(r)]);
   4639    
   4640   Variable (linear,change) (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,r,REG)
   4641       CNTqgmir(i,r)
   4642       # cont. to EV of changes in gov't consumption of import i in reg. r #;
   4643   Equation CONT_EV_qgmir
   4644   (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,r,REG)
   4645       CNTqgmir(i,r) = IGTAX(i,r) * [0.01 * EVSCALFACT(r)] * [qgm(i,r) - pop(r)];
   4646    
   4647   Variable (linear,change) (all,r,REG)
   4648       CNTqgdr(r)
   4649       # cont. to EV of changes in gov't consumption of domestics in reg. r #;
   4650   Equation CONT_EV_qgdr
   4651   (all,r,REG)
   4652       CNTqgdr(r)
   4653           = sum(i,TRAD_COMM,
   4654               DGTAX(i,r) * [0.01 * EVSCALFACT(r)] * [qgd(i,r) - pop(r)]);
   4655    
   4656   Variable (linear,change) (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,r,REG)
   4657       CNTqgdir(i,r)
   4658       # cont. to EV of changes in gov't consumption of domestic i in reg. r #;
   4659   Equation CONT_EV_qgdir
   4660   (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,r,REG)
   4661       CNTqgdir(i,r) = DGTAX(i,r) * [0.01 * EVSCALFACT(r)] * [qgd(i,r) - pop(r)];
   4662    
   4663   Variable (linear,change) (all,r,REG)
   4664       CNTqxsr(r)
   4665       # cont. to EV of changes in exports of all goods from SRCE r to all DEST #;
   4666   Equation CONT_EV_qxsr
   4667   (all,r,REG)
   4668       CNTqxsr(r)
   4669           = sum(i,TRAD_COMM, sum(s,REG,
   4670               XTAXD(i,r,s) * [0.01 * EVSCALFACT(r)] * [qxs(i,r,s) - pop(r)]));
   4671    
   4672   Variable (linear,change) (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,r,REG)(all,s,REG)
   4673       CNTqxsirs(i,r,s)
   4674       # cont. to EV of changes in exports of i from SRCE r to DEST s #;
   4675   Equation CONT_EV_qxsirs
   4676   (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,r,REG)(all,s,REG)
   4677       CNTqxsirs(i,r,s)
   4678           = XTAXD(i,r,s) * [0.01 * EVSCALFACT(r)] * [qxs(i,r,s) - pop(r)];
   4679    
   4680   Variable (linear,change) (all,r,REG)
   4681       CNTqimr(r)
   4682       # cont. to EV of changes in imports of all goods from all SRCE to DEST r #;
   4683   Equation CONT_EV_qimr
   4684   (all,r,REG)
   4685       CNTqimr(r)
   4686           = sum(i,TRAD_COMM, sum(s,REG,
   4687               MTAX(i,s,r) * [0.01 * EVSCALFACT(r)] * [qxs(i,s,r) - pop(r)]));
   4688    
   4689   Variable (linear,change) (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,s,REG)(all,r,REG)
   4690       CNTqimisr(i,s,r)
   4691       # cont. to EV of changes in imports of i from SRCE s to DEST r #;
   4692   Equation CONT_EV_qimisr
   4693   (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,s,REG)(all,r,REG)
   4694       CNTqimisr(i,s,r)
   4695           = MTAX(i,s,r) * [0.01 * EVSCALFACT(r)] * [qxs(i,s,r) - pop(r)];
   4696    
   4697   Variable (linear,change) (all,r,REG)
   4698       CNTalleffr(r) # total contribution to regional EV of allocative effects #;
   4699   Equation CONT_EV_alleffr
   4700   (all,r,REG)
   4701       CNTalleffr(r)
   4702           = [0.01 * EVSCALFACT(r)]
   4703           * [sum(i,NSAV_COMM, PTAX(i,r) * [qo(i,r) - pop(r)])
   4704             + sum(i,ENDW_COMM, sum(j,PROD_COMM,
   4705                   ETAX(i,j,r) * [qfe(i,j,r) - pop(r)]))
   4706             + sum(i,TRAD_COMM, sum(j,PROD_COMM,
   4707                   IFTAX(i,j,r) * [qfm(i,j,r) - pop(r)]))
   4708             + sum(i,TRAD_COMM, sum(j,PROD_COMM,
   4709                   DFTAX(i,j,r) * [qfd(i,j,r) - pop(r)]))
   4710             + sum(i,TRAD_COMM, sum(h, HHLD,
   4711                   IPTAX(i,h,r) * [qpmh(i,h,r) - poph(h,r)]))
   4712             + sum(i,TRAD_COMM, sum(h, HHLD,
   4713                   DPTAX(i,h,r) * [qpdh(i,h,r) - poph(h,r)]))
   4714             + sum(i,TRAD_COMM, IGTAX(i,r) * [qgm(i,r) - pop(r)])
   4715             + sum(i,TRAD_COMM, DGTAX(i,r) * [qgd(i,r) - pop(r)])
   4716             + sum(i,TRAD_COMM, sum(s,REG, XTAXD(i,r,s) * [qxs(i,r,s) - pop(r)]))
   4717             + sum(i,TRAD_COMM, sum(s,REG, MTAX(i,s,r) * [qxs(i,s,r) - pop(r)]))];
   4718    
   4719   Variable (linear,change) (all,i,DEMD_COMM)(all,r,REG)
   4720       CNTalleffir(i,r)
   4721       # total contribution to regional EV of allocative effects #;
   4722   Equation CONT_EV_alleffir_E
   4723   (all,i,ENDW_COMM)(all,r,REG)
   4724       CNTalleffir(i,r)
   4725           = [0.01 * EVSCALFACT(r)]
   4726           * [PTAX(i,r) * [qo(i,r) - pop(r)]
   4727               + sum(j,PROD_COMM, ETAX(i,j,r) * [qfe(i,j,r) - pop(r)])];
   4728   Equation CONT_EV_alleffir_T
   4729   (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,r,REG)
   4730       CNTalleffir(i,r)
   4731           = [0.01 * EVSCALFACT(r)]
   4732           * [PTAX(i,r) * [qo(i,r) - pop(r)]
   4733               + sum(j,PROD_COMM, IFTAX(i,j,r) * [qfm(i,j,r) - pop(r)])
   4734               + sum(j,PROD_COMM, DFTAX(i,j,r) * [qfd(i,j,r) - pop(r)])
   4735               + sum(h, HHLD, IPTAX(i,h,r) * [qpmh(i,h,r) - poph(h,r)])
   4736               + sum(h, HHLD, DPTAX(i,h,r) * [qpdh(i,h,r) - poph(h,r)])
   4737               + IGTAX(i,r) * [qgm(i,r) - pop(r)]
   4738               + DGTAX(i,r) * [qgd(i,r) - pop(r)]
   4739               + sum(s,REG, XTAXD(i,r,s) * [qxs(i,r,s) - pop(r)])
   4740               + sum(s,REG, MTAX(i,s,r) * [qxs(i,s,r) - pop(r)])];
   4741    
   4742   Variable (linear,change) (all,r,REG)
   4743       CNTtotr(r)
   4744       # contribution to regional EV of changes in its terms of trade #;
   4745   Equation CONT_EV_totr
   4746   (all,r,REG)
   4747       CNTtotr(r)
   4748           = [0.01 * EVSCALFACT(r)]
   4749           * [ sum(i,TRAD_COMM, sum(s,REG, VXWD(i,r,s) * pfob(i,r,s)))
   4750               + sum(m,MARG_COMM, VST(m,r) * pm(m,r))
   4751               - sum(i,TRAD_COMM, sum(s,REG, VXWD(i,s,r) * pfob(i,s,r)))
   4752               - sum(m,MARG_COMM, VTMD(m,r) * pt(m))] ;
   4753    
   4754   Variable (linear,change) (all,r,REG)
   4755       CNTcgdsr(r) # contribution to regional EV of changes in the price of cgds #;
   4756   Equation CNT_EV_cgdsr
   4757   (all,r,REG)
   4758       CNTcgdsr(r)
   4759           = [0.01 * EVSCALFACT(r)]
   4760           * [ NETINV(r) * pcgds(r)
   4761               - SAVE(r) * psave(r)];
   4762    
   4763   Variable (linear,change) (all,r,REG)
   4764       CNTendwr(r) # contribution to regional EV of changes in all ENDW_COMM #;
   4765   Equation CONT_EV_endwr
   4766   (all,r,REG)
   4767       CNTendwr(r)
   4768           = [0.01 * EVSCALFACT(r)]
   4769           * [ sum(i,ENDW_COMM, VOA(i,r) * [qo(i,r) - pop(r)])
   4770               - VDEP(r) * [kb(r) - pop(r)]];
   4771    
   4772   Variable (linear,change) (all,i,ENDW_COMM)(all,r,REG)
   4773       CNTendwir(i,r) # contribution to regional EV of changes in ENDW_COMM i #;
   4774   Equation CONT_EV_endwir
   4775   (all,i,ENDW_COMM)(all,r,REG)
   4776       CNTendwir(i,r) = [0.01 * EVSCALFACT(r)] * [VOA(i,r) * [qo(i,r) - pop(r)]];
   4777    
   4778   Variable (linear,change) (all,r,REG)
   4779       CNTtechr(r) # contribution to regional EV of all technical change #;
   4780   Equation CONT_EV_techr
   4781   (all,r,REG)
   4782       CNTtechr(r)
   4783           = [0.01 * EVSCALFACT(r)]
   4784           * [ sum(i,PROD_COMM, VOA(i,r) * ao(i,r))
   4785               + sum(j,PROD_COMM, VVA(j,r) * ava(j,r))
   4786               + sum(j,PROD_COMM, sum(i,ENDW_COMM, VFA(i,j,r) * afe(i,j,r)))
   4787               + sum(j,PROD_COMM, sum(i,TRAD_COMM, VFA(i,j,r) * af(i,j,r)))
   4788               + sum(m,MARG_COMM, sum(i,TRAD_COMM, sum(s,REG,
   4789                   VTMFSD(m,i,s,r) * atmfsd(m,i,s,r))))
   4790               + sum(i,TRAD_COMM, sum(s,REG, VIMS(i,s,r) * ams(i,s,r)))] ;
   4791    
   4792   Variable (linear,change) (all,r,REG)
   4793       CNTtech_aor(r)
   4794       # contribution to regional EV of output augmenting technical change #;
   4795   Equation CONT_EV_tech_aor
   4796   (all,r,REG)
   4797       CNTtech_aor(r)
   4798           = [0.01 * EVSCALFACT(r)] * sum(i,PROD_COMM, VOA(i,r) * ao(i,r));
   4799    
   4800   Variable (linear,change) (all,i,PROD_COMM)(all,r,REG)
   4801       CNTtech_aoir(i,r)
   4802       # cont. to regional EV of output augmenting tech change in TRAD_COMM i #;
   4803   Equation CONT_EV_tech_aoir
   4804   (all,i,PROD_COMM)(all,r,REG)
   4805       CNTtech_aoir(i,r) = [0.01 * EVSCALFACT(r)] * VOA(i,r) * ao(i,r);
   4806    
   4807   Variable (linear,change) (all,r,REG)
   4808       CNTtech_afer(r)
   4809       # contribution to regional EV of primary factor augmenting tech change #;
   4810   Equation CONT_EV_tech_afer
   4811   (all,r,REG)
   4812       CNTtech_afer(r)
   4813           = [0.01 * EVSCALFACT(r)]
   4814           * sum(j,PROD_COMM, sum(i,ENDW_COMM, VFA(i,j,r) * afe(i,j,r)));
   4815    
   4816   Variable (linear,change) (all,i,ENDW_COMM)(all,j,PROD_COMM)(all,r,REG)
   4817       CNTtech_afeijr(i,j,r)
   4818       # cont. to EV of primary factor i augmenting tech change in sector j #;
   4819   Equation CONT_EV_tech_afeijr
   4820   (all,i,ENDW_COMM)(all,j,PROD_COMM)(all,r,REG)
   4821       CNTtech_afeijr(i,j,r) = [0.01 * EVSCALFACT(r)] * VFA(i,j,r) * afe(i,j,r);
   4822    
   4823   Variable (linear,change) (all,r,REG)
   4824       CNTtech_avar(r)
   4825       # contribution to regional EV of value added augmenting tech change #;
   4826   Equation CONT_EV_tech_avar
   4827   (all,r,REG)
   4828       CNTtech_avar(r)
   4829           = [0.01 * EVSCALFACT(r)] * sum(j,PROD_COMM, VVA(j,r) * ava(j,r));
   4830    
   4831   Variable (linear,change) (all,j,PROD_COMM)(all,r,REG)
   4832       CNTtech_avajr(j,r)
   4833       # cont. to EV of value added augmenting tech change in sector j #;
   4834   Equation CONT_EV_tech_avajr
   4835   (all,j,PROD_COMM)(all,r,REG)
   4836       CNTtech_avajr(j,r) = [0.01 * EVSCALFACT(r)] * VVA(j,r) * ava(j,r);
   4837    
   4838   Variable (linear,change) (all,r,REG)
   4839       CNTtech_afr(r)
   4840       # cont. to regional EV of comp. int. input augmenting tech change #;
   4841   Equation CONT_EV_tech_afr
   4842   (all,r,REG)
   4843       CNTtech_afr(r)
   4844           = [0.01 * EVSCALFACT(r)]
   4845           * sum(j,PROD_COMM, sum(i,TRAD_COMM,
   4846               [VIFA(i,j,r) + VDFA(i,j,r)] * af(i,j,r)));
   4847    
   4848   Variable (linear,change) (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,j,PROD_COMM)(all,r,REG)
   4849       CNTtech_afijr(i,j,r)
   4850       # cont. to EV of composite i input augmenting tech change in sector j #;
   4851   Equation CONT_EV_tech_afijr
   4852   (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,j,PROD_COMM)(all,r,REG)
   4853       CNTtech_afijr(i,j,r)
   4854           = [0.01 * EVSCALFACT(r)] * [VIFA(i,j,r) + VDFA(i,j,r)] * af(i,j,r);
   4855    
   4856   Variable (linear,change) (all,r,REG)
   4857       CNTtech_atrr(r)
   4858       # contribution to regional EV of technical change in transportation #;
   4859   Equation CONT_EV_tech_atrr
   4860   (all,r,REG)
   4861       CNTtech_atrr(r)
   4862           = [0.01 * EVSCALFACT(r)]
   4863           * sum(m,MARG_COMM, sum(i,TRAD_COMM, sum(s,REG,
   4864               VTMFSD(m,i,s,r) * atmfsd(m,i,s,r))));
   4865    
   4866   Variable (linear,change)(all,m,MARG_COMM)(all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,r,REG)(all,s,REG)
   4867       CNTtech_afmfdsd(m,i,r,s)
   4868       # cont. to EV of tech change in transportation efficiency #;
   4869   Equation CONT_EV_tech_afmfdsd
   4870   (all,m,MARG_COMM)(all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,r,REG)(all,s,REG)
   4871       CNTtech_afmfdsd(m,i,r,s)
   4872           = [0.01 * EVSCALFACT(s)] * VTMFSD(m,i,r,s) * atmfsd(m,i,r,s);
   4873    
   4874   Variable (linear,change)(all,r,REG)
   4875       CNTtech_amsr(r) # cont. to EV of bilateral import-augmenting tech change #;
   4876   Equation CONT_EV_tech_amsr
   4877   (all,r,REG)
   4878       CNTtech_amsr(r)
   4879           = [0.01 * EVSCALFACT(r)]
   4880           * sum(i,TRAD_COMM, sum(s,REG, VIMS(i,s,r) * ams(i,s,r)));
   4881    
   4882   Variable (linear,change) (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,r,REG)(all,s,REG)
   4883       CNTtech_amsirs(i,r,s)
   4884    # cont. to EV of bilateral import augmenting tech change for TRAD_COMM i #;
   4885   Equation CONT_EV_tech_amsirs
   4886   (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,r,REG)(all,s,REG)
   4887       CNTtech_amsirs(i,r,s) = [0.01 * EVSCALFACT(r)] * VIMS(i,r,s) * ams(i,r,s);
   4888    
   4889   Variable (linear,change) (all,r,REG)
   4890       CNTkbr(r)
   4891       # cont. to EV of changes to beg. period capital stock and depreciation #;
   4892   Equation CONT_EV_kbr
   4893   (all,r,REG)
   4894       CNTkbr(r) = - [0.01 * EVSCALFACT(r)] * VDEP(r) * [kb(r) - pop(r)];
   4895    
   4896   Variable (linear,change) (all,r,REG)
   4897       CNTfyr(r)
   4898       # cont. to EV of changes to foreign income #;
   4899   Equation CONT_EV_FYr
   4900   (all,r,REG)
   4901           CNTfyr(r) = [0.01 * EVSCALFACT(r)]
   4902           * [ sum(h, HHLD, REMI(h,r) * (remih(h,r) - poph(h,r)))
   4903               - sum(h, HHLD, REMO(h,r) * (remoh(h,r) - poph(h,r)))
   4904               + sum(h, HHLD, FYI(h,r) * (fyih(h,r) - poph(h,r)))
   4905               - sum(h, HHLD, FYO(h,r) * (fyoh(h,r) - poph(h,r)))
   4906               + AIDI(r) * (aidin(r) - pop(r))
   4907               - AIDO(r) * (aidout(r) - pop(r))];
   4908    
   4909   Variable (linear,change) (all,r,REG)
   4910       CNTfkyr(r)
   4911       # cont. to EV of changes to foreign capital income #;
   4912   Equation CONT_EV_FkYr
   4913   (all,r,REG)
   4914       CNTfkyr(r) = [0.01 * EVSCALFACT(r)] *
   4915               [ sum(h, HHLD, FYI(h,r) * (fyih(h,r) - poph(h,r)))
   4916               - sum(h, HHLD, FYO(h,r) * (fyoh(h,r) - poph(h,r)))];
   4917    
   4918   Variable (linear,change) (all,r,REG)
   4919       CNTremr(r)
   4920       # cont. to EV of changes to remittances #;
   4921   Equation CONT_EV_REMr
   4922   (all,r,REG)
   4923       CNTremr(r) = [0.01 * EVSCALFACT(r)] *
   4924               [ sum(h, HHLD, REMI(h,r) * (remih(h,r) - poph(h,r)))
   4925               - sum(h, HHLD, REMO(h,r) * (remoh(h,r) - poph(h,r)))];
   4926    
   4927   Variable (linear,change) (all,r,REG)
   4928       CNTaidr(r)
   4929       # cont. to EV of changes to foreign aid #;
   4930   Equation CONT_EV_AIDr
   4931   (all,r,REG)
   4932       CNTaidr(r) = [0.01 * EVSCALFACT(r)] *
   4933               [AIDI(r) * (aidin(r) - pop(r)) - AIDO(r) * (aidout(r) - pop(r))];
   4934    
   4935   !<
   4936       -------------------------------
   4937       D. Terms of Trade Decomposition
   4938       -------------------------------
   4939    
   4940       Computations for decomposition the terms-of-trade effect
   4941       Reference: Robert McDougall, SALTER No. 12 Working Paper
   4942   >!
   4943    
   4944   Coefficient (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,r,REG)
   4945       SX_IR(i,r) # share of good i in total exports from r #;
   4946   Formula (all,m,MARG_COMM)(all,r,REG)
   4947       SX_IR(m,r)
   4948           = [sum(s,REG, VXWD(m,r,s)) + VST(m,r)]
   4949           / [sum(k,TRAD_COMM, sum(s,REG, VXWD(k,r,s)))
   4950               + sum(l,MARG_COMM, VST(l,r))];
   4951   Formula (all,i,NMRG_COMM)(all,r,REG)
   4952       SX_IR(i,r)
   4953           = sum(s,REG, VXWD(i,r,s))
   4954           / [sum(k,TRAD_COMM, sum(s,REG, VXWD(k,r,s)))
   4955               + sum(l,MARG_COMM, VST(l,r))];
   4956    
   4957   Coefficient (all,m,MARG_COMM)(all,s,REG)
   4958       VTICOMM(m,s) # margin usage of m in getting imports to region s #;
   4959   Formula (all,m,MARG_COMM)(all,s,REG)
   4960       VTICOMM(m,s) = sum(i,TRAD_COMM, sum(r,REG, VTMFSD(m,i,r,s)));
   4961    
   4962   Coefficient (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,s,REG)
   4963       VIWDIRALL(i,s) # imports of i into s, with direct allocation of margins #;
   4964   Formula (all,m,MARG_COMM)(all,s,REG)
   4965       VIWDIRALL(m,s) = sum(r,REG, VXWD(m,r,s)) + VTICOMM(m,s);
   4966   Formula (all,i,NMRG_COMM)(all,s,REG)
   4967       VIWDIRALL(i,s) = sum(r,REG, VXWD(i,r,s));
   4968    
   4969   Coefficient (all,s,REG)
   4970       VIWDATOT(s) # total imports into s, calculated on direct allocation basis #;
   4971   Formula (all,s,REG)
   4972       VIWDATOT(s) = sum(i,TRAD_COMM, VIWDIRALL(i,s));
   4973    
   4974   Coefficient (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,r,REG)
   4975       SM_IR(i,r)  # share of good i in total imports into r #;
   4976   Formula (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,s,REG)
   4977       SM_IR(i,s) = VIWDIRALL(i,s) / VIWDATOT(s);
   4978    
   4979   Zerodivide (zero_by_zero) default 0;
   4980   Coefficient (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,r,REG)(all,s,REG)
   4981       SX_IRS(i,r,s) # share of exports of good i from region r to s #;
   4982   Formula (all,m,MARG_COMM)(all,r,REG)(all,s,REG)
   4983       SX_IRS(m,r,s) = VXWD(m,r,s) / [sum(k,REG, VXWD(m,r,k)) + VST(m,r)];
   4984   Formula (all,i,NMRG_COMM)(all,r,REG)(all,s,REG)
   4985       SX_IRS(i,r,s) = VXWD(i,r,s) / sum(k,REG, VXWD(i,r,k));
   4986   Zerodivide (zero_by_zero) off;
   4987    
   4988   Coefficient (all,m,MARG_COMM)(all,r,REG)
   4989       SXT_IR(m,r) # share of margins in exports of good i from region r #;
   4990   Formula (all,m,MARG_COMM)(all,r,REG)
   4991       SXT_IR(m,r) = VST(m,r) / [sum(k,REG, VXWD(m,r,k)) + VST(m,r)];
   4992    
   4993   Variable (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,r,REG)
   4994       px_ir(i,r) # export price index for good i and region r #;
   4995   Equation EXPPRICE_MARG
   4996   # price index for total exports of m from r #
   4997   (all,m,MARG_COMM)(all,r,REG)
   4998       px_ir(m,r)
   4999           = sum(s,REG, SX_IRS(m,r,s) * pfob(m,r,s)) + SXT_IR(m,r) * pm(m,r);
   5000   Equation EXPPRICE_NMRG
   5001   # price index for total exports of i from r #
   5002   (all,i,NMRG_COMM)(all,r,REG)
   5003       px_ir(i,r) = sum(s,REG, SX_IRS(i,r,s) * pfob(i,r,s));
   5004    
   5005   Coefficient (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,r,REG)(all,s,REG)
   5006       SM_IRS(i,r,s) # share of imports of good i into s from r at FOB prices #;
   5007   Formula (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,r,REG)(all,s,REG)
   5008       SM_IRS(i,r,s) = VXWD(i,r,s) / VIWDIRALL(i,s);
   5009    
   5010   Coefficient (all,m,MARG_COMM)(all,r,REG)
   5011       SMT_IR(m,r) # share of transport cost in imports of margin commodity #;
   5012   Formula (all,m,MARG_COMM)(all,s,REG)
   5013       SMT_IR(m,s) = VTICOMM(m,s) / VIWDIRALL(m,s);
   5014    
   5015   Variable (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,r,REG)
   5016       pm_ir(i,r) # imports price index for good i and region r #;
   5017   Equation IMPPRICE1_MARG
   5018   # price index for total imports of m in s -- margins commodities #
   5019   (all,m,MARG_COMM)(all,s,REG)
   5020       pm_ir(m,s)
   5021           = sum(r,REG, SM_IRS(m,r,s) * pfob(m,r,s)) + SMT_IR(m,s) * pt(m);
   5022   Equation IMPPRICE1_NMRG
   5023   # price index for total imports of i in s -- non-margins commodities #
   5024   (all,i,NMRG_COMM)(all,s,REG)
   5025       pm_ir(i,s) = sum(r,REG, SM_IRS(i,r,s) * pfob(i,r,s));
   5026    
   5027   Coefficient (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,r,REG)
   5028       SW_IR(i,r) # share of region r exports in world total for good i #;
   5029   Formula (all,m,MARG_COMM)(all,r,REG)
   5030       SW_IR(m,r)
   5031           = [sum(s,REG, VXWD(m,r,s)) + VST(m,r)]
   5032           / sum(k,REG, sum(s,REG, VXWD(m,k,s)) + VST(m,k));
   5033   Formula (all,i,NMRG_COMM)(all,r,REG)
   5034       SW_IR(i,r)
   5035           = sum(s,REG, VXWD(i,r,s)) / sum(k,REG, sum(s,REG, VXWD(i,k,s)));
   5036    
   5037   Variable (all,i,TRAD_COMM)
   5038       px_i(i) # world export price index for commodity i #;
   5039   Equation WRLDPRICEi
   5040   # world export price index for good i #
   5041   (all,i,TRAD_COMM)
   5042       px_i(i) = sum(r,REG, SW_IR(i,r) * px_ir(i,r));
   5043    
   5044   Coefficient (all,i,TRAD_COMM)
   5045       SW_I(i) # share of exports of i in world total #;
   5046   Formula (all,m,MARG_COMM)
   5047       SW_I(m)
   5048           = sum(r,REG, sum(s,REG, VXWD(m,r,s)) + VST(m,r))
   5049           / [sum(k,TRAD_COMM, sum(r,REG, sum(s,REG, VXWD(k,r,s))))
   5050               + sum(l,MARG_COMM, sum(r,REG, VST(l,r)))];
   5051   Formula (all,i,NMRG_COMM)
   5052       SW_I(i)
   5053           = sum(r,REG, sum(s,REG, VXWD(i,r,s)))
   5054           / [sum(k,TRAD_COMM, sum(r,REG, sum(s,REG, VXWD(k,r,s))))
   5055               + sum(l,MARG_COMM, sum(r,REG, VST(l,r)))];
   5056    
   5057   Variable
   5058       px_ # world export price index for all commodities #;
   5059   Equation WRLDPRICE
   5060   # world export price index for all goods #
   5061       px_ = sum(i,TRAD_COMM, SW_I(i) * px_i(i));
   5062    
   5063   Variable (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,r,REG)
   5064       c1_ir(i,r) # contribution of world price, px_i, to ToT #;
   5065   Equation c1_irEQ
   5066   # contribution of world export price index of good i to ToT for region r #
   5067   (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,r,REG)
   5068       c1_ir(i,r) = [SX_IR(i,r) - SM_IR(i,r)] * [px_i(i) - px_];
   5069    
   5070   Variable (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,r,REG)
   5071       c2_ir(i,r) # contribution of regional export price, px_ir, to ToT #;
   5072   Equation c2_irEQ
   5073   # contribution of regional export price of good i for region r #
   5074   (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,r,REG)
   5075       c2_ir(i,r) = SX_IR(i,r) * [px_ir(i,r) - px_i(i)];
   5076    
   5077   Variable (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,r,REG)
   5078       c3_ir(i,r) # contribution of regional import price, pm_ir, to ToT #;
   5079   Equation c3_irEQ
   5080   # contribution of imports price index of good i for region r #
   5081   (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,r,REG)
   5082       c3_ir(i,r) = SM_IR(i,r) * [pm_ir(i,r) - px_i(i)];
   5083    
   5084   Variable (all,r,REG)
   5085       c1_r(r) # contribution of world prices for all goods to ToT #;
   5086   Equation c1_rEQ
   5087   # contribution of world price indexes of all goods to ToT for r #
   5088   (all,r,REG)
   5089       c1_r(r) = sum(i,TRAD_COMM, c1_ir(i,r));
   5090    
   5091   Variable (all,r,REG)
   5092       c2_r(r) # contribution of regional export prices to ToT #;
   5093   Equation c2_rEQ
   5094   # contribution of regional exports prices to ToT for r #
   5095   (all,r,REG)
   5096       c2_r(r) = sum(i,TRAD_COMM, c2_ir(i,r));
   5097    
   5098   Variable (all,r,REG)
   5099       c3_r(r) # contribution of regional import prices to ToT #;
   5100   Equation c3_rEQ
   5101   # contribution of regional import prices to ToT for r #
   5102   (all,r,REG)
   5103       c3_r(r) = sum(i,TRAD_COMM, c3_ir(i,r));
   5104    
   5105   Variable (all,r,REG)
   5106       tot2(r) # trade terms for region r, computed from components #;
   5107   Equation TOT2eq
   5108   # trade terms for region r, computed from components #
   5109   (all,r,REG)
   5110       tot2(r) = c1_r(r) + c2_r(r) - c3_r(r);
   5111   !Code for Levels shock to TMS!
   5112   VARIABLE (Levels, Linear_var=tms)
   5113   (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,r,REG)(all,s,REG)      TMS_L(i,r,s)
   5114   # import tax in s on good i imported from region r (levels value) # ;
   5115    
   5116   Zerodivide Default 1.0 ;
   5117   Formula (initial) (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,r,REG)(all,s,REG)
   5118           TMS_L(i,r,s) = VIMS(i,r,s)/VIWS(i,r,s) ;
   5119   Zerodivide Off ;
   5120    
   5121   Set REGBUTONE  #All but last region # = (all, r, REG:$pos(r)
   5122   < maxs(s, REG, $POS(s)));
   5123    
   5124    
   5125    
   5126   !
   5127   Variable (change)(all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,r,REG)(all,s,REG)
   5128    delMTAX(i,r,s) # change in tariff rev #;
   5129   Equation E_delMTAX (all,i,TRAD_COMM)(all,r,REG)(all,s,REG)
   5130    delMTAX(i,r,s) = 0.01*[VIMS(i,r,s)*{pms(i,r,s) +qxs(i,r,s)}]
   5131                   - 0.01*[VIWS(i,r,s)*{pcif(i,r,s)+qxs(i,r,s)}];
   5132   BackSolve delMTAX using E_delMTAX;
   5133   !
   5134    
   5135    
   5136   !<
   5137       ====================
   5138       END OF GTAP.TAB FILE
   5139       ====================
   5140   >!




